    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Signing of a Tripartite Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lankan, Indian and Japanese Entities for the establishment of a Liquefied Natural Gas (LNG) Terminal - Floating Storage Regasification Unit (FSRU)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8652",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka, with the collaboration of the Government of India and the Government of Japan has signed a Memorandum of Understanding for the establishment of a Liquefied Natural Gas (LNG) Terminal - Floating Storage Regasification Unit (FSRU) in the Kerawalapitiya area in Colombo and a Natural Gas Terminal for the distribution of infrastructure facilities for electricity power generation. In the joint venture established for the implementation of the project, it is proposed to award 15% equity of the joint venture with the State owned Sri Lanka Gas Terminal Company Ltd., to vest 47.5% equity with Petronet LNG Limited nominated by the Government of India and  to vest 37.5% of equity with Sojitz Corporation and Mitsubishi Corporation nominated by the Government of Japan. \n\n\tAccordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade and Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to sign a MoU with the relevant parties with the objective of making a basic feasibility study and to vest authority with the Sri Lanka Gas Terminal Company Ltd., to enter into Agreements with the Indian and Japanese parties to establish the proposed joint venture, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Construction of Accommodation facilities, the Mess and the Car Park for the Police Inspectors in Slave Island",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8651",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Non\u2011availability of adequate accommodation, mess and vehicle parking facilities for the Police Officers in the Inspector Grade who come over or called to Colombo from various areas of the Island for special duties, has become a problem. As such, a proposal has been made to construct a 06 storeyed building in the Slave Island in Colombo, as a solution to the problem. \n\n\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the then Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to implement the construction activities of the said project at an estimated cost of Rs.468.27 million, during the period from 2018-2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Construction of the Residential Building and the Administrative Building of the National Police Academy in Katana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8650",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the improvement of the infrastructure facilities a proposal has been made to construct the residential building and the administrative building of the National Police Academy in Katana, established for the purpose of enhancing the knowledge, skills and attitudes of the Officers of the Sri Lanka Police,  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the then Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to implement the said project for the construction of the said buildings, at an estimated cost of Rs.836.28 million,  during the period from 2018-2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Construction of 10,000 houses for the Plantation Community under the Grant Programme of the Indian Government",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8649",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India has already granted funds to construct 4,000 houses for the Plantation Community living in the Districts of Nuwara Eliya and Badulla and out of those, the construction work of 1,136 houses are nearing completion. The construction work of the rest of the 2,836 houses has  commenced in the month of January, 2018. During the visit by the Indian Prime Minister to Sri Lanka in May, 2017, he has agreed to provide funds for the construction of 10,000 more houses for the Plantation Community. \n\nIn order to commence the implementation of the project, the identification of suitable lands for the purpose is expected to commence in March, 2018, giving priority to the families affected in the landslide disasters. As such, the proposal made by Hon. U. Palani Digambaram, the Minister of  Hill Country New Villages, Infrastructure and Community Development, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the Government of India, to implement the project for the construction of 10,000 houses for the Plantation Community at a cost of Rs.10 Lakhs per house, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Granting of import duty concessions for the import of Squid and Wekkaya the bait for Long Line Fishing used by multiday fishermen",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8648",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the Long Line Fishing used by multiday fishermen in harvesting Tuna fish, Squid, Wekkaya, Sardinella and Black Fish are used as fishing baits. Although around 7000 metric tons of bait fish are required annually for the purpose, the local supply could provide only 3000 Metric Tons out of the total requirement.  As such, bait fish such as Squid and Wekkaya are imported and distributed among fishery associations and since these types of fish being used for human consumption, duty concessions granted on the import of normal bait fish are not granted when importing such fish. The Tuna fishing industry in Sri Lanka is adversely affected due to the exorbitant prices of the imported bait fish. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to grant a import duty concession for the types of bait fish, Squid and Wekkaya imported only for the purpose of distributing among fishery associations in accordance with the recommendation of the Ministry of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development and to take necessary measures to prevent the release of such imported bait fish for local consumption,was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "The construction and the management of warehouse complexes in the Polonnaruwa, Kilinochchi and Ratnapura Districts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8647",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The stores complexes constructed in the Districts of Anuradhapura, Moneragala and Mannar with the objective of storing the crop harvest of the farmers of the dry zone are operated presently, under the supervision of the District Secretaries in such Districts. In the stores complexes in the Polonnaruwa, Kilinochchi and Ratnapura where completion is nearing at present, the operational activities of the stores complexes are expected to be implemented in the year 2018 and to vest authority with the relevant District Secretaries to enter into management agreements with the Regionas Development Banks to carry out the operational activities of the stores complexes and to vest the regulation and supervision of the said activities with the relevant District Secretaries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Implementation of the Paddy Purchase Programme of the Government (PPPG) for 2017/2018 Maha Season",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8646",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- After reviewing the paddy purchasing programmes implemented by the Government previously and taking into consideration the matters raised by the District Secretaries and the other relevant officers at the meetings conducted recently, attention has been drawn to implement the oncoming paddy purchasing programme more effectively.   \n\nAccordingly, considering the proposal made by Hon. Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, and Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy in this regard, approval of the Cabinet was granted to purchase per kg of Nadu Paddy for Rs.38/-, per kg and Samba/Keeri Samba Paddy for Rs.41/- by the intervention of the Paddy Marketing Board and the relevant District Secretaries in the districts where the government intervention is needed to ensure the guaranteed purchasing price of paddy."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Establishment of the Regional Integrated Multi-Hazard Early Warning System (RIMES) Sub-Regional Hub in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8645",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to establish the Sub-Regional Hub of the  Regional Integrated Multi-Hazard Early Warning System (RIMES) of the South East Asian Region in Sri Lanka, which is an international institution working for the capacity building of the member countries in generating and utilizing user-relevant science based information for early warning of risks from natural hazards. \n\nConsidering the contribution that could be made to strengthen the  technological capability and the capacity, of the Department of Meteorology of Sri Lanka by this manoevure,  the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to construct a two storeyed building in the premises of the Department of Meteorology to establish the said sub\u2011regional centre in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Making a Feasibility Study and an Environmental Impact Assessment on the Construction of  Wandurapeenu Ella Reservoir",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8644",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- When supplying drinking water to the Kurunegala town and its suburban areas the considerable fall of the water flow of the Deduru Oya, which is the major water source,  during the dry spells has become a major obstacle. As a solution to the problem, it has been identified that a reservoir has to be constructed upstream of the Daduru Oya basin. As such, a proposal has been made to construct Wandurapeenu Ella reservoir with a 3.6 MCM capacity and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to make a feasibility study and an environmental impact assessment in this regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Improvement of the Central Expressway connectivity of roads in Kandy and its suburbs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8643",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Presently, the construction work of Section 1 and Section 2 of the Central Expressway from Kadawatha to Kurunegala has already commenced.  Section 3 of the Expressway from Pothuhera to Galagedara is due to be constructed and by which the Kandy Town and the other towns in the Central Province will be connected to the Expressway via Galagedara Interchange.  As a result of this, it is anticipated that traffic movement in the section of the highway from Galagedara to Kandy will be increased.  As such, it is proposed to improve the road section from Katugastota to Galagedara as a 4 lane road and to construct a new 4 lane sub\u2011road in the Katugastota Town.  \n \n\nThe EXIM Bank of India has consented to provide the necessary funds for the purpose.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the then Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to appoint RITES Ltd. of India to provide consultancy services to make a Comprehensive Project Report in regard to the development of the said road activities, taking into consideration the concurrence of the present Minister Hon. Kabir Hashim, in\u2011charge of the subject, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Obtaining exotic animals to the Department of National Zoological Gardens",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8642",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "-  The Dehiwala National Zoological Gardens is being presently modernized by adopting the provisions of proper animal welfare and therefore, it is essential to obtain animals for exhibition purposes. Obtaining animals through animal exchange programmes conducted by the different worldwide Zoological gardens and obtaining excess animals donated by Foreign Zoological gardens are the main strategies adopted for the purpose. Further, focus had been made to ascertain the possibility of purchasing animals from the parties  and institutions that import animals to Sri Lanka to raise them. \n\n      \tAccordingly, the proposal which had been made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the then Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to authorize the Director General of National Zoological Gardens to obtain animals through animal exchange and animal donation programmes and to purchase foreign birds and domestic animals from the parties and institutions that import to Sri Lanka. by following the proper procurement procedures, until the provisions in the National Zoological Gardens Act, No.41 of 1982 pertaining to the implementation of the animal exchange programme are amended, taking into consideration the concurrence of  Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera the present Minister, in-charge of the subject  as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Effective Management of Water Resources in the face of the challenges of Climate Change",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8641",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has an annual rainfall of more than 2,000 mm which feed nearly 103 rivers that flow into the ocean covering all areas of the country. However, due to the spatial and area changes that occur during  the periods of rainfall, 65% of the land area in the Island is known as the dry zone and this zone is subject to scarcity of water and droughts frequently.  The risk of Sri Lanka being prone to adverse effects of climatic changes have increased and it has been observed that the changes in the rainfall pattern which occur continuously within a short period of time as well, increasing the annual dry weather days during a year have also been observed. \n\nAs a result of the adverse effects of these extreme weather conditions, severe unpredictable disaster situations like floods, landslides and drought affect the agriculture and food security of the country, irrigated water supply, supply of safe drinking water, generation of hydro electricity power and the livelihood of the people, severely.  In order to overcome these challenges, the necessity has arisen for formulating a wide and integrated management framework for the development, conservation and management of water resources. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment to establish a Presidential Task Force with the Chairmanship of the Secretary to the President inclusive of all relevant institutions, to make recommendations within three (03) months, to establish a comprehensive integrated management mechanism for the proper management of water resources, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Amendment of the Explosives Ordinance, No.21 of 1956",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8640",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The importation of explosives and its regulation activates are carried out under the Explosives Ordinance. Considering the timely requirements, it has been proposed to amend the Ordinance. As such, focus has been made to amend the Explosives Ordinance, No.21 of 1956 incorporating the amendments for granting approval for the foreign ships or air crafts carrying either explosives or related cargo to travel across sea area or air zone of Sri Lanka, indicating the post of 'Controller of Explosives' as 'Controller General of Explosives' in the Act and incorporating better methodologies in the Act to suit the present needs. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to appoint an Officials' Committee representing the relevant institutions to seek proposals for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Sri Lanka's accession to the Convention on Cluster Munitions (Oslo Convention)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8639",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though some parties have made allegations that Sri Lanka had utilized cluster munitions, during the period of the armed conflict, there is no evidence at all to the effect that such cluster munitions have ever been used by the Security Forces of Sri Lanka and the stand taken up by Sri Lanka is that Sri Lanka has never used cluster munitions nor will Sri Lanka use such munitions  in future. \n\n\tDemonstrating the dedication of the Government of Sri Lanka and its commitment  towards the non\u2011usage of cluster munitions, towards ataining sustainable peace and stability through Humanitarian Disarmament making emphasis on the International Community and the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to express the consent of Sri Lanka by acceding to the Convention on Cluster Munitions (Oslo Convention) which has already been ratified by 102 states, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Vesting the authority with the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery Or Corruption (CIABOC) to file cases based on the facts revealed by the Commissions of Inquiry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8638",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The necessity has arisen to provide legal provisions to enable to vest the authority with the Director General of the CIABOC for instituting cases under the Bribery Act or the Assets and Liabilities Law, based on the facts revealed by such Commissions of Inquiry established under the Commissions of Inquiry Act, No.17 of 1948. \n\n\tThe Legal Draftsman has drafted the relevant amendments for the purpose, to amend the Commissions of Inquiry Act, No.17 of 1948. The Attorney General has advised that the said draft would have to be passed by a special majority of not less than two thirds of Parliament. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to publish the Commissions of Inquiry (Amendment) Bill in the Government Gazette and to present the same subsequently, in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Securing of funds from the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) for the implementation of the Sri Lanka Emergency Solid Waste Management Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8637",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tThe Sri Lanka Emergency Solid Waste Management Project has been planned, with the objective of providing sustainable solutions to the problem of solid waste disposal and the construction of a solid waste disposal facility at the Aruwakkalu area in Puttalam. The estimated cost of the said project implemented by the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development and the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government is US$ 274 million. \n\nOut of the cost, a sum of US$ 115 million, is to be obtained from the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development of the World Bank and the Asian Infrastructure Development Bank has also agreed to provide US$ 115 million.  The balance of US$ 44 million will be borne by the Government of Sri Lanka.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct loan negotiations with the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank to obtain the loan amount of US$ 115 million agreed to be provided by the said Bank was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Granting Lease Concessions for the lands alienated on Long Term Lease for Agricultural Purposes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8636",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the  State Land Ordinance, No.8 of 1947, lease concessions have been granted when alienating lands on lease basis for the purpose of constructing houses and for commercial activities. However, since the general procedure for the alienation of lands on commercial basis is not followed, in respect of the alienation of state lands for agricultural purposes on commercial basis under the said Ordinance, the release of state lands has been limited for the large scale agricultural development activities.   \n\nAccordingly, targeting the development goals in the agriculture sector of the country, the proposal made by Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms, to grant the following lease concessions in alienating lands for agricultural purposes on long term lease basis under the State Land Ordinance, in future, was approved by the Cabinet:\n\n(i)\tRefrain from changing a once and for all premium equal to thrice of the annual lease which is so recovered;\n\n(ii)\tRevision of the lease rental by the addition of an amount of 20% to the lease rental which was applicable to the year previous to the year in which the revision is to be made effective, instead of the revision of the lease rental by a 50%  increase once in every 05 years;  and\n\n(iii)\tThe addition of 20% to the lease rental recovered at the end of the initial lease period to be treated as the commencement value in the second lease period, when extending the lease period subsequent to the expiry of the initial lease period."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Awarding of the relevant contracts for the Development of the infrastructure facilities at the Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8635",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the following contracts for the development  of the infrastructure facilities in the University of Colombo, the Buddhist and Pali University of Sri Lanka and the Trincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet: \n\n(i)\tawarding of the contract for the construction of a Student Service Centre for the Faculty of Science of the University of Colombo, for a sum of  Rs.381.49 million, to the State Engineering Corporation of Sri Lanka;\n\n(ii)\tawarding of the contract for the construction of a language skills development centre and an examination hall in the Buddhist and Pali University of Sri Lanka, for a sum of Rs.215.42 million, to M/s Central Engineering Services (Pvt.) Ltd.;\n(iii)\tawarding of the contract for the construction of a multi purpose auditorium for the Trincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, for a sum of Rs.674.47 million, to M/s Link Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd.;  \n\n(iv)\tawarding of the contract for the construction of a building complex for the Faculty of Communication and Business Studies of the Eastern University, for a sum of Rs.701.18 million, to M/s Edward and Christie (Pvt.) Ltd."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Supply of the Firefighting Vehicles / Equipment for the Colombo Municipal Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8634",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is essential to strengthen the Fire Service Department in the Colombo Municipal Council in ensuring the protection of the lives and property of the residents especially in multy storied buildings, concurrent to the development activities carried out in the city of Colombo and the suburbs. Accordingly, it has been proposed to supply new fire fighting vehicles and equipment to the fleet of fire fighting vehicle pool of the Department which is maintained at an exorbitant cost. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to award the contract to M/s Rosenbauer International AG in Austria for a sum of Euro 10.3 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Development of the Grid Sub-station under the  Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Program",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8633",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to develop the Pannala Grid Sub-station, to purchase two (02) power transformers, for the  Pannipitiya and Veyangoda Grid Sub\u2011stations, to purchase five 36 KV GIS Adopter Panels for the Kalutara, Kesbewa, Old Anuradhapura, Kappalturai and Kerawalapitiya Grid Sub\u2011stations, by utilizing the balance funds available in the 'Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme' implemented under the Asian Development Bank loan aid, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Providing facilities for the disposal of waste water in the premises of the Colombo Port City",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8632",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The responsibility of ensuring the utility infrastructure facilities required for the Colombo Port City which is presently in progress, is entrusted to the Government of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, it has been planned to lay a 900 mm diameter waste water force main from the Colombo Port City to the Madampitiya pump station to a total length of 5.50 km. Since  a limited space is available in the section that crosses the Maccalum canal (Beirra Outfall) where the proposed waste water pipelines have to be laid, it has been planned to lay a common pipe line  in place of the 02 waste water pipe lines found there.   \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the piling work to M/s ELS Construction (Pvt.) Ltd., already mobilized in the same location for the Ceylon Electricity Board Micro Piling, for a sum of Rs.48 million, was approved by the Cabinet in principle."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Awarding of the contract for the construction of the Central Expressway Section 3",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8631",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi, Japan has agreed to grant a credit facility of Japanese Yen 100 billion for the construction of the road section in extent of 32.5 km from Pothuhera to Galagedara via Rambukkana which is the Section 3 of the Central Expressway. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to award the construction contract to M/s Taisei Corporation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Stabilizing the coastline from Mount Lavinia to Angulana under the Colombo South Sand Nourishment Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8630",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to implement a project for stabilizing  the coastline by way of the Sand Engine Methodology in the coastline from Colpetty to Mount Lavinia, covering the coastlines of Mount Lavinia, Dehiwala, Ratmalana Wedikanda and Moratuwa which have been identified as places subjected to sea erosion in the West coastline. \n\n\tIt has been planned to stabilize the coastline from Mount Lavinia to Angulana about 5.5 km in length through sand nourishment, utilizing the provision of Rs.800 million allocated by the Budget 2018 for the Southern Colombo Sand Nourishment Project implemented for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to select a suitable contractor for the implementation of the Project under the International Competitive Bidding Procedure, was approved by the Cabinet in principle."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Amending the Voluntary Social Service Organizations (Registration and Supervision) Act, No.31 of 1980",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8629",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the timely requirements, it has been proposed to amend the Voluntary Social Service Organizations (Registration and Supervision) Act, No.31 of 1980. Accordingly, the Voluntary Social Service Organizations (Registration and Supervision) Amendment Bill has been prepared, taking into consideration the recommendations made by the Parliamentary Select Committee which studied the operation of the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations and its impact as well as the views of the relevant stakeholders including the Financial Intelligence Unit of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. \n\n\tThe objectives of making the proposed amendment are to provide for the registration of all the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations, to establish the National Secretariat for Non\u2011Governmental Organizations as a Statutory Body which is the authorized institution for the regulation and supervision of the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations, to promote the mutual co\u2011operation between the State and Non\u2011Governmental Organizations, to recognize the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations in the effort to fulfill the common development requirements of the country, to strengthen and empower the civil society, to facilitate the effective operation of the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations and to ensure the transparency and accountability on its Finance, Policies and Management. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mano Ganesan, the Minister of National Co\u2011existence, Dialogue and Official Languages, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and to present same thereafter in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Establishment of the South Asian Regional Intelligence and the Coordination Centre on Organized Crimes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8628",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish the South Asian Regional Intelligence and the Coordination Centre (SARICC) in Sri Lanka to coordinate and to exchange intelligence information among the countries in the region, with a view to eliminating organized crimes and the drug menace in the South Asian Region. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to establish the said centre in Sri Lanka and to accommodate it  temporarily in the premises of the National Dangerous Drugs Control Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Construction of a Secretariat Building Complex for the Offices of the Parliament, Offices of the National Commissions and the Office of the Cabinet of Ministers and any compatible Government Offices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8627",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to construct a Secretariat on a land in close proximity to the Japan - Sri Lanka friendship road for offices related to  Parliamentary Affairs, the offices of the National Constitutional Commissions established under the Constitution, the office of the Cabinet of Ministers and any other compatible Government Offices. The construction of the proposed Secretariat will have a built up office floor area of 35,000 m2, 15,000 m2 for common spaces, adequate vehicle parking slots with other infrastructure facilities and it is planned to be constructed within a period of three (03) years. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to carry out the activities relevant to the project, was approved by the Cabinet in principle."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Implementation of the Sustainable Urban Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8626",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Strategic Cities Development Programme implemented by the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development, 13 cities namely Kandy, Galle, Jaffna, Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa, Trincomalee, Batticaloa, Badulla, Ratnapura, Matara, Kurunegala, Nuwara Eliya and Dambulla have been identified to be developed  as Strategic cities. The sustainable urban development project implemented under the said Strategic Cities development programme, the urban city centres out side Colombo with high growth potential in economic corridors  spread across the country will be developed. \n\n\tIn this respect, through the development of basic service improvements, focus will be made on minimizing the gaps existing in large scale infrastructure facilities, enhancing mobility and connectivity between the urban centres, improvement of urban facilities, heritage conservation, improvement of sanitation activities related to environmental conservation and livelihood improvements in the towns. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement the proposed Sustainable Urban Development Project and to secure the funds necessary for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Implementation of the Middle Income Housing Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8625",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Budget of 2018 has proposed to provide loan facilities at a subsidized rate of interest to the middle income earning community who purchase a house for the first time from the National Housing Development Projects implemented by the National Housing Authority and the Urban Development Authority.  \n\nAccordingly, it is planned to grant loan facilities with a maximum period of re\u2011payment for 25 years up to Rs.5 million through the National Savings Bank.  In this respect, it is proposed to release the loans under a subsidy interest rate of 7 % for the first 5 years. The 5% balance interest to be levied to the bank will be born by the Government.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to enter into the relevant agreements with the National Savings Bank, to implement the said loan scheme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Promotion in the Cooperation on Scientific and Research Studies between Sri Lanka and Germany",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8624",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the National Science Foundation of Sri Lanka and the German Academic Exchange Service for exchanging German Scientists to further promote Cooperation on Scientific and Research Studies between Sri Lanka and Germany, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Granting  an allowance of Rs.50,000/- for the owners of the houses who were evacuated due to the landslide that occurred at the Meethotamulla Solid Waste Dump",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8623",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has already taken appropriate measures to grant rental allowances to the families, whose houses were damaged or evacuated from the risk areas due to the landslide at the Meethotamulla solid waste dump, until such time that they were provided with alternative houses or compensation for their houses. Accordingly, the Cabinet has granted approval to take over the lands which were situated within the risk zone where the houses were located and the houses damaged due to such landslides and the Government to pay compensation for the private lands situated in the landslide area.  \n\nIt has been observed that the rental allowance need to be further granted to persons affected by the landslide and who have not accepted the alternative houses or in respect of private landowners within the risk zone and the owners of such houses have not been paid the valuation compensation as yet, in respect of houses until the valuation process of such lands is completed. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to continue to pay the monthly rental of Rs.50,000/- each further for  the 60 families so identified, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Draft Bill on Carriage By Air",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8622",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of 'the Convention on the Unification of certain Rules for International Carriage By Air' is to grant the unification and  predictability required for the rules pertaining to international carriage of passengers, luggage and cargo by air. Sri Lanka is a party to the Convention which has been entered into in Montreal in the year 1988. \n\nA draft Bill has been submitted to the Cabinet in a previous occasion for giving effect to the said Convention in Sri Lanka and the Cabinet had referred the matter to the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Constitutional Affairs. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to publish the draft Bill on Carriage By Air formulated by the Legal Draftsman incorporating the recommendations of the said Sub\u2011Committee in the Government Gazette and thereafter to present same in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Securing the funds required for the General Education Modernization (GEM) Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8621",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though there is a considerable progress in the field of education in Sri Lanka in the recent decade, in terms of learning outcomes in key subjects, the country shows regional variations. It has also been identified that further attention is required in better orienting the General Education System  to enhance the socio\u2011emotional skills such as problem solving and reaching targets, regulation, confidence, teamwork and improving ethics and productivity that are important for students to become good and productive citizens in the modern global economy. \n \n\tAs such, it has been planned to implement a new project named 'General Education Modernization Project' to further strengthen the education sector based on the experiences and knowledge gained from 'Transforming School Education Centered on the Foundation of a Knowledge Hub Project'  and with the educational system of the developed countries.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct loan negotiations for securing funds for a sum of US$ 100 million from the International Development Association (IDA) of the World Bank and to enter into the relevant loan agreements for the implementation of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Construction of Rural Bridges",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8620",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has planned to construct 4,000 bridges with the objective of increasing access to markets, education and health facilities through the building of transport connectivity for the people living in the far away remote villages.  It has been identified that the Direct Lending Facility of the United Kingdom is a favourable source of loan to secure funds for this project.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to vest authority with the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government to call for proposals from the construction institutions of the United Kingdom for the implementation of a Rural Bridge Project at a cost of  Pounds (UK) 50 million and to vest authority with the relevant Technical Evaluation Committee and the Procurement Committee to evaluate the bids and the proposals submitted thereby and make recommendations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Augmentation of the Water Pipelines along with the Orugodawatta - Ambatale Road Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8619",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The activities pertaining to the widening of the Orugodawatta - Ambatale Road have commenced presently. Since the main water transmission line to the Colombo City which is more than hundred years old is also laid along the said Road, the re\u2011laying of the water pipe line network also has to be commenced  to coincide with the said Road Development Work.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into loan agreements with the UniCredit Bank Austria AG and the People's Bank as per the approval granted by the Cabinet, with the objective of securing the funds necessary to implement the water pipe laying project expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "'Ape Suwaya - Rate Saviya' (Our Health is the Country's Strength) National Health Promotion Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8618",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tIt has been proposed to implement a National Programme called 'Ape Suwaya - Rate Saviya' (Our Health is the Country's Strength), with a view to relieving the people of Sri Lanka from the unfortunate situation they have fallen into due to the prevailing non\u2011communicable diseases and making them healthy and thereby creating a country with a strong economy through the commencement of community health development programmes, at rural level, for the prevention of communicable diseases.  As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement this programme by the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine in collaboration with the relevant Ministries and other Institutions under the purview of a special operational unit to be setup in the Presidential Secretariat  and to commence same as a pilot project in the Districts of Polonnaruwa, Kalutara, Moneragala, Badulla, Batticaloa and Kilinochchi  effective from the month of February of this year, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Prevention of the current misuse of Kerosene",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8616",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since most of the low income communities in Sri Lanka use kerosene for the requirements such as lighting houses etc, the Government provides a large subsidy in respect of the same. The consumption of kerosene by the rural community has declined since electricity is provided for the rural areas to a great extent. Nevertheless, the consumption of local kerosene during the past couple of months has greatly increased and it is found that the instant increase in consumption of kerosene has been caused due to modifying engines and mixing kerosene with petrol illegally by some parties to enable to drive long distance buses and lorries by using kerosene instead of diesel for the reason of the concessionary price of kerosene. It has also come to light that the mixing takes place through hired bowsers while transporting of fuel from the depots to the respective dealer filling stations. \n\n\tTaking into consideration the necessity of taking expeditious action to prevent this situation, the joint proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena and Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Petroleum Resources Development, to take necessary action to revoke the dealership of the fuel filling stations who are engaged in illegally mixing of fuel or in other illegal activities relating to kerosene or assisting in such activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Securing the Assistance of the United States Programme of the Peace Corps for the improvement of the English Language Education in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8615",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Programme of the Peace Corps of the United States of America was operative in Sri Lanka from time to time from the year 1962 and especially, during the Tsunami disaster which occurred in 2004, it provided significant assistance for the relief activities and as well as for rebuilding efforts. The programme is not operative in Sri Lanka after the year 2006. The  United States has decided to re-establish the programme for teaching of English based on a request made by the Government of Sri Lanka. \n\n\tAs such, the  assistance of the programme will be provided for the capacity building of the English language teachers of Sri Lanka and action will be taken  to place the volunteers in the Secondary Schools, Regional English Support Centres and in the Vocational Training Centres. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs,  to enter into an Agreement between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of the United States of America in regard to the re-establishment of the Programme of the Peace Corps in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Securing of funds for the implementation of the Sri Lanka Emergency Solid Waste Management Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8614",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Emergency Solid Waste Management Project has been designed with a view to providing sustainable solutions to the problem with regard to the disposal of solid waste. This project also includes the construction of a waste disposal yard at Aluwkkaru area in Puttalam, for the disposal of waste generated within the Metro Colombo Region, expanding the existing composting facility at Muturajawela and the stabilization and development of the existing open dump sites not in use at present.  \n\n\tThe total estimated cost of this project implemented by the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development and the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government is US$ 274 million. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct loan negotiations with the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD) of the World Bank in regard to obtaining a sum of US$ 115 million out of the cost estimate, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Upgrading of the Railway track from Maho to Omanthai",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8613",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has been granted for the rehabilitation of the section of the  railway track from Maho to Omanthai under the Indian Line of Credit. The pre-qualification process to identify the engineering, procurement and construction contractors for the project has commenced and bid documents have been issued to 03 selected companies which have fulfilled the pre-qualifications, taking into consideration the observations of the EXIM Bank of India. \n\n\n\n\n\tAccordingly, the Cabinet noted, the information submitted by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to the effect that the road development activities of the Maho - Anuradhapura section and Anuradhapura - Vavunia section have been planned separately in order to  complete the activities expeditiously."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Purchase of 75,000 pairs of Boots (High Leg) required for the Sri Lanka Army",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8612",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to award the contract for the purchase of 75,000 pairs of Boots (High Leg Black) for the members of the Sri Lanka Army, to M/s Irosha International (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.232 million, as recommended by the Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "The construction of a Stroke Treatment Unit at the District General Hospital in Ampara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8611",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'Stroke' is a leading cause of adult disabilities. Therefore, it has been decided to construct a Stroke Treatment Unit at the Ampara District General Hospital for the improvement of treatment facilities needed for stroke patients.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the Treatment Unit to M/s Link Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.213.9 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Development of the infrastructure facilities in the Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8610",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Budgetary provision has been set apart from the year 2018, to improve the infrastructure facilities in the Universities to suit the academic courses of the students creating space for their educational activities who enter the Universities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to implement the following infrastructure development projects utilizing the allocated provision, was approved in principle by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tConstruction of 02, three storey buildings for the Library and the Information Technology Centre of the Vavunia Campus of the University of Jaffna. \n\n*\tConstruction of a three storey building for the Lecture Hall of the Faculty of Technology of the University of  Ruhuna.\n\n*\tConstruction of Quarters for the staff of the Bhiksu University of Sri Lanka in Anuradhapura.\n\n*\tConstruction of a four storey building for the Postgraduate Institute of Pali and Buddhist Studies of the University of Kelaniya."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Procurement of 12 Railway Locomotives for operation in the Upcountry Railway Line",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8609",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for the procurement of 12 railway locomotives for the Department of Sri Lanka Railways for operation in the up country railway line to M/s General Electric Company of USA, for a sum of US$ 4.056 million each, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Amendment of Principal Ordinances and Acts related to the Local Authorities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8608",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The necessity to amend the three principal Ordinances and Acts being the  Municipal Councils Ordinance, Urban Councils Ordinance and the Pradeshiya Sabha Act relating to the Local Authorities to suit the timely requirements has been identified. As such, the Hon. Minister of  Provincial Councils and Local Government, has appointed a Committee headed by a President's Counsel to propose the amendments necessary, considering the matters emphasized by the Local Authorities, Provincial Councils, Political Parties and the Civil Society Organizations from time to time and the recommendations of the Commission on Local Government Reforms published in the Parliament Session Report No.1 of 1999. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare legislation to amend the related legislation inclusive of the proposed amendments in order to ensure a more People Friendly Democratic Governance within the Local Authorities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Implementation of the Development Programme in the Moneragala District to coincide with the 200th Anniversary of the Uva Wellassa freedom struggle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8607",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- When the British conquered  Sri Lanka completely in the year 1815, the people of Uva Wellassa launched a struggle in the year 1818 against the suppression and it was the first freedom struggle against the British. In order to suppress the struggle, the Britishers severely destroyed the properties such as lakes and anicuts, lands and paddy fields, temples and religious places and the human lives around the area resulting in a severe socio-economic deterioration.  \n\n\tAt present, the District which indicates the minimum development is  the Moneragala District which includes the areas which were subject to the suppression.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration and Management, to implement a programme in the Moneragala District, aimed at renovation of  the reservoirs and anicuts, the development of roads and infrastructure facilities, renovation of religious places, improvement of agricultural farms and cottage industries  to coincide with the commemoration in the year 2018 which marks the completion of 200 years from the freedom struggle of 1818, was approved by the Cabinet. It was further decided by the Cabinet that priority be given to implement the above programmes by utilizing the provisions already allocated under the Budget 2018 to the relevant Line Ministries."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Enhancing the pension allowance granted by the National Film Corporation Trust for the Film Artists and Technicians",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8606",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A programme for granting a monthly pension allowance for the Film Artists and Technicians who have completed 60 years of age has been established by an Act, of Parliament  No.3 of 1986 and it is being implemented by the 'National Film Corporation Trust' since the year 1987. Under this programme 57 Film Artist and Technician pensioneers are presently granted a monthly allowance of Rs.2,000/- each and a further 106 eligible applicants are there in anticipation of the allowance. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration and Management, to enhance this monthly pension allowance up to Rs.5,000/- considering the present situation and to seek a Treasury grant of Rs.10 million for the National Film Corporation Trust to enable the Trust to pay the said allowance for 163 Film Artist and Technician pensioners, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Implementation of a pilot project for the issuance of Electronic Phytosanitary Certificates",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8605",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The issuance of Phytosanitary Certificates which is an essential certificate for ensuring the quality of plants and plant materials exported by Sri Lanka, by the    Plant Quarantine Unit of the Department of Agriculture of Sri Lanka is carried out in the print form. The International Plant Protection Convention of the United Nations has emphasized the necessity of issuing the Electronic Phytosanitary Certificates as a safe and efficient methodology of exchanging documents among countries. Accordingly, Sri Lanka has been selected for the pilot project to be implemented in the Asia Pacific Region to experiment on the programme of issuing Electronic Phytosanitary Certificates. In view of this programme, new commercial and marketing opportunities will be created for Sri Lanka with the enhancement of the efficiency and security of the exchange of plants and plant material at international level. \n\n\tThe Agriculture and Water Resources Department of Australia under the guidance of the International Plant Protection Convention of the United Nations will provide the sponsorship for the implementation of this pilot project. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, and to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Department of Agriculture of Sri Lanka and the Department of Agriculture and Water Resources of Australia to implement the pilot project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Granting of an alternative land for the plot of land to be obtained by the Ceylon Electricity Board for the expansion of the Panadura Divisional Secretariat",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8604",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since the existing office space of the Panadura Divisional Secretariat is inadequate, an Agreement has been reached to obtain the adjoining land in extent of 80 perches owned by the Ceylon Electricity Board, for the purpose of making the District Secretariat most spacious and to give an alternative plot of land to the Ceylon Electricity Board in lieu of same. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to allocate a land in extent of 120 perches at the Modarawila Industrial Zone belonging to the Urban Development Authority (UDA) to be granted as an alternative land for the CEB and to vest a land in extent of 124 perches located at Pattiya North, Panadura, with the Urban Development Authority instead, as a free grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Implementation of the concessionary loan schemes under the 'Enterprise Sri Lanka' Programme proposed in the Budget 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8603",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Enterprise Sri Lanka' Programme was proposed in the Budget 2018 with the objective of upgrading the Per Capita income up to  US$ 5,000, creation of 1 million new employment opportunities, doubling of the value of exports and sustaining an economic growth of over 5% to reach the Government's midterm development goals by the year 2020. Under this, it is scheduled to provide 15 loan schemes inclusive of financial and non\u2011financial facilities aimed at small scale and medium scale to entrepreneurs, youth and women entrepreneurs and the self employed identified as the driving force of the economic development. For this purpose, a sum of Rs.20,230 million has been set apart for the year 2018.  \n\n\tUnder the concessionary loan scheme 'Green Loan' proposed in the Budget 2018, financial facilities are due to be provided to induce local entrepreneurs to manufacture packing material by using the biodegradable raw material instead of using polythene, small scale hotel owners who provide services to tourists and the house owners registered in the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority under the 'Homestay' programme.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to implement the said loan scheme through the public and private banks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Introduction of a new Indigenous Medical Council Bill to regularize the functions of the Ayurveda Medical Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8602",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The ancient Ayurveda system of medicine which is older than 3,000 years, performs a significant role in the medical sector in Sri Lanka operating along side the traditional system of medicine in the country and concurrently the  Siddha system of medicine as well as the Unani System of medicine also is operating in the system of Indigenous Medicine. The Ayurveda Medical Council established under the Ayurveda Act, No.31 of 1961 is presently engaged in the registration of Ayurvedic doctors serving in the Ayurveda Medical System, regulating them and dealing with their  ethical aspects. Presently, the Ayurveda Mediccal System, by now is popular among Sri Lankans as well as foreigners, and therefore, it has been found that it is appropriate to expand the functions of the Ayurveda Medical Council as suited to the current requirements. \n\nAccordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to present a new Indigenous Medical Council Act, for the betterment of the system of Indigenous Medicine by segregating the Ayurveda Medical Council from the Ayurveda Act, No.31 of 1961 and to regulate the functions of the Ayurveda Medical Council, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Entering into a Collaborative Research Agreement with the International Agency for Research on Cancer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8601",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The crude incidence rate of cancer patients in Sri Lanka in the year 1985 shows 31.6 for per population of 100,000 and it has risen up to 82.1 for per population of 100,000 by the year 2010. When taking measures for controlling cancer, the proper maintenance of population based cancer registers on all types of cancers is highly important. In Sri Lanka, a cancer register at the national level is maintained since 1985 and a population based cancer register has also been established for the Colombo district since 2012. \n\nThe International Agency for Research on Cancer has recommended that, the cancer registers in Sri Lanka can be further expanded, based on the population. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to enter into a Collaborative Research Agreement between the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine and the International Agency for Research on Cancer, with a view to obtaining the required technical assistance for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Amending the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No.15 of 1979 pertaining to the increase of the minimum age of Criminal Responsibility",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8600",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the law prevailing in Sri Lanka, a child below the age of 08 years is not vested with the criminal responsibility. Yet, in the opinion of the psychiatrists and the experts in the relevant fields, this age limit is  comparatively a tender age. As such, approval of the Cabinet has been granted to amend the Penal Code to increase this age limit up to 12 years and in case of  a child above 12 years but below 14 years, to confer the discretion to the Magistrate to determine in a case where a child is accused of a crime whether such child has attained sufficient maturity to understand the gravity of the offence with which he has been charged. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to publish the Bill formulated to amend the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No.15 of 1979 providing provision in such circumstances to direct such a child to be examined by a Government Medical Officer, to enable a Magistrate to obtain expert guidance to assist in forming the relevant opinion on a scientific basis, in the Government Gazette and subsequently, to present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Establishment of an Office of the 'Delegation of German Industry and Commerce' in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8599",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The policy of the Government is to obtain the maximum economic benefits through the integration into the global economy and therefore, a key strategy under the said policy is the establishment of effective partnerships in countries with advanced economies. As such, it has been proposed to establish an office of the 'Delegation of German Industry and Commerce' in Colombo with a view to promoting co-operation and partnership among the trading companies, organizations and persons engaged in the commercial field in Germany as well as in Sri Lanka. \n\n\tBy the establishment of such an office in Sri Lanka, it would create greater assistance for facilitating the promotion of commercial activities between the two countries covering specially, the small and medium size industries, thereby opening up new opportunities for the investors of both countries. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs and Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to provide facilities for the establishment of an office of the Delegation of German Industry and Commerce in Colombo, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Establishing a Regional Consular Office in Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8598",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- More than 600 persons are travelling daily from various districts of the country, to visit the Colombo Office of the Consular Division of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to obtain the services rendered by the said Consular Division. Action is being taken to establish Regional Consular Offices to enable the general public to obtain these services easily.  Accordingly, action has already been taken to establish a Regional Consular Office in Jaffna for the general public of the Northern Province and presently, appropriate action has been initiated to open such  a Regional Consular Office in Matara as well. \n\nIt has been proposed to set up a Regional Consular Office in Polonnaruwa as well, with a view to providing such services easily to the public living in the Districts of Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa, Trincomalee, Batticaloa, Kurunegala, Ampara and Matale. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to establish the said Regional Consular Office in a building located close to the Divisional Secretariat, Thamankaduwa of Polonnaruwa, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Master Plan for the Development of the Ratmalana Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8597",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ratmalana Airport, being the first international airport in Sri Lanka  was operating as the major international airport up to the year 1969. The airport which has been located very close to the major commercial city in Colombo, with easy access to all the main roads, presently operates around 70 domestic aircraft movements per day, the airport serves domestic aviation needs including commercial passenger flights, Aviation Training, International Commercial Aircrafts and the arrangement of VIP and VVIP movements,   humanitarian missions during national crisis situations and conducts the Sri Lanka Air Force (SLAF) operational activities, as well. The number of flight operations conducted are rapidly increasing and to suit the situation, considering the Colombo centered development projects, the existing capacity of the airport is required to be improved.  \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to implement the Master Development Plan of the  'Way to 2030' incorporating the strategic plans to be implemented from 2018 to 2030, prepared for the improvement of the Ratmalana Airport as an Airport providing efficient domestic and international flight services, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Co-operation in the field of Tourism between Sri Lanka and Estonia",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8596",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Economic Affairs and Communications of the  Republic of Estonia  on co-operation in the field of Tourism, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Securing of Funds for the implementation of the Greater Ratnapura Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8595",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Greater Ratnapura Water Supply Project, it is anticipated to provide around 3,500 new pipe born water connections covering 29 Grama Niladhari Divisions. The contract for installing the other accessories required for the distribution system, the DI Valves and the supply and laying of pipes has by now been awarded in accordance with the Cabinet approval and the Bank of Ceylon has agreed to grant a loan of Rs.1,528.9 million to secure the required funds to cover its cost. \n\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to vest the authority with the National Water Supply and Drainage Board (NWS&DB) to enter into an Agreement with the Bank of Ceylon to obtain the loan facility, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Securing of Funds for the implementation of the Hasalaka Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8594",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hasalaka Water Supply Project has been designed to address the drinking water issue in the Hasalaka area and plans are underway to provide clean water for about 49,370 people covering 33 Grama Niladhari Divisions. Presently, the contract for the implementation of the project has been awarded in accordance with the approval of the Cabinet and the People's Bank has agreed to grant a loan of Rs.6,235 million to secure the required funds to cover its cost.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to vest the authority with the National Water Supply and Drainage Board (NWS&DB) to enter into an Agreement with the People's Bank to obtain the loan facility, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-14-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-02-14",
    "description": "Amending the National Defence Fund Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8593",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approval has been granted to amend the National Defence Fund Act, No.9 of 1985 by which the National Defence Fund has been established with a view to further expanding the services rendered by such fund for the  welfare of the families of the War-heroes who have died or become disabled, and streamlining its administrative functions. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to publish the amended Bill so formulated in the Government Gazette and subsequently, to present it in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Establishment of a Special High Court to inquire into cases pertaining to allegations of bribery and corruption and extremely complex financial crimes, expeditiously",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8592",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tApproval of the Cabinet has been granted to amend the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978 for the purpose of establishing a dedicated three Bench High Court to inquire into cases expeditiously pertaining to allegations of bribery and corruption and extremely complex financial crimes. Accordingly, in terms of the Draft Bill prepared, the Attorney General or the Director General of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC) will file indictment in respect of the specified offences therein, in the proposed three Bench High Court. The particulars such as the nature of the relevant offences, the gravity, the complexity, the effect on the State or the victims, the national interest etc., incidental thereto, as the case may be, will be taken in to consideration subject to a formal methodology. \n\nThe Cabinet noted the matters submitted by Hon. Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to publish the Draft Bill prepared to amend the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978, providing for the establishment of the three Bench High Court, in the Government Gazette and subsequently, to present it in Parliament, for approval."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Granting of further relief to the farmers affected by the drought",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8591",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tIt has been identified that 291,945 farmer families have been affected by the drought caused by the dry climatic condition which prevailed in the country recently. An Officials' Committee comprising of the Secretaries to the Ministries of Finance and Mass Media; Disaster Management; Home Affairs; and Agriculture has been appointed by the Cabinet to submit proposals for providing further relief in addition to the relief already provided for by the Government to those farmer families.  \n\nAs such, the  joint proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, and Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to extend the monthly dry ration provided to the farmer families who have not cultivated continuously during 03 seasons namely Maha Season of 2016/17, Yala Season of 2017 and Maha Season of 2017/18 due to the drought situation, further for the period from January 2018 to April 2018 as well, as recommended by the Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Introduction of legislation for the Demutualization of the Colombo Stock Exchange",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8590",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe Colombo Stock Exchange  has been established in the year 1985 as a non for profit 'company limited by guarantee' and it is the only major Stock Exchange operated in South Asia as a 'Shareholder Owned Company'. Demutualization is the process through which, exchanges operating as 'not for profit' member controlled organizations are converted into 'for profit' shareholder owned companies.  \n\nIt is essential that, the Colombo Stock Exchange is established as a  Demutualized Stock Exchange, to ensure proper management and to promote the ownership of diversified shares. As such, Cabinet approval has been granted to convert the Colombo Stock Exchange into a Demutualized Stock Exchange limited by shares and to make the legislative amendments necessary for the purpose. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to publish the Draft Bill prepared for 'the Demutualization of the Colombo Stock Exchange', in the Gazette and subsequently, to present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Obtaining Additional Loan Assistance from the Asian Development Bank for the implementation of the Skills Sector Enhancement Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8589",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\t'The Skills Sector Development Programme', which has been planned by the Government within the period from 2014 to 2020, with a view to creating an efficient Skills Development Methodology to meet the labour market demand, is implemented under the Loan Assistance obtained from the Asian Development Bank, for the purpose of assisting the 'Skills Sector Development Programme'. Through this programme, it is anticipated to achieve the goals such as improved quality of Provision of Tertiary Vocational Education and Training, (TVET), enhanced industry partnership for TVET, policy and the implementation of Institutional and Operational Reforms. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct negotiations to obtain US$ 100 million from the Asian Development Bank and to enter into the relevant loan agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Amendments to the Bribery Act to eliminate Bribery and Corruption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8588",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe approval of the Cabinet has been granted to amend to the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption Act and the Laws incidental thereto, having identified the necessity of the amendments required to be made to suit the present requirements, for the elimination of bribery and corruption prevalent in Sri Lanka. Presently, action is also being taken to amend the Judicature Act to establish a three Member Bench High Court to expedite the conducting of financial crimes and corruption trials. \n\nConcurrently, section 70 of the Bribery Act, No.11 of 1954 has also to be amended to enable the corruption charges apart from bribery charges to be conducted not only by the Magistrate's Court but also by the High Court.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena to publish the Draft Bill prepared for the purpose in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Construction of an Officer Quarters Complex at Kalapaluwawa for Officers of the Special Task Force",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8587",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tApproval of the Cabinet has been granted for the construction of an Officer Quarters Complex, at Kalapaluwawa  for married officers of Special Task Force in the ranks of  Police Constable, Police Sergeant, Sub Inspector of Police and Inspector of Police. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to award the said contract to M/s Construction Managers and Planners (Pvt) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.289.59 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Procurement for the construction of a Stroke Treatment Unit at the Teaching Hospital in Kurunegala",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8586",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tStroke is a leading cause of adult disabilities and it has become the 4th leading cause of deaths in the hospital system in Sri Lanka. Except for the rehabilitation hospital in Ragama a properly developed stroke unit is not available in any hospital, in the country, at present.  As such, the approval of the Cabinet has been granted for the construction of a stroke unit at the teaching hospital in Kurunegala. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the stroke unit to M/s Link Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.230.57 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Selecting a Contractor for the expansion of the Nanotechnology and Science Park at Mahenwatte, Pitipana in Homagama",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8585",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to award the contract for the expansion of the Nanotechnology and Science Park at Mahenwatte, Pitipana in Homagama under Phase 1B, to M/s Access Engineering PLC, for a sum of Rs.3,088 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Construction of an additional lane each at the Entry and Exit Ramps at the Ja-Ela Interchange on Colombo - Katunayake Expressway",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8584",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThere are two lanes for the Entry and Exit ramps for vehicles at the Ja-Ela Interchange on Colombo - Katunayake Expressway. At the outset, the Manual Toll Collection (MTC) took place in all these lanes and subsequent to the introduction of the Electronic Toll Collection (ETC) separate lanes were allocated for the purpose. Since most of the daily users of the expressway are still not attracted to the ETC method, the number of vehicles moving on the MTC lane has increased. \n\n\n\n\n\tAlso, the number of vehicles which use the Ja-Ela Interchange has gone up unprecedentedly, due to the rapid development of the residential areas in Ja-Ela and associated areas as well and this has caused a huge traffic congestion in the MTC lane at the Interchange at peak hours. \n\n\tAs such, taking into account the long term advantages in the ETC method, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to further maintain the lane set apart and to construct an additional MTC lane each in the entry and exit ramp at the Ja-Ela Interchange as a remedial measure for the above said traffic congestion, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Obtaining Consultancy Services for the Construction Supervision of the Western Province Road Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8583",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe Western Province Road Development Project is implemented with the funds provided by the OPEC Fund for International Development (OFID). Under this project, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the contract for the provision of consultancy services for the supervision of the construction in the roads namely, Kaduwela-Athurugiriya, Walgama-Athurugiriya, Wadduwa-  Moronthuduwa, Bellana-Moragala,  to M/s Green Tech Consultants (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.150.75 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Consultancy Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
