    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8582",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Turkmenistan on Bilateral Consultations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Disposal of Documents pertaining to Vehicles that are not in use",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8581",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tWith the increase of the per capita income of the country during the past decade, the annual import of vehicles have also increased gradually. The information related to the tabulated increase in several types of vehicles registered in the Department of Motor Traffic during the period from the year 2008 up to the month of October in 2017 is given below. \n\n\n Class of Vehicle \n2008\n by October 2017\n\n\n Motor cars \n381,448\n749,797\n\n\n Three wheelers \n406,531\n1,135,765\n\n\n Motor cycles \n1,760,600\n3,990,505\n\n\n Buses \n81,050\n106,804\n\n\nConsequent to the annual increase of the number of registered motor vehicles, the number of vehicle files in the Department of Motor Traffic also have been increased.  A four storey building is being constructed presently, for storing these files, but the maximum number of documents that can also be stored in the record room under construction is estimated to be around 3.5 million. \n\n\tAs such, a proposal has been made to provide accommodation to store new files by the formal disposal of all files pertaining to the vehicles presently not in use. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to dispose of the files of vehicles systematically, for which no revenue licenses have been obtained continuously during the last five years, treating them as vehicles not in use, under the supervision of a group of officials of the Department of Motor Traffic, was approved by the Cabinet.  It was also decided that the files relevant to vehicles where the legal proceedings have not been completed as yet, should not be disposed under this programme."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Establishment of the Secretariat for the Operations at Sea on Piracy off the Coast of Somalia (CGPCS)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8580",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tIn the Indian Ocean zone close to Somalia, a series of incidents of hijacking of commercial ships were reported since the year 2005 and  the year 2010 was the peak year where the most number of such incidents were reported. This made a severe effect on the free passage of maritime trade and the global economy. The responses made by deploying of armed guards on board the commercial vessels and deploying navies in the seas close to Somalia have, by now, resulted, in the reduction of incidents of piracy. However,  as a deterrent measure considered essential for enhancing the efforts to combat piracy and increasing coordination among the countries of the region. \n\n\tThe Contact Group on combating Piracy off the Coast of Somalia was established in the year 2009 as an international mechanism for the purpose and Sri Lanka has been a founder member in the Group. Sri Lanka has gained an opportunity to function as the Secretariat for the Working Group on operations at sea and the Sri Lanka Navy has both the ability and the experience to deal with the activity. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to make a formal request to the Contact Group on piracy off the Coast of Somalia, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Amendments to the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration (SLIDA) Act, No.9 of 1982",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8579",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe functions and the administrative setup of the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration - SLIDA, the pioneer public sector training institute of Sri Lanka has been subject to changes during the last few years. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration and Management, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to amend the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration  Act, No.9 of 1982 concurrently, with the inclusion of the following amendments,  to effect the changes, was approved by the Cabinet.   \n\n\n*\tamendments to the organizational structure, objectives and functions and authorities, of the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration to suit the the present status and the requirements; \n\n*\tinclusion of new provisions in the Act to reflect the functions and the authorities of the School of Postgraduate Studies of the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration; \n\n*\tIn accordance with the Cabinet approval already granted, the inclusion of new provisions in the Act to reflect the functions and the authorities of the Examination Unit of the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Establishment of a 'Think Tank Forum' for the promotion of the Fisheries Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8578",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe importance of making group decisions has been identified for the purposes  of formulation of policies pertaining to the management and sustainable utilization of the marine resources of Sri Lanka, modernization of the Fisheries and Marine Tourism Sector, inclusive of the realization of aspirations, with a view to achieving economic development. In this regard, it has been proposed to establish a Think Tank Forum to enable to take decisions, taking into account the views and proposals of the experts and research data. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to establish a Think Tank Forum comprising of the economic experts, environmentalists, legal experts, marine engineers, naval and guided wave technicians, sociologists, representatives of the fisheries and tourism sectors and fishermen, under the Ministry of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Implementation of the 04th Round of Duty Concessions under the Asia Pacific Trade Agreement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8577",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asia Pacific Trade Agreement (APTA) which is a Regional Co-operation Agreement comprising of 06 member countries namely, Bangladesh, China, India, Laos, South Korea and Sri Lanka (previously known as the Bangkok Agreement), is the only operational trade agreement in which China and India, the two of the fastest growing markets in the world, are members. Under this trade agreement, the 03 rounds of duty concessions on selected trade items are implemented from 1990 up to now and accordingly, Sri Lanka has granted duty concessions on 442 items. \n\n\tUnder the 04th round of the agreement, Sri Lanka has agreed to grant duty concessions for a further 143 items so as not to cause any adverse effect on the state revenue and the local industries. All member countries have agreed to implement the duty concessions effective from January 2018 at the 4th round of duty concessions. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to implement the duty concessions of the said 143 items agreed upon by Sri Lanka effective from January 2018 and for this purpose to issue an Order under the Revenue Protection Act, No.19 of 1962 and present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Renaming the Institute of Personnel Management (IPM), Sri Lanka as the 'Chartered Institute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8576",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'The Institute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka' was founded in the year 1959, with a view to creating competent professionals in the field of human resources and utilizing same to elevate the productivity of the country to a higher level, recognizing the uniqueness of professions relating to the subject of human resource management. Subsequently, the Institute has been incorporated by the Act, No.24 of 1976. \n\n\tThe Institute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka which is regarded as the pioneering institute which provides the knowledge and training required for the public and private institutions in regard to human resource management, represents approximately 1,500 full time members who have fulfilled the professional qualifications.  A proposal has been made to amend its name to read as the 'Chartered Institute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka' in order to formalize the function of the institute, to enhance its standardized  professionalism, recognition and the reputation. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour, Trade Union Relations and Sabaragamu Development, to amend the Institute of Personnel Management, Sri Lanka Act, No.24 of 1976 making provisions for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Taking action in respect of the encroachments in the Railway reservations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8575",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The total extent of the railway reserved lands belonging to the Sri Lanka Railways is about 14,000 acres. Out of which, around 10% of lands has been provided to various stakeholders on lease basis and the rest of 80% of the said  lands are encroachments. The majority of these encroachers is the general public and among them, there are a few officers presently serving and as well as few retired officers in the Sri Lanka Railways. It is an unhealthy precedent to allow the railway employees themselves to occupy the lands   belonging to the Sri Lanka Railways unlawfully and thereby causing a loss of tax revenue to the Government.\n\n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to appoint a Cabinet Sub Committee headed by himself, comprising of the following Ministers as members to examine the possibility of adopting a fair and concessionary measure in respect of these railway employees and to submit a report to the Cabinet, within three (03) months, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n\t*\tHon. Mangala Samaraweera, \n\t\tMinister of Finance and Mass Media; \n\n\t*\tHon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, \n\t\tMinister of Public Administration and Management; and\n\t\t\n\t*\tHon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, \n\t\tMinister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-01-30",
    "description": "Directions to prevent the use of the property belonging to the State  during the period of election for the purpose of promoting political activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8574",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to preventing the use of any movable or immovable property belonging to the State or any Public Corporation during the period of election, for the purposes of promoting political parties, groups and candidates or causing injustice or obstructing the conduct of a free and fair election, the Direction, No.2048/2 made by the Election Commission under sub paragraph (a) of paragraph(4) of Article 104(B) of the Constitution, has been published in the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2017-12-04. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to present the Gazette Notification, incorporating the said provisions in Parliament by the adoption of a resolution, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Establishment of a Special High Court to inquire into legal proceedings expeditiously with regard to allegations of Bribery and Corruption and extremely complex charges on financial crimes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8573",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to establish a High Court comprising of three judges specially designated to inquire into the legal proceedings expeditiously with regard to allegations of Bribery and Corruption and extremely complex charges on Financial Crimes. An amendment to the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978, for this purpose, has been drafted by the Legal Draftsman. \n\nAccordingly, taking into account, the objective criteria such as, the nature, gravity and the complexity of the offence, the impact of the crime on the victim or the state, the national interest etc., as the case may be, the crimes specifically mentioned in the Act, could be referred by the Attorney General or the Director General of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption, to the proposed High Court. The draft Bill has now been referred to the Attorney General for clearance.  The above mentioned matters presented to the Cabinet by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, were noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and Vietnam in the field of Information and Communication",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8572",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between Sri Lanka and Vietnam pertaining to Information and Communication, with a view to strengthening the friendly relations between the two countries for the promotion of bilateral cooperation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Signing of the Sri Lanka - Singapore Free Trade Agreement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8571",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Experts in both countries have made deliberations and reached consensus regarding the provisions incorporated in the Free Trade Agreement proposed to be signed between Sri Lanka and Singapore.  Provisions relating to the fields of trade in goods, trade in services, liberalization of  services, investment, government procurement, competition etc. are included in the proposed Free Trade Agreement. Action has been taken to incorporate appropriate amendments  as well considering the observations made by several Ministers in regard to the draft Agreement. By the incorporation of the said amendments, a more favourable environment would be created for investments and as such, the foreign direct  investments from Singapore to Sri Lanka will be enhanced.   \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to sign the Sri Lanka - Singapore Free Trade Agreement on behalf of Sri Lanka, subject to clearance of the final draft Agreement by the Attorney General, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Active Liability Management Draft Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8570",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The maintenance of Public Debt of Sri Lanka on a sustainable level has received focus at national level. Appropriate systems of reforms have to be adopted to prevent any risk that may occur in this regard. Therefore, the Cabinet has granted approval to draft legislation to adopt the liability management as a strategy for active public debt management. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to publish the Active Liability Management Draft Bill prepared accordingly, in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present it in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "The Host Country Agreement  with regard to the CITES CoP, 18th Summit which Sri Lanka will host in 2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8569",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has been a party to the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora - CITES from the year 1976. The Cabinet has granted approval to host the 18th Summit of the parties of this Convention in Sri Lanka in the year 2019. \n\nAccordingly, it is due to hold the said Convention from 22nd of May 2019 to 03rd of June 2019 in Sri Lanka and as such, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to sign a host county agreement pertaining to the Convention which Sri Lanka will host in 2019, between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Secretariat to the above mentioned International Convention, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Construction of New Court Buildings",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8568",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Most of the buildings where the Courts are housed in Sri Lanka are very old and, therefore, a large amount of money has to be spent for their maintenance.  Since the legal proceedings are ever increasing the space available in the buildings are also inadequate. Further, the Court Complexes in Welimada and Ratnapura which are situated in landslide risk prone areas are required to be relocated.   \nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to construct new buildings for the Court Complexes situated in the areas of Welimada, Ratnapura, Theldeniya, Pugoda, Kantale and Kilinochchi by utilizing the financial provisions set apart from the budget for the year 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Implementation of the Anuradhapura North Water Supply Project - Phase 1",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8567",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Anuradhapura North Water Supply Project - Phase 1 is implemented with the objective of providing safe drinking water to the people living in the Rambewa and Medawachchiya Divisional Secretary Divisions who depend on unsafe ground water which causes Chronic Kidney Diseases and Dental and Skeletal Fluorosis. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the construction of the Intake Facility, the Water Treatment Plant, the Water Storage Structures and the Mechanical, Electrical and Building Works, under Phase 1 of the project, to M/s Access Engineering PLC for a sum equivalent to a total of US$ 6.17 million received from the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) and a sum of Rs.2,349 million of domestic funds , as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Implementation of the Phase III of the Medirigiriya Water Supply Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8566",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The  Medirigiriya Water Supply Scheme is implemented with the objective of providing safe drinking water to the people in the Medirigiriya Divisional Secretariat division, which has  been identified as an area which lacks safe drinking water resources and where the chronic kidney disease prevails. Owing to the resettlement of families in the same area, displaced due to the Moragahakanda reservoir project, the demand for safe drinking water is increasing and the Phase III of the Medirigiriya Water Supply Scheme has been decided to be implemented so as to supply water to cover  the demand. \nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the Design and Build contract for the distribution system under Phase III of the said project to M/s Squire Mech Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.1,230 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Development of the Infrastructure facilities of the Uva Wellassa University - Phase 2",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8565",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Uva Wellassa University conducts 13 degree courses relevant to the industrial sector and currently about 2,200 students are engaged in educational activities. The intake of students to the university is being gradually increased and accordingly to coincide with it, the infrastructure facilities too have to be upgraded. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to commence the construction activities of the library building, auditorium, staff learning unit, the alternative water supply system, students' welfare centre of the Uva Wellassa University and the activities related to the development of the main entrance of the University, in the year 2018 and to call for bids to select suitable contractors for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Procuring of 50 Electric Buses for the Sri Lanka Transport Board to upgrade the urban public transport service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8564",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Most of the people use their private vehicles for their day today transport needs due to the lack of comfortable, dependable and efficient public transport service and it contributes to a heavy traffic congestion on city roads and  air pollution.  \n\nThe Sri Lanka Transport Board (SLTB) possesses 6,300 buses in running condition and out of which 2,467 are more than 10 years old. Since such buses are subject to frequent wayside breakdowns, it causes problems to provide the public with a more reliable and efficient bus service. Further, the total number of buses required for the Transport Board is 7,257 to operate in accordance with a time table. At present, the fleet of buses of the SLTB consists 100% of diesel buses, which is a contributory factor for air pollution. \n\nAccordingly, the proposals made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to install an environment friendly Bus Rapid Transit System (BRT) within the city of Colombo, so that the elderly and the disabled passengers also can travel easily, and to purchase 50 electronic low floor air conditioned buses to the Sri Lanka Transport Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Installation of an Aeronautical Information Management System",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8563",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been called for the Supply, Installation and Commissioning of  an Aeronautical Information Management System for Sri Lanka and accordingly, a French and a Canadian company have presented their bids for the purpose. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the above contract to M/s Thales Air Systems S.A.S., France, for a sum equivalent to the total of Euro 3.3 million and Rs.65 million, as recommended by the Technical Evaluation Committee which evaluated the bids and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
