    "description": "Improvements to the Grand Oriental Hotel, Colombo through  Public-Private Partnership",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8561",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to develop the Grand Oriental Hotel in Colombo, under the Public-Private Partnership process while protecting its heritage and to transform it into a luxurious hotel brand. The HPL Hotels and Resorts of Singapore  has submitted a proposal to conduct a feasibility study in this regard.  \n\n\tAs such, the joint proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media; Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Public Enterprise Development; and Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to appoint a Project Committee for the evaluation of the said proposal and to pursue action in this regard, subject to the relevant guidelines of the Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Vietnamese People's Police Academy and the National Police Academy of Sri Lanka on Cooperation in Police Training and Scientific Research",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8560",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Vietnam and Sri Lanka have agreed to enhance bilateral cooperation between the two countries for the prevention of crimes. As such, with a view to strengthening the cooperation through the exchange of updated information on Police Training and Scientific Research, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Vietnamese People's Police Academy and the National Police Academy of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Increasing the Free Postal Facilities granted to the Hon. Members of Parliament and the Members of the Provincial Councils",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8559",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The free postal facilities granted to the Hon. Members of Parliament and the Members of the Provincial Councils have not been revised since the year 2007 and now, requests have been made to revise the existing postal charges to coincide with the revision of the postal charges made from time to time. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. M.H.A. Haleem, the Minister of Posts, Postal Services and Muslim Religious Affairs, to increase the limit of the free annual postal facilities offered presently to the Hon. Members of Parliament from Rs.175,000/- up to Rs.350,000/- and to increase the limit of the free annual postal facilities offered presently to the Hon. Members of the Provincial Councils from Rs.24,000/- up to Rs.48,000/-, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Amendment to the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No.15 of 1979 to dispense with the requirement of producing of a suspect/accused in person to court at identified specific instances",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8558",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Every suspect taken into custody should be produced before a Magistrate within 24 hours and where such suspect is committed to remand custody without granting bail, such detainee should be produced in the Magistrate's Court  for the extension of the order generally once in two (02) weeks.  Further, even in circumstances in which the Magistrate does not have the jurisdiction to grant bail, the suspect/accused person should be produced before the Magistrate from time to time.   \n\n\tTaking into consideration the delays in the judicial process and especially the unfortunate incidents that occurred while transporting the detainees to the Court, the life threats against the detainees and the opportunities for them to flee away from custody, focus has been drawn for limiting the instances of taking the suspects/accused before Court. As such, in accordance with the recommendations of the Special Committee appointed for the above amendments to the Penal Code and the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, while further maintaining the requirement of monitoring the welfare of the detainee, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to amend the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No.15 of 1979, to introduce a procedure which does not require  a suspect or an accused  person to be produced in person before the Magistrate under identified specific instances for the purpose of extending the order relating to the committal to remand custody, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Obtaining Technical Assistance for improving the production of the major fruit crops and fruit value chains in Sri Lanka and commercialization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8557",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The South-South Cooperation of the People's Republic of China has agreed to provide technical assistance for a project implemented with the objective of increasing the production of fruits in Sri Lanka and enhancing the business activities to suit the local and export markets by promoting an effective agro-business sector. Under this project, it has been planned to raise the production, quality and effectiveness targeting fruits such as, banana, mango and pineapple, to enhance the value chains and to promote the Public-Private Partnership process to attract the interest of investments for fruit orchards and processing centres.  \n\n\tThe value chain activities of banana will be carried out mainly based in the Districts of Monaragala and Kalutara, and the value chain activities of mango will be carried out based on the Districts of Anuradhapura and Kilinochchi and the same of Pineapple based on the Districts of Gampaha, Kurunegala and Monaragala. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to enter into a Tripartite Agreement among the Government of Sri Lanka, the Government of China and the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO) for the implementation of the above project, which will be beneficial for the development of the agricultural sector in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Agricultural Cooperation between Sri Lanka and  Turkey",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8556",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Agricultural Cooperation, for the exchange of knowledge, technology and techniques relating to agricultural activities between Sri Lanka and Turkey, was approved by the Cabinet. The Cabinet also took note of the fact that it has been planned to enter into a special Agreement pertaining to the increase of the quantity of tea to be exported to the Republic of Turkey from Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Import of Bristle Fiber for export with Value Addition",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8555",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- A quantity between 8,000 MT to 15,000 MT of Bristle Fiber, which is a coconut related product, is exported annually from our country to around 20 countries and a considerable amount of foreign exchange is received by such export process. Even though, there is a possibility of deriving more foreign exchange by exporting bristle fiber brushes and brooms as Value Added products, the process has been interrupted due to the difficulties in obtaining bristle fiber locally.  \n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to permit the importation of Bristle fiber from India for value addition and exportation, subject to strict plant quarantine rules and regulations, the recommendations of the Coconut Research Institute and the relevant conditions, until the local coconut harvest becomes stable, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Agreement between Turkmenistan and Sri Lanka on Mutual Visa Exemption for Holders of Diplomatic and Official Passports",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8554",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. S.B. Navinne, the Minister of  Internal Affairs, Wayamba Development and Cultural Affairs, to enter into an Agreement  between Sri Lanka and Turkmenistan on Mutual Visa Exemption for citizens who are Holders of Diplomatic and Official Passports when traveling between the two countries, with the objective of furthering friendly relations between the two countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Implementation of Land Surveys and Socio-Economic Surveys of all lands belonging to the Sri Lanka Railways",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8553",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka Railways owns a considerable extent of lands set apart by the Government of Sri Lanka, considering the present and future needs. Encroachment on railway lands and utilizing them due to various socio- economic and political reasons have resulted in a number of problems with regard to clear demarcation of boundaries and this has become a hindrance for the improvement of railway operations and its modernization activities. The Sri Lanka Railways has given around 7,000 plots of land on lease basis with a view to generating revenue and the management of such lands and the collection of outstanding lease payments are not carried out satisfactorily.   \n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to conduct surveys covering all lands belonging to the Sri Lanka Railways, in order to define the boundaries of the railway lands, to map out them accurately and as well as to conduct socio-economic surveys covering  encroachment of all railway lands to resettle the encroachers residing on them and to formalize the management of railway lands given on lease basis, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-16-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-01-16",
    "description": "Smallholder Agribusiness Partnership (SAP) Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8552",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Smallholder Agribusiness Partnership Programme' is implemented under the financial assistance of the International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD) with a view to enhancing their competitive abilities while assisting in broadening the livelihood avenues of rural small scale agri producers. This project which is implemented Island wide giving priority to low income generating districts provides benefits to around 57,500 low income rural families. \n\n\tA major component of this project is the provision of the necessary financial facilities for the young agri-entrepreneurs for the development of their farms and to strengthen their enterprises at commercial level. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to provide credit facilities with an annual interest rate of 6.5% for the producer groups, farmer groups, and the young agri-entrepreneurs, under this programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-09-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-01-09",
    "description": "Granting Relief Measures to Media Persons who were subject to various harassments and oppressions during the period from 2005 - 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8551",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- By the publication of press notifications, opportunities were afforded to the media persons who were subject to various harassments and oppressions during the period from 2005 - 2015 to submit their appeals, with a view to granting relief to them. A Cabinet Sub-Committee was appointed under the Chairmanship of the Ex-Minister of Foreign Affairs to make recommendations to the Cabinet, with regard to such appeals. Subsequently, the period of time for appeals was then extended up to 01st May 2017 and in response to which 14 more applications have been received. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to appoint a fresh Cabinet Sub-Committee comprising of the following Ministers to examine the appeals and make recommendations, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\t*\tHon. Mangala Samaraweera,\n\t\tMinister of Finance and Mass Media - (Chairman);\n\n\t*\tHon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, \n\t\tMinister of Disaster Management; and\n\n\t*\tHon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, \n\t\tMinister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-01-09-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-01-09",
    "description": "Anuradhapura North Water Supply Project - Phase - II - Consultancy Contract for Detailed Design and Bidding Assistance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8550",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the Anuradhapura North Water Supply Project - Phase - II - Consultancy Contract for Detailed Design and Bidding Assistance to M/s NJS Concultants Co. Ltd. of Japan in association with M/s Ceywater Consultants (Pvt.) Ltd. and M/s EML Consultants (Pvt.) Ltd. of Sri Lanka, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Consultants Procurement Committee (SCACPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
