    "doc_id": "2017-12-19-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Providing Police Quarters for Junior Police Officers in the Southern Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8499",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been decided to purchase 192 houses from the 'Nila Sewana' housing project at Wekunagoda in  Galle, to provide housing facilities adequately, to the junior police officers in service in the Police Divisions of Galle, Matara, Elpitiya and Tangalle in the Southern Province.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to secure funds to the amount of Rs.729.6 million for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-19-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Securing a plot of land for the construction of an Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit for the Colombo East Base Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8498",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The functions of the Colombo East Base Hospital situated in Mulleriyawa, has been greatly expanded during the previous years and concurrent to same, it has become essential to upgrade the space facilities of the hospital. Therefore, it is essential to construct an Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit for the hospital and for this purpose, a plot of land  adjoining the hospital land with easy access facilities is required. \n\nA plot of land around 01 hectare out of the land belonging to the hospital has been given on a 30 year lease to a private party in 2001, but the said party has failed to fulfill the conditions of the lease. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to cancel the relevant lease agreement and to release the said land  for the construction of an Emergency Treatment Unit for same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-19-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Enhancing the organic food production and opening of export markets for such products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8497",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- A great demand is being created in the International Market for organic food products produced devoid of chemical fertilizer, insecticide and pesticide. As such, having selected 15,000 farmers engaged in organic agriculture under the 'National Programme on Food Production', a programme has been planned to be implemented to provide them with the basic knowledge and training to engage in  organic farming in a systematic manner to give them the production certificate required to present their products to the International markets and to provide facilities for export of such products. \n\n\tA proposal has also been made to implement a programme to provide technical training for 2,500 young farmers on mushroom cultivation, inviting a specialist group from China and to provide them with market opportunities and financial facilities. It has also been planned to establish several model farms within the country where technological equipment and implements are used to attract the young community to agriculture and to impart about 6,500 youth  with agri entrepreneur knowledge.\n\n\tAccordingly, the Joint proposal made by H.E. the President, Maithripala Sirisena, and Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment, Welfare and Kandyan Heritage, to implement the said programmes, with the objective of enhancing the domestic food production and making avenues for obtaining a high revenue for the local farmers by exporting the agri products of Sri Lanka to the International markets, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
