    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Construction of another 44 bridges by utilizing the balance of provisions of the  Rural Bridges Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8494",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The project duration of the Rural Bridges Project implemented to construct steel bridges, with the objective of avoiding transport difficulties faced by the people in the rural areas is due to expire on 8th March 2018. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to design and construct 35 additional rural bridges  and 09 temporary span panel bridges for each Province, by utilizing the balance of the contingencies allocated under Phase II and III of the said project and to extend the project duration up to 31st August 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-19-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Carrying out maintenance work of the  Turbine of Unit 2 and the major accessories of the Lakvijaya Power Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8493",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Lakvijaya power plant in Puttlam consists of 3 units each of 300 MW.  The unit 02 of the Turbine which started its power generation activity in the year 2014,  consists of 15 major systems and the maintenance work pertaining to the  system due for the first time has to be carried out. The Memorandum of Understanding entered into with the China Machinery Engineering Corporation (CMEC), the original contractor, is valid until September 2019.\n\nTherefore, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the said maintenance contract to  the China Machinery Engineering Corporation (CMEC) for a sum of Rs.263.4 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
