    "doc_id": "2017-11-14-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-11-14",
    "description": "Establishment of the Selacine Television Institute as a State Owned  Company Limited by Guarantee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8365",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The fully state owned Selacine Television Institute which commenced in the year 1982 primarily conducts Government Commercial advertising and event management. As such, for the institution to enable build up stability as an effective commercial institute functioning competitively along with the other commercial advertising and event management institutions, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to establish the Selacine Television Institute under the Companies Act, No.7 of 2007 as a fully state owned company limited by guarantee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-14-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-11-14",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and South Africa on Scientific and Technological Cooperation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8364",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and South Africa to promote an effective cooperation in the fields of science, research and technology for the enhancement of social and economic development. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to sign the MoU during the Science Forum which will be held on 07th and 08th of December 2017 in South Africa, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-14-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-11-14",
    "description": "Renovation of the unstable Slopes and Landslides along the Upcountry Railway Line",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8363",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Buildings Research Organization (NBRO) has pointed out the need of implementing a project for stabilizing the landslides prone areas and unstable slopes found along the upcountry railway line with a view to ensuring the uninterrupted and safe operational activities of the railway line, taking into consideration the adverse effects of the landslides which occurred during the past period.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation and Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, for the National Buildings Research Organization and the Sri Lanka Railways to implement the project jointly for the renovation of landslide risk areas and unstable slopes in the upcountry railway line including the improvement of the drainage system giving priority over to the areas between Rambukkana and Badulla, which would span over the next 5 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-14-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-11-14",
    "description": "Establishment of a Flying School at the Batticaloa Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8362",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the opening of the Batticaloa Airport more constructively, for civil aviation operations it is anticipated that a significant development will take place in the economic activities of the Eastern Province owing to the reawakening of the domestic Civil Aviation Services simultaneously with the development of the tourism industry. Considering the conducive weather condition prevailing in the area for the civil aviation activities, the presence of 5 domestic aerodromes within a radius of 135km with less air traffic congestion, the ability of making operational activities in a free air space etc., proposals for Expression of Interests (EoI) have been called for from the parties interested in the domestic air services operational activities of the Batticaloa Airport.   \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to provide the facilities required to implement the project proposal presented by M/s Skurai Aviation to operate domestic aviation services at the Batticaloa Airport and to establish a Flying Training School at the Batticaloa Airport, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-14-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-11-14",
    "description": "Formulation of a formal methodology for the management of hazardous wastes and chemicals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8361",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the face of rapid industrialization, many countries have focused their attention on the mitigation of the adverse effects caused to the human health and environment due to the increased use of chemical substances.  Sri Lanka is also a signatory to the Basel Convention, Stockholm Convention, Rotterdam Convention and the Minamata Convention adopted in this regard. \n\n\tTherefore, when encouraging industry related investments for the economic development of Sri Lanka, it is necessary for Sri Lanka to take measures to ensure that chemical substances are used securely without being harmful to the eco-system. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, for the formulation of a National Policy on the Management of hazardous wastes and chemicals in Sri Lanka and a comprehensive methodology for implementation of same with the participation of all relevant stakeholders, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Bringing back to normalcy to the prevailing shortage of Petrol in the country  expeditiously",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8360",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The attention of the Cabinet has been drawn to the shortage of Petrol countrywide which has caused an obstruction to the day to day activities of the General Public.  As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to appoint a Ministerial Sub\u2011Committee comprising of the following Ministers to examine and make recommendations in regard to urgent measures to be adopted to avoid the prevailing shortage of petrol, the causes which have led to such situation, the parties responsible for such occurrence and measures to avoid recurrence of such situation in future, was approved by the Cabinet.   \n\ni.\tHon.\t(Dr.) Sarath Amunugama\n\tMinister of Special Assignments - (Chairman)\n\t\t\t\nii.\tHon.\tAnura Priyadharshana Yapa\n\tMinister of Disaster Management\n\niii.\tHon.\tPatali Champika Ranawaka\n\tMinister of Megapolis and Western Development\n\niv.\tHon.\tArjuna Ranatunga\n\tMinister of Petroleum Resources Development"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Awarding of the Contract for the Balance Construction Work of the Four Storey Building for the District Secretariat of Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8359",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously to construct a four storey building for the District Secretariat of Polonnaruwa.  Accordingly, the contract for the construction of its Phase\u2011I had been awarded to M/s Micro Construction (Pvt.) Ltd., and the construction activities are at the level of nearing completion. \n\nConsidering the progress of the construction activities, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to award the construction of its Phase\u2011II over to the same company for a sum of Rs.952.90 million, excluding taxes, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Construction of a New Two Storey Building for the Divisional Secretariat of Mahiyanganaya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8358",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously to construct a new two storey building for the Divisional Secretariat of Mahiyanganaya. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to award the contract for the construction of the building to M/s Finite Lanka (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.140.96 million, excluding taxes, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Establishment of a High Court in terms of Article 105 (1)(c) of the Constitution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8357",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been practically difficult to complete the cases expeditiously, pertaining to financial frauds, corruption, defrauding the State of its assets and revenue and similar offences, owing to the backlog of cases in the Courts of Law of the country.  As such, it has been identified that the establishment of a High Court dedicated to hear expeditiously, the charges pertaining to offences committed  against Public Property, Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing, Criminal Breach of Trust, Misappropriation of Public Property and Organized Crimes including Bribery and Corruption and highly complex financial frauds, is suited. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation necessary to establish a High Court in terms of the provisions of Article 105 (1)(c) of the Constitution,  comprising of 3 Benches each with 3 judges named by the Chief Justice and for the Chief Justice to refer the cases relating to the commission of the  specified offences, at the request of the Attorney General or on his own motion and to provide for an appeal directly to the Supreme Court against an Order made by such High Court, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Submission of the Report on 'Recent Economic Developments: Highlights of 2017 and Prospects for 2018' of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka to  Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8356",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to present the Report published by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka on 'Recent Economic Developments: Highlights of 2017 and Prospects for 2018' inclusive of the performance of the Real Sector, External Sector, Fiscal Sector and the Monetary Sector', up to October 2017, in Parliament, to coincide with the 2018 budget, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Amending legislation  relating to Bribery and Corruption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8355",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to amend the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption Act and the Acts incidental thereto, in order to make the laws applicable for eradicating bribery and corruption in Sri Lanka to meet the contemporary legal requirements and to overcome the issues which have surfaced due to the inconsistencies found in the existing laws when implementing same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Establishment of a 400 MW Natural Gas Power Plant in Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8354",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the prime objective of providing electricity to the industrial zone proposed to be constructed at Hambantota and to overcome the power scarcity that may occur in the future, it has been decided to establish a Natural Gas Power Plant of 400 MW, in Hambantota as a joint project implemented by the Government of China and the Government of Sri Lanka. The project is expected to be implemented as a Joint Venture between the the China Machinery Engineering Corporation (CMEC), nominated by the Government of China and the Ceylon Electricity Board. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to implement the proposed project with relevant approvals, having included it into the long term energy plan accepted by the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "House of Justice Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8353",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The accommodation of the buildings  presently, used for  the High Courts, District Courts and Magistrate's Courts in the Hulftsdorp Court Complex, Colombo is limited and an element of risk has cropped up due to the buildings being very old.  Further, adequate building facilities need to be provided for the different institutions related to the justice sector, located in the Superior Courts Complex. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to select a suitable developer/contractor from among the local and foreign contractors who are presently engaged in the implementation of development projects in the country on competitive basis, to implement the 'House of Justice' project for the construction of a Courts complex comprising of 40 Court Houses, Ministry of Justice complex, upgrading the Judges' Institute and a Law Centre for training of Attorneys-at-Law, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Purchasing Coal for the Coal Power Plant in Puttalam through Spot Tenders",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8352",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the requirement of the supply of coal expeditiously to the Coal Power Plant in Puttalam, authority has been granted to purchase the required coal through spot tender procedure subject to the covering approval of the Cabinet and as approved by the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SSCAPC). Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy,  to purchase an amount of 300,000 MT of coal required for  the plant from the Swiss Singapore Overseas Enterprises Pte. Ltd., the lowest substantially responsive bidder, out of the registered suppliers at FOBT price of US$ 87.97 per MT, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Galigamuwa Water Supply Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8351",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement project, it is expected to provide upgraded Water Supply facilities for about 530,000 people and upgraded sanitation facilities for another 175,000 people living in 540 Grama Niladhari Divisions, in the Districts of Mullaitivu, Kilinochchi, Badulla, Monaragala, Ratnapura, Kegalle and Nuwara Eliya. \n\nUnder the first component of this project, the Galigamuwa Water supply scheme, in Kegalle district is expected to be constructed  and by which safe drinking water will be provided for a population of 45,000 in 29 Grama Niladhari Divisions including the Galigamuwa town, as well in future. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the construction of a  Water Treatment Plant with a treated water production capacity of 9,000 cubic meters per day and the laying of transmission and distribution systems and the related activities, to M/s Sierra Construction (Pvt.) limited, for a sum of US$ 4.6 million and LKR 1,268 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Construction of the Training Centre and other buildings at Thelawala under the Greater Colombo Water & Wastewater Management Improvement Investment Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8350",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of the Greater Colombo Water & Wastewater Management Improvement Investment Programme is to regulate the use of non\u2011revenue water and the improvement and management of the water facilities provided to the general public. Under  second phase of the programme, it is proposed to construct the training centre at Thelawala  and this training centre is expected to be used to train officers of different levels who are engaged in the regulatory project of non\u2011revenue water and other officers of the National Water Supply & Drainage Board. \n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the construction of a four storey training centre, five storey hostel building and a canteen to M/s Sierra Construction (Pvt.) Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Implementation of the expansion of Pipe Borne Sewerage Coverage in the Dehiwala-Mt. Lavinia",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8349",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to secure funds for the project for the expansion of Pipe Borne Sewerage Coverage in the Urban Area of Dehiwala-Mt.Lavinia subject to high urbanization and to award the contract of the project to M/s Vinci Construction Grands Projects/LUDWIG PFEIFFER Hoch\u2011u Tiefabau GmBH & Co., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Renovation activities of the Akuressa Nilwala National College of Education damaged due to natural disasters",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8348",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The buildings and equipment of the Akuressa Nilwala National College of Education were severely damaged due to the effects of natural disasters that took place in last May and consequently, the assignment of teachers to the schools duly, has been delayed as a result of the inability to complete the training courses of teachers within the stipulated period. \n\n\tTherefore, it is necessary to renovate those damaged buildings expeditiously and modernize same to suit the future needs and the Czech Republic has agreed to provide the financial assistance required for the purpose. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to obtain financial aid amounting to Rs.15 million for carrying out the renovation and improvement activities of the Nilwala National College of Education, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Use of underutilized Lands for Housing and Human Settlement Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8347",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that certain challenges have surfaced in the use of underutilized lands for development activities as a result of the regulations imposed by the Government for the prevention of paddy lands, other agricultural lands and forest reserves being used for other purposes. When lands are used for human settlement development, specially, in rapidly urbanizing areas and  if the name of a portion of land ends with the terms 'Wela', 'Kumbura', or 'Deniya' in a survey plan, it has been found difficult to use such lands for housing construction although the lands cannot actually be used for cultivation.  As such, the Cabinet has already appointed a Committee to formulate an expeditious methodology and make recommendations with regard to releasing of underutilized lands for development purposes.  \n\n\tThe joint proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture and Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to appoint a special team of officers from the Head Office of the Agrarian Development Department to accord  priority and take action to carry out field inspections expeditiously with the officers of the relevant institutions,  when such underutilized lands have to be used for housing construction and subsequently grant the approval required, in accordance with the recommendations of the Officials' Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Signing of an Agreement for the Transfer of sentenced persons between Sri Lanka and  Thailand",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8346",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to enter into an Agreement between Sri Lanka and Thailand to transfer a citizen of Thailand who has been convicted by a Court of Law in Sri Lanka  and imprisoned and a citizen of Sri Lanka who has been convicted by a Court of Law in Thailand and imprisoned subject to punishment, between the two countries to enable them to spend the rest of their period of punishment in their own countries and to ratify the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Vesting of the lands utilized for the Parliamentary Complex",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8345",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- A part of the lands in extent of about 1,000 acres acquired from the areas of Battaramulla, Kaduwela, Sri Jayawardenapura and Maharagama by the Urban Development Authority (UDA) under the Administrative Capital City Development Programme of Sri Jayawardenapura, Kotte, have been utilized for the construction of the Parliamentary Complex and another part apportioned as water reserves. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to vest such portions of land which are utilized for the Parliamentary Complex but not formally vested up to now, with the Sri Lanka Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Presenting the Gazette Notification No.2031/49 issued in terms of the Revenue Protection Act for approval of Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8344",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the requests made by the relevant industrialists, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to present the Gazette Notification No.2031/49 dated 11th August 2017 in terms of the Revenue Protection Act, No.19 of 1962, to amend the descriptions of the selected Harmonized Commodity Codes and to create new sub divisions therein, in accordance with the policy decisions of the Government, in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Providing a monthly allowance to the elderly citizens over 100 years of age",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8343",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The existence of elderly population over 100 years of age is considered a benchmark that reflects a country's development in the field of health. It has been identified that by now around 350 elderly people over 100 years of age live in Sri Lanka.  \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment, Welfare and Kandyan Heritage, to grant a payment of Rs.5,000/- per month for the low income earning elderly citizens over 100 years of age with a view to ensuring the security of their lives, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-07-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-11-07",
    "description": "Entering into a Framework Agreement for Economic Development Cooperation with the Republic of Korea",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8342",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Korea has agreed to grant a concessionary loan of a sum  equivalent to US$ 500 million to Sri Lanka for development purposes within the period from 2017 to 2019, with a view to further strengthening the friendship and the economic cooperation between the two countries. The Korean loan aid is granted at  very low interest rates with a 40 year repayment period including a 10 year grace period. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into a Framework Agreement with the Government of the Republic of Korea to obtain the said loan scheduled to be given from the Economic Development Corporation Fund of the Export and Import Bank of Korea, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
