    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Supply and Installation of a Whole Body MRI Scanner for the General Hospital, Sri Jayawardenepura",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8119",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is essential to have the MRI Scans to diagnose the conditions of the brain and the central nerves system and as well as the breast and heart diseases. It has, therefore, been found that the purchasing of a 3.0 Tesla Whole Body MRI Scanner is essential for enhancing the quality of treatment services provided by the General Hospital of Sri Jayawardenepura. \n\nAs such, Open International Bidding has been called for and in response 03 bids have now been submitted for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the relevant contract to M/s. Dimo (Pvt) Ltd., the lowest evaluated substantially responsive bidder, for a sum of Rs.45 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC) which evaluated the bids, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "The Establishment of Public-Private Joint Ventures for the upliftment of the Pharmaceutical Industry of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8118",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the upliftment of the Pharmaceutical Industry of Sri Lanka, a considerable amount of foreign exchange used for the import of pharmaceuticals could be saved and it would also pave the way for keeping the prices of pharmaceuticals stable.  Therefore, the Government has planned to identify investors with the possibility of making an uninterrupted supply of fresh and high quality Pharmaceutical items effectively to the Government Hospitals and establish joint ventures between such investors and the State Pharmaceutical Manufacturing Corporation. \n\nAs such, the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee has recommended to accept the 31 proposals out of the 36 proposals submitted by 24 investors who have responded. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to implement the accepted proposals with the selected investors to commence Joint Ventures on the Public-Private-Partnership basis subject to the recommendations of the Officials' Committee appointed headed by the Secretary to the Treasury, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
