    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for the Supply, Installation and Commissioning of Air Traffic Control Simulator Training System for the Civil Aviation Training Centre to M/s. Adacel Technologies Limited as decided by the Procurement Appeal Board and  in accordance with the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) pertaining to the field of migrant labour proposed to be entered into between Sri Lanka and Lebanon",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8113",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- A considerable number of Sri Lankan migrant labour is employed in Lebanon and in the year 2017 alone, the number of 1,593 persons registered in the Foreign Employment Bureau have left for employment in Lebanon and 79% out of them have taken up household employment. The two countries have come to an Agreement to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding pertaining to the field of migrant labour with the objective of safeguarding the rights and the welfare of the Sri Lankan migrant labour employed in Lebanon. \n\tThrough the proposed MoU, positive measures will be taken for the  implementation of a safe service environment and a transparent and low cost recruitment procedure for the Sri Lankan migrant labour. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice and Foreign Employment, to sign the proposed MoU between the two countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Provision of Bursaries for the Pirivena Student Monks",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8112",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The traditional education system formed in the country for the purpose of  creating a systematic and formal education to the Buddhist Monks is the Pirivena education system.  At present, 758 Pirivenas function throughout the Island in the form of Elementary Pirivena, Maha Pirivena and Vidyathana Pirivena. The budget 2017 proposed to grant a bursary for the Pirivena student monks for the promotion of their educational activities. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to grant a 'Learning Improvement Grant' to the Account of the Head of the Pirivena 'Kruthyadikari' to be used for the welfare activities of the Pirivena student monks for the supply of books and equipment, co-curricular activities, skills development activities, promotion of English language skills and to meet the travelling expenses and to implement the project under the strict supervision of the Ministry of Education, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Strengthening of the mechanism for the implementation of the Charter on the Child Rights",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8111",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka signed the Child Rights Convention and ratified same in the year 1991. As such, the Government of Sri Lanka is bound to ensure the rights of children to the maximum. The responsibility of giving effect to the commitments under the convention is vested with the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs and measures have been taken to give effect to the commitments  through the Officers of the Department of Probation and Child Care Services, National Child Protection Authority, the Children's Secretariat and the Officers attached to the Divisional Secretary's Offices.  \n\n\tSteps had been taken in the year 2000 to establish Operational Committees at the National, District and Divisional Level for follow-up and reporting on the activities under Section 40 of the Convention. Taking into consideration the present requirement, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to widen the composition and the functions of the Operational Committees, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Crash Programme for the supply of seed paddy for the 'Maha' Season 2017/18",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8110",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Normally paddy is cultivated in 8 lakh hectares of paddy land during the Maha season for which 4 million bushes of seed paddy are being used.  Due to the unfavourable weather conditions which prevailed in certain parts of the Island, it is expected that there will be a shortage in the supply of seed paddy during the Maha season of 2017/2018.  Therefore, a proposal has been made to jointly implement a crash programme for the supply of germination certified seed paddy by the Department of Agriculture in collaboration with the Provincial Departments of Agriculture, Mahaweli Authority and other relevant Institutions. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to purchase 560,000 bushels of high quality seed paddy expeditiously, from the areas where seed paddy cultivation was carried out successfully and from the paddy cultivations done for the purpose of consumption during the Yala season of 2017 and to sell such seed paddy among the farmers in areas where there is a shortage of seed paddy, was approved by the Cabinet.  Further, the Cabinet also granted approval to sell the seed paddy to the farmers in the Districts which were subject to severe drought during the past season and suffered loss of harvest, charging only 50% of the value."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Implementation of a project to undertake fish farming in cages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8109",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Global Ceylon Sea Food (Pvt) Ltd., the joint venture established in collaboration with the Continental Ceylon Sea Food (Pvt) Ltd., of Sri Lanka and the Continental Ceylon Sea Food A.S. Ltd., of Norway has submitted a proposal to undertake commercial scale fish farming such as the Sea Bass, Pompano and Grouper with high market demand by utilizing the technology of fish farming in cages in the open sea.  It has been proposed to be implemented in two (02) phases, adopting the best environmental conservation practices and modern technology.     \n\nThe proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to grant a 30 year lease to the Global Ceylon Sea Foods (Pvt.) Ltd. of the sea bed in extent of 150 hectares of the local coastal area in the Koddiyar Bay in the District of Trincomalee belonging to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority, for the implementation of this project identified as a project of high feasibility, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Establishment of Final Disposal Facility for Municipal Solid Waste (MSW) at Aruwakkalu, Puttalam",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8108",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the sudden collapse of the Meethotamulla landfill facility, the disposal of Municipal Solid Waste in the City of Colombo and suburbs has become a crisis.  In this situation, the expeditious implementation of the sanitary landfill in the Puttalam Aruwakkalu area for which approval has already be granted, is essential.   \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to carry out the activities of  the construction of the waste distribution centres relevant to the Solid Waste Management Project, the Sanitary Landfills and the connectivity railway tracks expeditiously and commence the waste disposal activities by the year 2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Construction of a new Auditorium in the town of Galle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8107",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Certain state functions, conferences, seminars, public gatherings and discussions relevant to the District of Galle and the entire Southern Province, are held in places close to the town of Galle. The Hall de Galle belonging to the Ministry of Home Affairs is mostly used for these activities at present and the existing facilities and space available are  not sufficient to carryout such activities. Therefore, a new Auditorium has been proposed to be constructed for the District Secretariat of Galle.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to construct an Auditorium of 2,000 seats with modern facilities, adjacent to the road having access to the Southern Expressway, to be used as a public Auditorium for such events held in the town of Galle, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Providing of Student Hostel facilities in the Sri Lanka - German Training Institute (SLGTI) in Killinochchi",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8106",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka-German Training Institute (SLGTI) belonging to the National Apprentice and Industrial Training Authority, situated in Killinochchi was established in the year 2016 and presently, around 200 students follow training courses at NVQ Levels 4,5, and 6. Around 57% of the present number of students are residents of the Districts outside the District of Killinochchi. The hostel facilities need to be improved since the present hostel facilities of this institute are sufficient only for 144 students and is expected to enroll 400 more students to its training courses within this year. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Chandima Weerakkody, the Minister of Skills Development and Vocational Training, to construct a new hostel building for the Sri Lanka-German Training Institute, Killinochchi, to enable to provide hostel facilities for 400 more students, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Establishment of a Social Innovation Lab",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8105",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish a Social Innovation Lab as a methodology to examine the effectiveness of the Government Policies, prior to their  implementation. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to implement the proposed Social Innovation Lab as a pilot project at the Ministry of Science, Technology and Research, with the assistance of the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), aimed at formulating effective policies as well as a vibrant and productive public service delivery through stability of policies, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Construction of small bridges for the convenient transportation of communities in the remote areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8104",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that in the most difficult remote areas in Sri Lanka, there are around 1,500 locations where people commute with the use of extremely unprotected temporarily erected trunk bridges across streams and rivers and in about 500 locations where people commute by crossing rivers and streams with difficulty without any kind of safety measures put in place. Therefore, it is essential to construct small bridges with the objective to providing safe transportation for the people living in such remote areas. In this respect, the National Engineering Research and Development Centre (NERDC) has been successful in designing and experimenting a long term durable special foot bridges at a low cost with the use of advanced technology. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to identify the locations where people commute unsafely by crossing streams, rivers etc. and construct 1,000 bridges within the forthcoming three years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Development of Sri Lankan Graphite to be used in Rechargeable Batteries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8103",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although Sri Lanka is a high quality graphite producing country, the economic benefit derived by the country takes a low value as a result of it being exported as a raw material without value addition. Therefore, the focus of the Government has been directed in promoting the export after improving the natural graphite as a value added product with the aim of generating a higher income. \n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to implement a research project by the National Institute of Fundamental Studies (NIFS) for the  improvement of the quality of the natural graphite in the country under appropriate innovative initiatives to enable it to be used in rechargeable batteries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Carrying out a feasibility study on the Greater Vavuniya Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8102",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to implement the Greater Vavuniya Water Supply Project with the main objective of providing safe drinking water to the people living in the Vavuniya Divisional Secretary's Division and the Vavuniya South and Cheddikulam where people have been severely affected with the Chronic Kidney Disease.  \n\n\tThe information submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply to the effect that a Memorandum of Understanding has been signed between the National Water Supply and Drainage Board and the M/s China National Complete Plant Import and Export Corporation Limited (COMPLANT) to carry out a feasibility study in regard to the implementation of the project was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Obtaining blocks of land for the construction of the Ratnapura and Badulla District Labour Office Complexes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8101",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Labour Offices,  the District Labour Offices and the District Factory Inspecting Engineer's Offices functioning under the Department of Labour coming under the purview of the Ratnapura and Badulla zones are housed in rented out buildings. A large number of people visit these offices daily to obtain services from these offices and as such, it has been proposed to construct permanent buildings for these offices to provide the public with adequate facilities as well as the accommodation facilities necessary for the staff.   \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour, Trade Union Relations and Sabaragamuwa Development, to obtain the land required for the establishment of District Labour Office Complexes in Ratnapura and Badulla,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Draft Bill on Sign Language",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8100",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The hearing impaired population living in Sri Lanka is reported to be 389,677.  In terms of the National Policy on Disability, Sign Language has been accepted as the language of communication of the profoundly hearing impaired persons. With the establishment of the Sign Language, as a recognized language it ensures the hearing impaired persons right to education and paves the way for them to have access to  the services provided by the Government without any discrimination.   Affording  equal opportunities in this manner to the hearing impaired persons will enhance their self esteem as well.  \n\n\n\nAccordingly, with the objective of making legal provision to establish the Sign Language as a recognized language in Sri Lanka, the proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment, Welfare and Kandyan Heritage, for drafting the proposed Draft Bill on Sign Language, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "The 10th conference on  the Air Services Negotiations of the  International Civil Aviation Organization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8099",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The annual International Civil Aviation Negotiation Conference (ICAN) organized by the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO), provides the opportunity for the World Air Services to enter into bilateral negotiations for the traffic rights between States.  Arrangements are underway to host the said Conference which is held for the 10th time in Sri Lanka from 04th to 08th of December 2017.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to enter into an Agreement between the International Civil Aviation Organization and the Government of Sri Lanka for hosting the event in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Declaration of the Ritigala - Yan Oya National Park and the declaration of the revised boundary limits of the Horowpothana National Park",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8098",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Ritigala Elephant Transit Home' in Sri Lanka has been established as the second such Home for taking care of the displaced wild elephants and elephant calves covering the North, the North Central and the North Western Provinces of the Island.  The land extent of 427.8 hectares inclusive also of the forest area adjacent to it has been proposed to be declared as Ritigala - Yan Oya National Park. \n\nWith a view to minimizing the human elephant conflict, it has been proposed to revise the boundary limits of the Horowpothana National Park inclusive of the land area adjacent to  the Elephant Retention Centre in Horowpothana established for the capture and keeping them in captivity of the elephants who often trespass the villages and behave aggressively and also to re-declare it as the Horowpothana National Park.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to declare the Ritigala - Yan Oya National Park and the Horowpathana National Park with revised boundary limits, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Construction of Bridges in Rural Areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8097",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has accorded high priority for connectivity improvement within the country with a view to providing the maximum benefits of the National Level Development Project Activities not only to the Urban but to the remote villages as well. Under this activity, it has been planned to construct around 3,500 to 4,000 bridges in rural areas and 02 projects pertaining to the construction of bridges are presently underway with the financial assistance of the United Kingdom and the Netherlands.  \n\n\tIn the mean time, Governments of Hungaria and Belgium have come forward to provide financial assistance for the projects for constructing bridges in the rural areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs,  to authorize the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government to call for proposals for the implementation of the 02 projects for the construction of bridges in rural areas with the financial assistance of the said Governments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Draft Bill on Bio-safety",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8096",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The sustainability of bio-diversity is affected due to the natural causes and the various human activities. It is an accepted fact that the release of genetically modified organisms created through the development of bio-technology to the environment without safety measures is also a kind of human activity which is a threat to bio-diversity.  Adopting safety measures to minimize the imminent damage caused to the bio-diversity in Sri Lanka is a timely need. \n\n\tAs Sri Lanka is a signatory to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety the necessary legislative provision have to be provided by Sri Lanka  for the use of the genetically modified organisms, created using bio-technology, for the  promotion, marketing, utilizing in commercial activities, transport, import, export, re-export, transfer, disposal and release in a manner not causing a risk or causing a minimum risk for the human health and the bio-diversity.  As such, \tthe proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to introduce a new draft Bill on Bio-safety, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Providing relief for Temples situated in areas affected as a result of the drought prevailing in the Island",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8095",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana and the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to grant  relief to the Temples situated in areas affected by floods as well similar to the relief granted to the people affected by the severe drought prevailing in some parts of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Preparation of a Mechanism to manage the declining Price of Pepper",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8094",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet appointed a Cabinet Sub Committee under the Chairmanship of the Minister of Finance and Mass Media on 09-08-2017 to put forward suitable proposals with the objective of safeguarding the livelihood and the income of the persons engaged in pepper cultivation and who are affected as a result of the declining price of pepper in the international market and as well as in the local market.   \n\nAccordingly, as recommended by the Cabinet Sub-Committee, the proposal made by Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Primary Industries, to maintain a certified price of Rs.900 per kg of dry pepper, to formulate a relief mechanism by the Government, taking into consideration the difference of the proposed certified price and the prevalent market price, to pay an amount subject to a  maximum of Rs.150 per kg and to continue with the relief programme until such time that the market price of a kilogram of dry pepper exceeds Rs.900/-, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Amendment to the Municipal Councils Ordinance, Urban Councils Ordinance and the Pradeshiya  Sabha Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8093",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Amendment) Bill incorporating provisions on the new system of electing Members for the local government authorities, was passed in Parliament recently. Concurrently to the above, in determining the number of Members of Local Authorities to be elected, the existing legal provision has to be amended to provide for returning a further additional number of Members not exceeding 40% of the members due to be elected on ward basis, from the list, at divisional level.  \n\nThe proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to amend section 5 of the Municipal Councils Ordinance, section 5 of the Urban Councils Ordinance and section 4 of the Pradeshiya Sabha Act, as amended by the Local Authorities (Special Provisions) Act, No.21 of 2012 providing for same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Completion of the Construction of the City Traffic Building for the Sri Lanka Police",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8092",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction work of the 11 storied city traffic building for the Sri Lanka Police at Mihindu Mawatha in Colombo 12 has been commenced and construction works of 3 storeys had been completed under its first contract.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to award the contract for the completion of the balance construction work to M/s. CML-MTD Construction Ltd., for a sum of Rs.388.5 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Construction of the Nadukuda Grid Substation and augmentation of the \tMannar Grid Substation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8091",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the construction of the Nadukuda Grid Substation and augmentation of the Mannar Grid Substation under the Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme for strengthening the transmission network of the Ceylon Electricity Board, to M/s. Seimens Ltd., India, for a sum of Rs.2,697.96 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Construction of four (04) Grid Substations under the Renewable Energy Absorption Transmission Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8090",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Four (04) Grid Substations and the related transmission lines have been planned to be installed in the areas of Nawalapitiya, Ragala, Wewalwatta and Maliboda to provide interconnections to electricity generated in mini hydro power plants to be amalgamated into the main network in the future. The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for design, civil works, installation of the relevant equipment and commissioning, to M/s. Ceylex Engineering (Pvt) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.1,233 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Construction of the Renal Care Treatment unit at the General Hospital, Trincomalee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8089",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The District of Trincomalee too has been identified as a District in which the Chronic Kidney Diseases unknown aetiology (CKDu) is widely spread. Hence, the Government is pursing action to construct a Renal Care Unit at the General Hospital, Trincomalee with dialysis, wards, clinic and laboratory facilities for the purpose of identifying this Chronic Kidney Disease at the early stage and preventing the deaths occurring due to same. \n\nThe proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the Renal Care Unit to M/s. Electro Metal Pressings (Pvt) Ltd., at the cost of Rs.249.32 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Construction of a building complex for the Stroke Unit at the District \tGeneral Hospital, Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8088",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Stroke is a leading cause for adult disability and it is the forth major cause of deaths in the hospital system. Although stroke can be cured with proper treatment and rehabilitation facilities, apart from the Rehabilitation Hospital at Ragama, no other hospital in the Island is equipped with an advanced Stroke Unit with proper facilities.   \n\nAs such, the government is in the process of constructing a building complex for the development of the stroke unit of the District General Hospital, Polonnaruwa also inclusive of the Neurology, Rheumatology, Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation Units with the objective of improving the treatment facilities necessary for the stroke patients. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the said building complex to M/s. Link Engineering (Pvt) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.348 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Construction of the Cardiothoracic Complex (Phase II) at the Lady Ridgeway Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8087",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The government is in the process of further developing the health care services provided by the Lady Ridgeway Hospital (LRH) which is the main tertiary care institution in Sri Lanka for pediatric treatment.  Therefore, it has been planned to commence the construction work of the Cardiothoracic Complex (Phase II) for providing advanced qualitative Cardiothoracic treatment and for the improvement of  facilities for medical research.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the said treatment unit to M/s. Electro Metal Pressings (Pvt) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.159.94 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Construction of the Renal Care Unit at the General Hospital, Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8086",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The District of Hambantota has been identified as a District in which the Chronic Kidney Diseases unknown aetiology (CKDu) is widely spread. Hence, the Government is pursing action to construct a Renal Care Unit at the General Hospital, Hambantota with dialysis, wards, clinic and laboratory facilities for the purpose of identifying this Chronic Kidney Disease at the early stage and preventing the deaths occurring due to same. \n\nThe proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the Renal Care Unit to M/s. RN Constructions (Pvt) Ltd., at the cost of Rs.210 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Establishment of a Research Unit for the Sri Lanka Anti-Doping Agency",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8085",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Anti-Doping Agency has been established under the provisions of the Convention Against Doping in Sports Act, No.33 of 2013 with the objective of preventing the use of prohibited substances, conducting research in that regard and co\u2011operating with other international organizations operating against prohibited substances.   \n\nPresently, a building is being constructed for this agency in the premises of the Sugathadasa Sports Stadium. The proposal made by Hon. Dayasiri Jayasekara, the Minister of Sports, to construct a laboratory research unit within the premises of the building being constructed for the Sri Lanka Anti-Doping Agency with the objective of minimizing the risk of Sri Lankan Sports men and women being subject to the allegations of using prohibited substances and to provide the equipment needed for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Development of Infrastructure Facilities in Sports",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8084",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of the government is to improve the sports skills of the youth and take them to international level, by paving the way for sports to the village. The government is pursuing action to construct 'Provincial Sports Complexes' to cover all provinces in the country and to construct 'District Sports Complexes' covering the rest of the 16 districts except in the districts where the Provincial Sports Complexes will be established and most of its construction work has already been completed. Moreover, these Provincial Sports Complexes should consist of hostel facilities and the sports men and women residing in the areas away from those Provincial and District Sports Complexes, should be provided with sports infrastructure facilities. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Dayasiri Jayasekara, the Minister of Sports, to construct 08 hostels with accommodation for 100 sports men and women at a time, close to the 08 Provincial Sports Complexes located in Polonnaruwa, Kilinochchi, Kurunegala, Badulla, Digana, Ratnapura, Matara and Trincomalee at the estimated cost of Rs.1,087 million and to construct fully fledged 06 indoor stadiums in the 06 identified areas located away from the Provincial and District Sports Complexes at the estimated cost of Rs.1,050 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Hosting of International Conferences relevant to the field of Agriculture",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8083",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Agriculture has organized to host two International Conferences in Sri Lanka in collaboration with the Asian Productive Organization (APO), African\u2011Asian Rural Development Organization (AARDO) and the Centre for Integrated Rural Development for Asia and Pacific (CIRDAP) of which Sri Lanka is a Member. \n\nWith a view to reviewing policy programmes and plans required for Disaster Risk Management and Climate Change Adaptation and developing sustainable development strategies suitable to face Disaster Risk Management in Agriculture and Climate Change Adaptation, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to conduct a workshop under the theme of 'Disaster Risk Management in Agriculture and Climate Change Adaptation', from 11th to 15th of September 2017 and another International Conference with the objective of gaining knowledge on the safety of major food items found in the global market, new development methods and identifying advanced food safety standards on Strengthening of Food Safety Standards from 31st October to 02nd November in 2017, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "The Government Policy on the usage of Liquid Natural Gas (LNG) for  Electricity Generation and the Construction of required infrastructure for the purpose",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8082",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet appointed a Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on 18.07.2017 under the Chairmanship of Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Special Assignments, to determine the government policy relevant to the infrastructure facilities required for the usage of LNG for Electricity Generation and the Construction of required infrastructure focusing attention on ensuring the energy security of Sri Lanka, diversification of fuel options used for electricity sector and the minimizing of electricity generation cost.  \n\nThe Cabinet granted approval to implement the recommendations made by the said Sub\u2011Committee to accept as a matter of policy for the usage of natural gas as a fuel for generating electricity in Sri Lanka by the year 2019 and to operate the Natural Gas Electricity Plants with the capacity of about 1000MW, and to improve expeditiously the infrastructure facilities for unloading and re\u2011transforming  of LNG."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Implementation of a Middle Income Housing Development Project at Ragama for Government Employees",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8081",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of the Middle Income Housing Development Project implemented by the government is to construct 500,000 houses required by the Middle Income Groups within the next 05 year period.  It has been identified that the majority of the middle income employees belong to the Government and the Semi\u2011government Sector. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement a housing project with 400 housing units by developing a 03 acre land situated in the Ragama area belonging to the Land Reclamation and Development Corporation, with the objective of providing affordable houses to the employees of the Government and the Semi\u2011government Sector under the above project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "Improvement of road infrastructure in the Homagama Region (Tech City)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8080",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The government has focused its attention on the improvement of the Homagama - Pitipana road infrastructure facilities associated with the Tech City Development Plan implemented in accordance with the Western Region Megapolis Master Plan. Under this programme, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, with a view to upgrading the road infrastructure facilities to ensure better connectivity of the transport network, to construct two new roads and to improve three existing roads with a cost estimate of Rs. 3,143 million as given below, was approved by the Cabinet.   \n\n*\tconstruction of a new access road with four lanes of 6.18km in length from Kottawa to Mahenwatta; \n\n*\tconstruction of internal roads of 1.7km in length at the State Universities situated within the Mahenwatta cluster; \n\n*\timprovement of 8.83km in the Pitipana Thalagala Road inclusive of the Dampe - Pitipana Road; \n\n*\timprovement of the Uduwana Pansala Handiya Road with 2.9km in length; and\n\n* \timprovement of access road from Kahathuduwa to Kottawa and up to the Thalagala Junction with 3km in length."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-29-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-08-29",
    "description": "70th Independence Day Celebrations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8079",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to appoint a Ministerial Sub Committee under the Chairmanship of Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to organize and monitor the necessary activities of the 70th Independence Day Celebrations falling on the 04th of February 2018, and the cultural event to coincide with the celebrations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
