    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation to award the tender for the construction of the proposed new extension to the Navigational Services Complex Building at the Bandaranaike International Airport, Katunayake for a sum of Rs.201.39 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Issuance of a certified copy of the judgment or the final decree free of charge  to each party to the case",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8029",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Civil Procedure Code and the Code of Criminal Procedure contain provisions to the effect that a certified copy of the judgment or the final decree can be issued to each party to the case upon payment of a fee.  However, it has been observed that the parties to certain cases do not possess the money necessary to obtain copies of such judgment or final decree. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to amend the Civil Procedure Code and the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, incorporating provisions to enable the issuance of a  certified copy of a judgment or a decree free of charge to each party to the case, for ensuring the dispensation of justice and for the betterment of the judicial system, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Display the Ozone Friendly Tea Logo on Sri Lanka Cricket sportswear",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8028",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Montreal Protocol on Ozone Depleting Substances decided in the year 1992, to limit the consumption of Methyl Bromide or Bromo-Methane hazardous to the ozone layer.  Accordingly, Sri Lanka has been successful in completely eliminating the use of this chemical as a pesticide, particularly in the tea plantation by focusing on alternative technical methods and it has come under international praise.   \n\nAs a mark of this achievement, the Sri Lanka Tea Board has introduced the  'Ozone Friendly Tea Logo' created by it and the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to have a discussion with the relevant institutions to display the logo in the official sportswear of the Sri Lanka Cricket Team, with a view to promoting Sri Lanka as an Ozone friendly tea manufacturing country in the international market, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Management of the price decline in pepper",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8027",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The farmers engaged in pepper cultivation have faced various difficulties due to the decline in the price of pepper in the local and international markets.  Therefore, with the objective of ensuring the security of the livelihood and the revenue of the farmers engaged in pepper cultivation, the Cabinet decided to   appoint a Ministerial Sub\u2011Committee headed by the Hon. Minister of Finance and Mass Media comprising of Hon. Minister of Primary Industries; Disaster Management; Development Strategies and International Trade; Industry and Commerce; and Irrigation and Water Resources Management, as its members to study the matter and submit a Report to the Cabinet without any delay."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Implementation of the Western Region Megapolis Initiative through the respective Project Offices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8026",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Western Region Megapolis planning project office was established in the year 2015 and for the implementation of the projects established under the Megapolis initiative, approval has also been granted to establish 11 project offices until the Western Region Megapolis Authority is established. With the objective of preventing duplication of work by the main project and the project offices, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development to wind up the operations of the Western Region Megapolis planning project and to rename the project offices by their original names as follows, in order to ensure the proper functioning of other project offices, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n* \tWestern Region Aero City Development Project;\n\n* \tWestern Region Maritime City Development Project;\n\n * \tWestern Region Plantation City Development Project;\n\n * \tWestern Region Tourism City Development Project;\n\n* \tWestern Region Tech City Development Project;\n\n* \tWestern Region Administrative City Development Project;\n\n* \tWestern Region Green City Development Project;\n\n* \tWestern Region Transport Development Project;\n\n* \tWestern Region Solid Waste Management Project;\n* \tWestern Region Integrated Community  Development Project; and\n\n* \tWestern Region Planning Project."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Establishment of the Amaradeva Aesthetic and Research Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8025",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The musical influence and the creations of Dr. Pandith Amaradeva who was instrumental in creating a local culture of music unique to the native features based upon the North Indian music, mingling with local folk music can be considered as a national heritage of the country. With a view to preserving that heritage to be experienced and admired by the future generations as well, the Government has proposed to establish the 'Amaradeva Asapuwa' with all essential components and infrastructure related to music. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media to establish the 'Amaradeva Asapuwa' as 'Amaradeva Aesthetic and Research Centre' by an Act of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "New Development Projects in the Health Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8024",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the long term investments carried out in the health sector by the Government of Sri Lanka, health service has achieved improvements in the health outcomes and approximately 100% of preventive health care, 90% - 95% of in-patient care and 40% - 50% of out-patient care are being provided  by the Public Sector. Health indexes are maintained on par with the developed countries and accordingly, the health services in Sri Lanka should be further upgraded with a view to making the population more healthy while also carrying out the health services free of charge uninterruptedly. \n \nAccordingly, the Government has planned to improve the facilitates of the peripheral hospitals in order to minimize the overcrowding of major hospitals while also ensuring the optimal distribution of physical and human resources and for the construction of ward complexes for paediatrics, oncology, surgical, maternal, neonatal and oral health, operating theaters, drug stores and clinics in remote areas enabling easy access for the public to have specialist healthcare. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine to seek funds to initiate and implement several diverse projects which cost around Rs.28,000 million in the year 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Modernization activities of the Sri Lanka Planetarium",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8023",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Planetarium which is one of the largest Planetariums in the world with a 23 meter diameter dome has seating facilities to accommodate 500 visitors per session. This planetarium constructed using the pre-fabricated concrete plates technology has not been subject to modernization during recent times. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to refurbish the dome and the surrounding sections of the Planetarium buildings identified as necessary to be refurbished expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Guidelines to be adopted when resettling the families displaced due to floods and landslides and the plans to be used when constructing houses for such families",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8022",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has initiated a programme for granting houses to the families who were deprived  of their dwelling places due to the floods and landslides that occurred in several Districts including Ratnapura, Kalutara, Galle and Matara due to the adverse weather conditions which affected the Island in May 2017. Under this programme the National Building Research Organization has prepared Guidelines and the Housing Plans to be adopted for the houses under construction for the resettlement of the displaced families. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management to implement the programme for the resettlement of the displaced families due to floods and landslides in accordance with the said Guidelines and the Housing Plans, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Preservation of the Kandyan Heritage",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8021",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The preservation of the ancient historic places subject to destruction located in the Central and Uva Provinces which are the centres of the Kandyan Heritage, the rehabilitation of the small tanks, anicuts and irrigation systems, which had largely contributed to the upcountry economy and for the protection of folk art and Janakala techniques including traditional Kandyan dancing forms, the metal, lacquer and cane industry and the flax plant production, rush and reed handicrafts, is of vital importance. \n\n\tAccordingly, it has been proposed to implement various projects including the implementation of the project for developing the Traditional Kandyan Village, renovation of rural tank and irrigation canals, rehabilitation of ancient historic places and the promotion of art techniques, including the establishment of museums and cultural centres. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment, Welfare and Kandyan Heritage, for the establishment of a Statuary Board by an Act of Parliament  titled the 'Kandyan Heritage Protection Authority' was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Consideration of the operational activities of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport under the Public Private Partnership Framework",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8020",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The accumulated loss of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport as at 31st December 2016 which runs at a loss presently, is US$ 112.9 million (equivalent to Rs.15,600 million). In the circumstances, carrying out the operational activities of this Airport further incurring losses is a substantial financial burden on the Government. As such, with a view to converting the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport into a high revenue deriving Airport under the Public Private Partnership framework, proposals have been invited from Investors dealing with the aviation related ventures.  However, no proposals have yet been received to cover the entire operation of the Airport, Management and Maintenance. In the meantime, a proposal has been submitted by the Government of India to commence a joint venture focusing attention not only on the commercial Air Services of the Mattala International Airport, Aircraft maintenance, repair and overhaul, and flying schools but also in the areas of its operation, management, maintenance and the development.   Accordingly, the proposal made by  Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to appoint a Committee comprising of several senior Secretaries to Ministries to make a further study on the matter, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-08-09",
    "description": "Revision of the fines imposed on traffic offences committed under the Motor Traffic Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8019",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Having identified 7 violations of traffic rules which severely affect the fatal road accidents to a large extent, it was proposed in 2016 to increase the fines imposed on these traffic offences, up to a minimum of Rs.25,000/- with a view to minimizing road accidents.  However, taking into consideration the protest made by the Bus and Three-Wheeler Associations the President appointed an Officials' Committee to inquire into the increasing of fines imposed under the Motor Traffic Act and accordingly, the proposal made by  Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation to implement the following recommendations made by the said Committee, was approved by the Cabinet. \n*\tIncrease of the minimum fine up to Rs.25,000/- in respect of the following traffic offences:\n\n-\tdriving a vehicle without a valid driving license\n\n-\temploying in service persons who do not possess a driving license\n\n-\tdriving vehicles under the influence of liquor or drugs\n\n-\tcrossing a railway line haphazardly\n\n-\tdriving a vehicle without a valid insurance cover\n*\tRevision of the minimum fines presently imposed in respect of the following traffic offences:  \n\n-\thigh speed driving \n\t(imposing a spot fine - of Rs.3,000/- for driving a vehicle at high speed above the 20% limit of the maximum speed stipulated; of Rs.5,000/- for driving a vehicle at high speed above the 20% limit and less than 30% limit of the maximum speed stipulated; of Rs.10,000/- for driving a vehicle at high speed above the 30% limit and less than 50% limit of the maximum speed stipulated; and of Rs. 15,000/-; for driving a vehicle at high speed above the 50% limit) \n \n- \tOvertaking from the left\n\t(the minimum spot fine for this offence is increased up to Rs.2,000/-)\n-\tdriving a motor vehicle carelessly or without due regard to others or without due diligence\n\t(a minimum fine of Rs.10,000/- is imposed for the offence)\n\n\n\n-\tdriving a motor vehicle recklessly or in a dangerous manner or at a dangerous speed \n\t(a minimum fine of Rs. 10,000/- is imposed for the offence)\n\n-\tdriving vehicles by underaged persons\n\t(the minimum fine of Rs. 5,000/- imposed on this offence presently is increased up to Rs. 30,000/-) \n\n- \tthe increase of the minimum fine imposed under the general penalty for any offence for which a punishment has not been specified under the Motor Traffic Act up to Rs.2,500/-.\n\n*\tImposing a spot fine of  Rs. 2,000/- for using a mobile phone while driving.\n\n*\tExpediting of the implementation of a driver score card system.\n\n*\tInstalling of CCTV cameras in the places where many road accidents occur and taking legal action against the offenders based on such information.\n\n*\timplementation of the proposal for the use of electronic facilities for payment of spot fines for traffic offences expeditiously.\n\n*\tproper display of the speed limit sign boards on expressway and highways. \n\n*\timplementation of an integrated timetable and the operation of the SLTB buses and the private buses or to adopt a suitable procedure expeditiously. \n\n*\tEstablishment of institutions to regulate the three-wheelers and the buses and vans transporting school children.\n\n*\tEstablishment of a public transport service ensuring the safety of passengers.\n\n*\tUse of modern technological equipment to minimize the various irregularities caused by some of the officers who enforce the traffic rules and to ensure transparency in the enforcement of traffic laws."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
