    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2017-08-01",
    "description": "Social Values and Psycho-Intellectual Values to be enhanced based on Reconciliation and Equality through Pre-School Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8013",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to enhance the life skills of school children with a view to creating a future generation endowed with social values which would successfully adapt to the social diversity of nationality, religion and gender.  Accordingly,  the joint proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education and Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to introduce a series of lessons with a half an hour session  once a week, including practical activities in order to equip the Pre\u2011School children with personal and social values to enhance their life skills, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-01-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2017-08-01",
    "description": "Expediting the Rehabilitation and Reconstruction work in the areas damaged  by Flood and Landslide",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8012",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the floods and landslides that occurred  in May this year, a number of areas including the districts of Matara, Galle, Kalutara, Ratnapura and Hambantota were severely affected.  In order to completely bring back the daily lives of the people there to normalcy, the reconstruction work and the supply of other amenities will have to be carried out expeditiously.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to autherize the District Secretaries to award the contracts relevant to the reconstruction work which should be done expeditiously, not exceeding Rs.50 million  based on the engineers' estimates and subject to the approval of the Procurement Committees, to the contractors registered in the Construction Industry Development Authority(CIDA), and the relief activities which should be made on medium term and long term to be implemented through the relevant Ministries and Provincial Councils, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
