    "date_str": "2017-07-25",
    "description": "Appointment of a Board of Management for the Maintenance of the Services of the Dr. Neville Fernando Teaching Hospital, Malabe",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7983",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the approval granted by the Cabinet, necessary steps have been taken to vest Dr. Neville Fernando Teaching Hospital with the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine with effect from 2017\u201108\u201101. This State of the Art hospital consisting of modern high tech facilities is expected to be maintained as a teaching hospital which provides a high qualitative patient care service and as such, it has to be established similar to the manner adopted in establishing the Sri Jayawardenapura Hospital, by an Act of Parliament. \n\n\tAccordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to appoint a Board of Management operative from 2017\u201108\u201101 comprising of experts who represent the medical, administrative, managerial and civil society under the chairmanship of  Dr. U.A. Ajith Mendis, the former Director General of Health Services for the administration and management of the services of the hospital until the hospital is established by an Act of Parliament, and to provide a sum of Rs.200 million per month for the operational cost of the hospital by managing the funds allocated to the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine for the year 2017, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-25-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-07-25",
    "description": "Procurement of the required medical equipment for treating Dengue patients and taking expeditious action for controlling the Dengue Outbreak",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7982",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval to procure some essential medical and laboratory equipment  expeditiously, treating it as an emergency procurement to provide efficient intensive care treatment to Dengue patients, taking into consideration the Memorandum submitted by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, and also the Memorandum submitted by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine on the measures to be taken to control the Dengue epidemic.  Accordingly, it was decided to procure  the equipment expeditiously which can be purchased locally, to take necessary action to purchase the rest of the equipment via the Sri Lankan Diplomatic Missions abroad and to allocate a provision of Rs.300 million to the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine for the purpose. \n\nIn addition, it was decided to grant approval to take the following action to prevent the further spreading of Dengue. \n\ni.\tStrictly enforce the circular instructions issued by the Secretary to the President to the effect that the Heads of Departments are accountable for maintaining Dengue free office premises.  \n\nii.\tThe Ministry of Education to carry out the Dengue prevention  programmes in schools with the participation of parents and students. \n\niii.\tThe Western Provincial Council has employed field officers to carry on house to house supervision in order to identify the breeding places of the Dengue mosquito and the same methodology to be followed by the other Provincial Councils. \n\niv.\tThe Ministry of Finance and Mass Media, to produce and broadcast suitable short video programmes/audio programmes to make the general public aware of the importance of preventing Dengue. \n\nv.\tProvide training to 2,000 Sri Lanka Army personnel with the assistance of the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine to  make available the required care and services to the Dengue patients. \n\nvi.\tImplement Dengue Prevention Programmes in the respective areas in collaboration with the Medical Officers of Health (MOH), Local Authority Institutions, Divisional Secretariats and Police Stations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-25-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-07-25",
    "description": "Concession Agreement of the Port of Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7981",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka is expected to enter into a Concession Agreement with the China Merchant Ports Holdings Company Limited (CMPort), with a view to making the operational activities of the Port of Hambantota commercially viable under a Public-Private Partnership. The Agreement submitted previously in this regard to the Cabinet has been reformulated to be more favourable to the country, in consultation with all the relevant stakeholders. According to the new proposed Concession Agreement, 02 companies due to be established in which the state partner will be the Government of Sri Lanka (Sri Lanka Ports Authority) and the relevant investor company will be the private partner. \n\n*\tHambantota International Port Services Co. (Pvt.) Ltd. (HIPS); \n\n\twill be established for the management of the services and common user facilities of the Port of Hambantota and its capital will be US$ 606 million. The Sri Lanka Ports Authority will own 50.7% of the shares of the Company and the remainder of 49.3% will be owned by the CMPort Company.\n\n*\tHambantota International Port Group (Pvt.) Ltd. (HIPG);\n\n\tthe Company to be established for the management of operational assets of the Port, further development activities, its infrastructure facilities and commercialization of cargo handling and other operations, with US$ 794 million of its capital, the Sri Lanka Ports Authority will own 15% of the share capital and 85% by the CMPort Company, identical to the share split  of the SAGT terminal and CICT terminal of the Port of Colombo.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the ownership of shares of the entire investment will be amended as 69.55% to the CMPort Company and 30.45% to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority, as against the share split of 80:20 as proposed in the previous Agreement.  \n\n\tThe freehold right of the Port of Hambantota and the lands thereunder will not be transferred to the investor Company at any time and those lands will be granted to the 02 Companies to be established in partnership with the Government of Sri Lanka, on lease basis under the proposed Agreement. The Sri Lanka Ports Authority will be entitled to purchase the shares of the said two Companies as follows; \n\n*\tAfter 70 years of the date of enforcement of the Agreement;  \n\n\tthe Sri Lanka Ports Authority will be entitled to purchase the shares held by the CMPort and its affiliates and partners in both companies HIPS and HIPG Companies, at a reasonable value to be determined by the Government Valuer or an independent valuer. \n\n*\tAfter 80 years of the date of enforcement of the Agreement;   \n\n\tthe Sri Lanka Ports Authority will be entitled to purchase the shares held by the CMPort, its affiliates and partners in both companies at a cost of US$ 01 and the Sri Lanka Ports Authority will own 60% of the shares of the HIPG Company and 76.8% of the shares of the HIPS Company. \n\n*\tAfter 99 years of the date of enforcement of the Agreement; \n\n\tall shares held by the CMPort, its affiliates and partners in both companies HIPG and HIPS will be transferred to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority by the CMPort  at a cost of US$ 01.  \n\n\tMoreover, the provisions have been incorporated in the proposed agreement  for preventing the  utilization of the Port of Hambantota for military activities and the sole responsibility and the authority of the security of the Port will be with the Government of Sri Lanka.  \n\n\tAccordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, the Cabinet granted approval to further seek the views of the parties interested in the proposed concession Agreement, to present the Agreement in Parliament and make amendments where necessary, in accordance with the proposals if any, made therein, thereafter to accept it and sign the same."
  },
