    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, the Cabinet decided to grant approval as a matter of National Policy, to empower District Secretaries to secure the support of Divisional Secretaries, other officers attached to other Ministries serving in those offices and other relevant institutions to implement all relief measures more efficiently and effectively including rescue operations for saving the victims of sudden disasters and providing expeditious relief and to incur the required expenditure to carry out the essential activities efficiently and independently."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-11-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-07-11",
    "description": "Payment of compensation for persons deceased due to the  landslide that occurred at the  Meethotamulla Solid Waste Dump",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7909",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the landslide that occurred at the Meethotamulla Solid Waste Dump 1,670 persons of 393 families were displaced while 60 houses were totally destroyed and 27 houses were partially damaged.  The number of  risk prone houses identified are 201 and 33 persons died as a result of this incident.  In accordance with the decision taken at the Cabinet meeting held on 25th April 2017, the following measures have already been taken to provide relief: \n\n*\tout of these families who were victims of the disaster, provision of houses constructed by the Urban Development Authority, for the families who have expressed their consent to be the recipients  of such houses;  \n \t\n* \tprovision of the assessed value of the house for the families who declined to accept the houses;\n\n\n*\tprovision of Rs. 250,000/-\tfor the purchase of household appliances for the owners of the damaged houses;\n\n*\tprovision of Rs.50,000/- per month for a period of 03 months for the families who were evacuated from the risk prone areas;\n\n*\tprovision of Rs.10,000/- as a transport allowance for the families who are moving to live in permanent houses.\n\nIn addition to these reliefs, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to grant Rs.1 million as compensation per deceased person inclusive of the Rs.100,000 granted under the National Disaster Insurance Programme with the Rs.900,000 provided by the General Treasury, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-11-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-07-11",
    "description": "Acquisition of Government vehicles on Operating Lease Basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7908",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Police needs 1,050 vehicles constituting of 800 Motor Cycles and 250 Land cruisers for its use.  According to the existing market prices a sum of Rs.4.5 billion is required for the purpose.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to obtain these vehicles under the operating lease basis instead of the general financing lease basis, taking into consideration the benefit of reducing the risk to be borne by the state and the advantage of the significant reduction in the loan amount to the government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-11-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-07-11",
    "description": "Introduction of a loan scheme for young graduates for business  initiatives",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7907",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the Budget 2016, it was proposed to provide loan facilities to young graduates subject to a maximum of Rs.1.5 million with a view to encouraging their participation in the economic development process of the country.  The  Bank of Ceylon and the People's Bank have expressed their willingnes to participate in the implementation of this loan scheme. In this regard, applications have been called through paper advertisements and 80 such applications have been received.   Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, for the Bank of Ceylon and the People's Bank to award the loan funds necessary for the implementation of 40 business projects recommended by the Sectoral Evaluation Committee comprising of experts relating to the relevant fields which evaluated the said business projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-11-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-07-11",
    "description": "The study on supply of potable water to the population in Jaffna Peninsula through the development of water resources in the Vadamarachchi Lagoon",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7906",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although, the National Water Supply and the Drainage Board has implemented 16 various water supply projects in the Jaffna Peninsula, it has been able to provide pipe borne water facilities only to a fraction of 9% out of a total population of 600,000 living in the area.  The scarcity of  potable water resources is the major obstacle for the implementation of drinking water projects in Jaffna.  As a remedial measure, it has already been decided to establish a Desalination Water Plant to purify sea water and provide drinking water.  \n\nIn addition, it has been proposed to store the rain water from the rains that occur from the period of October to December of the year in an area of 10 km of the Vadamarachchi lagoon and to implement a potable water supply project out of the water so collected.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs to make a comprehensive feasibility study on this, taking into consideration the data and information collected pertaining to the research already carried out in this regard, with the collaboration of the related Government institutions as well as the Northern Provincial Council, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-11-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-07-11",
    "description": "Proper Management of the use of polythene to minimize environmental issues caused by polythene",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7905",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 06th September 2016 granted approval to appoint a Committee of Experts to prepare a national policy and action plan with a view to managing properly the use of polythene and plastic in order to minimize the environmental issues caused by polythene and plastic. The proposal made by H.E. the President, Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the following short term, middle term and long term activities included in the action plan prepared by the said Committee of Experts so appointed, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\nShort Term Measures: \n\n*\tto ban the use of polythene for decorative purposes of all ceremonies pertaining to national, religious, social and political;\n\n*\tto enforce further the present regulations made for banning the use, sale and production of polythene equal to or less than 20 micron in thickness;\n                          \n*\tto permit the use of polythene of less than 20 micron for essential purposes only with the approval of the Central Environmental Authority;\n\n*\tto ban the import, production and sale of polythene used for domestic use and wrapping food (lunch sheets);\n\n* \tto ban the import, production, sale and use of food storage containers, plastic plates, cups and spoons manufactured using polystyrene as raw material;\n\n*\tto ban the sale of processed and cooked foodstuffs in bags made of  polythene;\n\n*\tto provide environmental friendly biodegradable bags such as paper, pan or cloth bags as alternatives to polythene bags given to customers when purchasing items and to promote the use of degradable plastic material in the production of such bags;\n\n*\tto ban the burning of polythene and plastics in open spaces or premises;\n\n*\tto introduce and promote biodegradable plastic raw material.\n\n\n\nMiddle Term Measures:\n\n*\tto grant tax relief and VAT exemption for the importation of machineries required for productions using biodegradable plastic raw material;\n\n*\tto impose a CESS of 15% upon the import of plastic raw material and plastic products.\n\nLong Term Measures:\n\n*\tto completely ban the importation of recycled plastic raw material."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-11-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-07-11",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Mechanism for minimizing the Green House Gas emission in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7904",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka, being a party to the 21st conference of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change held in the year 2015 in Paris, is bound to keep Green House emission at a minimum level.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President, Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to name the Ministry of Mahaweli Development and Environment as the national focal point for the approval of the related projects and for the successful implementation of the Nationally Appropriate Mitigation Activities (NAMA) on minimizing the Green House Gas emission, to establish the relevant coordinating unit at the Climate Change Secretariat of the said Ministry and to establish the implementing mechanism and the institutional framework needed for the successful implementation of the projects in Sri Lanka, approved by the above Coordinating Unit, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
