    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "The Early Childhood Development Standards to be declared as 'National Standards for Early Childhood Development'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7859",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The child, during the period of 3 to 5 years of age while getting accustomed   to the formal pre-school life and in association with the  pre\u2011school prepares for receiving the fundamentals of education.  Presently, as the pre\u2011school teachers design their activity plans according to various subject matters, it has become essential to introduce correct standards. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to declare the Early Childhood Development Standards as 'National Standards for Early Childhood Development' compiled by the Children's Secretariat and reviewed by a Committee which comprised of the relevant Ministries and the representatives of all Provincial Councils and to activate such standards with the collaboration of the Provincial Councils, Local Government Institutions and the District and Divisional Secretariats, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-06-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "Initiation of a Scientific Collaboration with the Yunnan Academy of Agricultural Sciences and the Yunnan Sugarcane Research Institute of Yunnan Province of China with Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7858",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to enter into Agreements for the development of sugarcane research and exchange of sugarcane genetic material with the Yunnan Academy of Agricultural Sciences in the Province of Yunan, situated in Kunmin of the People's Republic of China and the Sugarcane Research Institute of Sri Lanka with regard to the exchange of sugarcane germplasm and utility, evaluation of germplasm, exchange knowledge pertaining to sugarcane cultivation, exchange of information and expertise knowledge, training of young scientists, carrying out a study on subjects of mutual benefit and importance to the two countries and the settlement of common issues with a view to promoting collaboration between Sri Lanka and China, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-06-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "Allocation of  lands required by the Thai Lanka Aqua (Private) Company for Pacific White Marine Shrimp Farming",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7857",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Tiger Shrimp farming is undertaken over an extent of around 10,000 acres of land making the Puttalam District as the centre of Sri Lanka and the annual total production is around 6030 MT.  Out of this production about 2500 MT are exported deriving an annual revenue of US$ 16 million. Due to being subject to the white spot disease resulting in the lack of export quality standards the industry has turned out to be an under\u2011performing activity and as such, it has been proposed to introduce White Shrimp Farming for a rapid increase of Marine Shrimp to the country which shows resistance to white spot disease and as there is a high demand for same in the Global Market. The project proposal submitted by the Thai Lanka Aqua (Private) Ltd. to implement a White Pacific Shrimp Farming Project alongside the proposed Aquaculture Industrial Park in the Manthai - West Divisional Secretariat Division of the Mannar District has been recommended by the Project Committee of the  Ministry of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to give over a land of 250 acres to the Thai Lanka Aqua (Private) Ltd. close to the land identified to develop as an Aqua Industrial Park in the  Manthai - West Divisional Secretariat Division, on lease basis, for a period of 30 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-06-27-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "Development of the Kottawa-Pinhena road, as the main access Road leading to the Homagama-Pitipana Technological City",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7856",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The technological city under the Megapolis Development Plan is to be built to cover the areas of Malabe, Kottawa, Homagama, Athurugiriya and Kaduwela.  Accordingly, 200 acres of land situated at Pitipana, Homagama has been set a part for the establishment of the Information Technology and other Technological Faculties affiliated to State Sector Universities. Concurrent to the development activities, widening and development of the access road network for providing convenient access to the new zone has been identified as an urgent need. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to develop the Kottawa - Pinhena Road coming under the purview of the Road Development Authority and identified as a road to be developed expeditiously, utilizing the funds set a part for the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-06-27-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "Implementation of development projects by the Urban Development Authority (UDA) with the Treasury funds",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7855",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Urban Development Authority has planned to implement 6 major development projects utilizing the funds set a part to the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development by the Budget 2017, under the 6 major projects. In this respect, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement under 3 major projects, exceeding a sum of Rs.20 million, under which 39 sub projects namely, 13 projects under the project component of the Urban Development Authority, 16 projects under the Provincial Urban Development Projects and 10 projects for the Township Development and  Urbanized Waste Management with the Treasury Funds, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
