    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "Allocation of a land to the Sri Lanka Police for the establishment of the Galewela Police Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7854",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to vest a portion of land in extent of 1\u00bd Acres from the land of about 24 Acres situated in the Galewela Town, acquired by the Urban Development Authority under the Greater Dambulla Development Plan, with the Sri Lanka Police for the construction of the Galewela Police Station, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-06-27-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "Presenting the Government Revenue Report of the first quarter 2017 in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7853",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government revenue of the first quarter of 2017 is Rs.436 billion and of which 95% amounting to Rs.415 billion is the tax revenue collected. The revenue collection of the first quarter is 22% of the annual estimate and 94% of the target of the first quarter. Tax collection from the Value Added Tax and the Nation Building Tax has exceeded the expected targets. However, the targeted revenue has not been achieved from the Income Tax and the Excise Tax.  The attention has been drawn especially, on the low progress from Excise Tax liquor and cigarettes. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to table the report pertaining to the above fact and the summary of Government revenue at the end of each month of the first quarter and the end of the quarter of 2017, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-06-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-06-27",
    "description": "Obtaining the contribution of Local Government Institutions for minimizing  disaster risk and making disaster response",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7852",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The disaster management policy has recognized that the local government institutions has a significant role to play in the minimization of the risk of facing disaster situations. The approval of the local government institutions has to be obtained for  all development activity planning and the National Disaster Management Policy has made provision to enact by-laws to enable the inclusion of methods for the minimization of disaster risk in the development projects implemented within their local government area of authority. As such, when preparing development plans in the disaster prone areas and carrying out constructions, following the guidelines on the specifications of buildings is really important. \n\n\tSince, the Provincial Councils are vested with the authority of governing and monitoring the local government institutions, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to assist the Chief Ministers of Provincial Councils in the Development of a disaster management plan in respect of their areas of authority in accordance with the guidelines provided for in the Disaster Management Act., and to get the support of the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government related to coordination, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
