    "date_str": "2017-04-04",
    "description": "Procurement for the Supply of Anesthetic Machines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7654",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-04-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- When providing a high standard health care service to patients in the Government hospitals anesthetic machines are of great importance and as such,  the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the supply,  installation and commissioning of 137 Anesthetic Machines with Ventilators to M/s Meditechnology Holdings (Pvt.) Ltd. at a cost of US$ 1.3 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-04-04-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-04-04",
    "description": "Construction of a Specialized Paediatric Unit in the Teaching Hospital, Karapitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7653",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-04-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Teaching Hospital at Karapitiya in Galle,  is the third largest tertiary care hospital in Sri Lanka.   There are 60 wards and 1,900 beds in the hospital out of which only 250 beds have been allocated for the child patients. To meet the requirements, it is necessary to develop the Paediatric Neuro\u2011Intensive Care Unit, Paediatric Intensive Care Unit and the Paediatric Surgical Unit of this hospital.  As such, it has been decided to construct a building complex to establish a State of the Art Child Care Unit in the Karapitiya Teaching Hospital with all necessary facilities and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the building complex, to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau and the Engineering Services (Pvt) Ltd. subject to the recommendations of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-04-04-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-04-04",
    "description": "Revision of the Total Cost Estimate of Ruhunupura Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7652",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-04-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is proposed to revise the cost estimate of Rs.8,653.54 million of the Ruhunupura Water Supply Project to Rs.10,029.64 million, for reasons beyond the control of the contractor.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to revise the contract sum concerned in accordance with the Agreement reached after consultation with the Secretary to the Treasury and to proceed with the implementation of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
