    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Budget Proposals of 2017 have made provision for the 12 proposed  concessionary loan schemes in several fields inclusive of providing concessions to the farmers dealing with small scale subsistence agriculture and the companies engaged in commercial level agriculture and to fulfil the housing needs of the low income groups. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to implement these loan schemes through the State and Private Sector Banks in the following manner, to be covered under 8 schemes, taking into consideration the executional convenience, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\n\n\n\nLoan Scheme \nBeneficiary Group \nProposed Loan Amount (Rs.)\n\n\n\n'Ran Aswenna' \nFarmers, farmer organizations, agro processing establishments, rice mill owners, poultry farmers, ornamental fish farmers and floriculture farmers\n750 million\n\n\n'Govi Navoda'\nSmall scale farmers and farmer organizations\n500,000/-\n\n\n'Diri Sawiya'\nPersons engaged in the field of poultry sector\n75 million/td>\n\n\n'Jaya Isura'\nAgriculture, fisheries, livestock, floriculture, horticulture, light engineering, printing, tourism, information technology sector, manufacturing industry, small and medium scale entrepreneurs engaged in handicrafts and garments\nupto 400 million\n\n\n'Riya Shakthi'\nPersons engaged in the transport of School children\n04 million\n\n\n'Sonduru Piyasa'\nSonduru Piyasa Low income group unable to build their houses on their own\n200,000/-\n\n\n'Mehesara'\nRegistered media personnel\nupto 300,000/-\n\n\n'Rivi Bala Savi'\nGeneral public who purchase solar panel system for their households\n350,000/-"
  },
