    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Development Bank has agreed to provide funds for the rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance of around 4,000 km. of roads in the North, East, Uva and Western Provinces.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to carry out the remaining activities pertaining to the implementation of Programme - 2 of the proposed Integrated Road Investment Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-24-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-01-24",
    "description": "Provision of the land ownership and suitable houses to the beneficiaries of the Hautiville Housing project under the concept of creating New Villages in the Estate Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7424",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hautiville Housing project in the Nuwara Eliya District has been initiated under the concept of creating New Villages, with a view to providing a better living condition to the Plantation Community.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. U. Palani Digambaram, the Minister of Hill Country New Villages, Infrastructure and Community Development, to issue Title Deeds to 71 of the beneficiaries of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-24-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-01-24",
    "description": "Importation of quality seeds for enhancing the productivity of Local Big Onion production",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7423",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, 65% to 70% of the local big onion seed requirement needed for the consumption in the country is imported annually. Therefore, priority has been accorded to enhance the production of big onion under the Food Production National Programme 2016-2018 and to achieve the purpose, high yielding seed varieties have to be introduced to enhance the yield per unit of land.  Although, the annual requirement of big onion in the country is approximately 40,000 kg., only a half of it is produced locally. The balance is imported by the private sector of which some draw backs have been reported with regard to the quality of such imported big onions.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to import 6,200 kg. of high quality seeds from the 'National Horticultural Research and Development Foundation' which is a Research Institution of the Indian Government and fulfil the local need of the big onions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-24-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-01-24",
    "description": "Implementation of the Sustainable Fisheries Development Project in the Northern Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7422",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is a special and a priority need of the government to develop the infrastructure facilities in the Northern Province where the development activities were held up for a long time due to the conflict which prevailed over there. The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has agreed to provide funds for the purpose and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to implement the 'Northern Province Sustainable Fisheries Development Project', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-24-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-01-24",
    "description": "Implementation of the e-friends Project II of the Revolving Fund Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7421",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, for the implementation of the e-Friends II Revolving Fund utilizing the remaining funds out of the sum debited to the Revolving Fund under the Environmentally Friendly Project II Loan Scheme implemented from the year 2004 up to the year 2010 under the financial assistance provided by the Japanese International Cooperation Agency (JICA) and the provision of Rs.1,300 Million, set a part by the General Treasury for the year 2017 for this purpose, for waste minimization, for energy saving and for assisting the industrialists in the environment pollution control and also for formulating a suitable mechanism to ensure that the most suitable beneficiaries identified are provided with loans to achieve the objectives of this loan scheme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-24-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-01-24",
    "description": "Transfer of the Railways Department Stores at Matale to the Municipal Council, Matale, on Lease Basis for constructing a Public Market",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7420",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to transfer the Stores of the Railways Department at Matale to the Municipal Council, Matale, on lease basis for constructing a public market, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-24-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-01-24",
    "description": "Construction of Luxury Tourist Camp Sites adjoining the Yala National Park",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7419",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the year 2012, an extent of 07 Acres from the land belonging to the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority (SLTDA) situated in the Palatupana area adjoining the Yala National Park had been allotted to M/s Wild Coast Lodge (Pvt.) Ltd., to construct environmental friendly luxury tourist camp sites, with a view to attracting the tourists of the higher income group. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to give an additional 155 perches of land on lease basis for a period of 50 years, to the above company, in order to carry on the project successfully as planned earlier, to obtain the approval of the  Department of Coast Conservation and Coastal Resource Management, the recommendation of the Department of Wildlife Conservation and also to direct the company to carry out its activities following the recommendations of the other government institutions as well, when the relevant constructions are underway, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-24-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-01-24",
    "description": "Procurement of Equipment necessary for the Sri Lanka Army Contingent Deployed for Peace Keeping Operations in Mali",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7418",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka has made a commitment to the United Nations to deploy a contingent of Sri Lanka Army for peace keeping operations in Mali. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into a Loan Agreement with a Bank of Russia known as SBERBANK, to procure the items and equipment necessary for the Sri Lanka Army Contingent, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Hosting the International Forum of the Independent Audit Regulators (IFIAR) Annual Workshop",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7417",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Independent Audit Regulators in the World over have formed the International Forum of the Independent Audit Regulators to discuss and share information relating to oversight of Audits by its members. Sri Lanka Accounting and Auditing Standards Monitoring Board has been working as a member of the forum since the year 2007 and it has participated actively in its discussions.  The IFIAR conducts a workshop  every year, attended by the staff of its member organizations and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to host its Annual Workshop for the year 2018, in the month of February in Colombo, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "National Human Rights Action Plan (2017-2021)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7416",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval last year, for the establishment of an Inter Ministerial Committee for Human Rights with the Co-chairmanship comprising of the Ministers of Foreign Affairs; Skills Development and Vocational Training; Justice and Strategic Development and International Trade, for the preparation of 'National Human Rights Action Plan 2017-2021' and to study all facts which should be taken for consideration.  The Cabinet approved, the 'Five Year National Human Rights Action Plan (2017-2021)', crafted with the consultations of the said Inter Ministerial Committee and wide participation of the relevant Stakeholders, presented by Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva, the Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Awarding the Contract for the Design and Building of St. Sebestian North Lock Gates and Pumping Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7415",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the contract for the Design and Building of St. Sebestian North Lock Gates and Pumping Station implemented under the Metro Colombo Urban Development Project financed by the World Bank Loan for controlling floods in the Colombo City, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Construction of a Pre-fabricated Structured Building for Storing Medical Supplies in the Medical Supplies Division at Welisara Hospital Premises",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7414",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- As the storing facilities available in the Medical Supplies Division of the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine are inadequate, a sum of nearly Rs.1 Million per month is incurred as rent for the storage facilities to be obtained from the private sector.  Therefore, considering the long term storage facilities needed, a pre-fabricated structured building has been planned to be constructed at the Welisara Hospital Premises, to ensure uninterrupted medical supplies to the hospital.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senarathe, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the stores building, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Awarding of the Contracts for buildings to be constructed at the University of the Visual & Performing Arts and the Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7413",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the contracts pertaining to the construction of  a building and landscaping for the Faculty of Visual Arts at the University of Visual & Performing Arts and the contract for the construction of academic and administration buildings for the Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education located in areas in Galle, Gampaha, Kandy, Kurunegla and Samanthurei, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Memoranda of Understanding between Sri Lanka and Ukraine and Denmark on the Recognition of Certificates issued to seafarers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7412",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- For a seafarer with a certificate of competency, to serve on ships registered in a foreign country, flying its flag has to obtain a similar certificate of recognition from the country concerned, in addition to his certificate of competency.  For the issuance of such certificates of equal status, their should be a Convention or a Memorandum of Understanding between the relevant countries and Sri Lanka has already entered into such Agreements with 30 foreign countries. Entering into such Agreements, generate job opportunities for a large number of Sri Lankan Seafarers who have obtained the Certificates of Competency to serve in foreign vessels. The Governments of Ukraine and Denmark have expressed their willingness to enter into an Agreement  with Sri Lanka relating to the issue of these certificates and therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to enter into Memoranda of Understanding between the Governments of Ukraine and Denmark relating to the recognition of the Oceanic Certificates of Competency, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Regulations made under the Merchant Shipping Act, No. 52 of 1971 to regularize Small Commercial Vessels",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7411",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, there is a great interest in Sri Lanka, over the activities carried out by the small commercial vessels. At the same time, with the development of the tourism industry, there is a significant increase in the passenger transportation by ships and as well as in the tourism activities.    As such, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to make regulations for the regularization of small merchant vessels under the Merchant Shipping Act, No. 52 of 1971, with a view to formalizing the registration and regularization of these small merchant vessels, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Providing relief to persons adversely affected due to the acquisition of land for the Yan Oya Reservoir Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7410",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- By now, 85% of the construction work of the Yan Oya Reservoir Development Project connecting the Anuradhapura and the Trincomalee Districts has been completed.  Around 242 families to be affected due to the impact of the project have to be evacuated from their places of residence expeditiously before commencement of filling the reservoir with water. As such, taking into consideration, the need to provide the families affected with more conducive living facilities, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management, to provide the above families with relief measures such as granting them financial aid to facilitate them to construct houses with the basic needs resembling their present houses, deviating from the existing provision, paying compensation on a suitable methodology to the encroaches who have developed and are in possession of government lands earmarked to be acquired, awarding compensation for crop damage, for those who could not continue with their seasonal cultivation as a result of the implementation of the project and  evacuating them from their places of residence expeditiously and complete the work of the project within the scheduled time frame, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Prohibition of trawl fishing operation using mechanized boats within Sri Lankan waters",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7409",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to present the Draft Bill for the amendment of the Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Act, No. 2 of 1996 in Parliament, making the necessary provisions for the prohibition of trawl fishing operation using engine mounted boats or mechanized boats within Sri Lankan waters, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Economic Empowerment of Women through Apparel Based Mini Factories",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7408",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted approval to provide training for rural women from the Eastern and the Uva Provinces and from the selected districts prioritizing women of displaced families and those who had become widowers as a result of war in sewing under the 'Programme for Economic Empowerment of Rural Women', anticipated to be implemented by the Ministry of Industry and Commerce, and subsequently to establish 150 mini apparel factories. Taking into consideration the great demand in respect of this project, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to expand the number of direct beneficiaries per mini factory from 15 to 20 and to install 5 more additional machines in each factory and to vest the ownership of the sewing machines to the respective cooperative societies that provided the training to the beneficiaries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Construction of Quarters/Housing facilities for the Medical Officers,  and the rest of the Health Services Staff in all Government Hospitals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7407",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Budget proposals of 2016, a proposal has been made to provide the basic accommodation requirements of Doctors and other medical staff serving in rural areas through Public Private Partnership Project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senarathe, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to construct government quarters for the Medical Specialists, the Medical Officers and the Internship Medical Officers and the other Health Services as well, through the Public Private Partnership Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Seeking the consent of drivers to donate organs and tissues for transplantation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7406",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the advancement of medical science, it is becoming prevalent to successfully transplant an organ of a healthy person who voluntarily donates such organ to be transplanted in place of the damaged organ of another person.  Organs can be donated by persons who are living, by those who have had a brain death or circulatory death, in case the person has given his/her consent prior to death. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senarathe, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to amend the application form when applying for a driving license and renewing it with the inclusion of a statement indicating the consent of the bearer who suffers a brain death or a circulatory death as a result of a road traffic accident, enabling the drivers to donate their organs and tissues, to be transplanted for the benefit of the needy patients and to amend the present driving license so as to display such consent given, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Management of the Water Supply Facilities during the Drought situation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7405",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The drought situation prevailing in the Island, at present, has caused and adverse effect on the small community water systems in the rural areas. Due to the dry climatic conditions, the water supply capacity of the small water supply sources have been reduced with an anticipated  increase in the demand for water. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to expand the water supply activities carried out by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board by deploying water bowsers, to construct 400 hand pump wells and to repair and rehabilitate the existing 1,000 public hand-pump fitted in deep wells located within the drought prone rural areas, to construct 200 hand pump wells in the remote villages and to create awareness among the public of the need to water economically and to facilitate coordination activities with the relevant authorities and the institutions for the purpose of taking expeditious action at instances when the water supply is suddenly hampered, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Implementation  of the National Human Resources and Employment Policy (NHREP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7404",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations, for the implementation of the updated National Human Resources and Employment Policy designed, taking into consideration, the views of all stakeholders and paying more emphasis on private sector participation, to achieve a higher rate of economic growth under the economic development plan of the present government and to generate more employment opportunities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Upgrading the quality of service of the passenger transportation in the three-wheelers and the student transportation in the school vans",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7403",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Budget proposals of 2017, a proposal has been made to establish a Regulatory Authority to upgrade the quality of service of the passenger transportation in the three-wheelers and the student transportation in the school vans.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to appoint a Committee comprising of the Ministry Secretaries, to study and propose a methodology for implementation of the proposal and submit a Report to the Cabinet, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Taking over of the Land leased to the US Embassy at Iranawila",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7402",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- A block of land at Iranawila situated in the Puttalam District, in extent of 166.038 Hectares had been leased out to the Embassy of the United States in 1991, to establish a radio transmission station 'the Voice of America' in Sri Lanka.  The US Embassy has informed its intention to close down the radio transmission station and handover the land and other assets/properties back to the Government of Sri Lanka before the expiry of the lease period. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, for the government to terminate the relevant Lease Agreement and take over the land and other assets/properties found in the premises, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Implementation of an Integrated Municipal Solid Waste Management System  for the Kandy District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7401",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- Around 250 Metric Tons of waste is collected within the Municipal Council authority area of the Kandy District and also in other Local authority areas daily and as such a need has arisen for the disposal of such solid waste adopting an environmentally sound integrated mechanism. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement a Waste Management Programme for the Kandy District through a joint venture Company formed between the Municipal Council Kandy and a Private Investor selected through open proposal procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-17-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-01-17",
    "description": "Amendment of the Firearms Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7400",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that amendment of the Firearms Ordinance No.33 of 1916 is a timely need to formalise the usage of firearms to preserve law and order in the country, in the issuance and usage of firearms for the protection of agricultural crops and other property and in prohibiting the usage of firearms in public places.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to instruct the Legal Draftsman, to draft the amending legislation necessary in accordance with the recommendations made by the Officials' Committee appointed in this respect to make a study and report, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Policy and Legal Framework relating to the Counter Terrorism Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7399",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to refer the Amended Policy and Legal Framework relating to the Counter Terrorism Act to the Parliamentary Sectoral Oversight Committee on Legal Affairs, including the provisions to be incorporated into a new law to make provision for the protection of Sri Lanka's National Security and the Security of it's people from acts of terrorism and related attacks, the protection of the unity, territorial integrity and the sovereignty of Sri Lanka from acts of terrorism and related attacks, the protection of other countries and areas from the scourge of terrorism, the prevention of the use of Sri Lankan territory and its people for the preparation of terrorism in overseas, the prevention and detection of acts of terrorism and related offences, the identification of acts related to terrorism and the related offences, the identification of person who have committed acts of terrorism which would affect the national security and the security of the people of Sri Lanka, arrests, detention, investigations, prosecution and punishment and to commence drafting of Legislation in accordance with the said Framework, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Amendment of the Code of Criminal Procedure (Special Provisions) Act, No.2 of 2013",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7398",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Bill was drafted in August 2016, with a view to providing for a suspect arrested by the Police, the right of access to a lawyer immediately after recording his statement, but taking into consideration the representations made by certain parties interested on the matter, the Draft Bill was not tabled in Parliament. Subsequently, a Committee was appointed comprising the representatives of the Sri Lanka Bar Association, the Attorney General's Department and other Stakeholders to evolve a more acceptable draft on the subject as recommended by the Parliamentary Sectoral Oversight Committee on Legal Affairs (Anti Corruption).  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to instruct the Legal Draftsman, to draft necessary Legislation, based on the draft prepared by the said Committee which has made provision to ensure the rights of a suspect arrested and to publish the draft so prepared, in the Government Gazette and present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Implementation of the Government Borrowing Programme for 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7397",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, for the issuance of Sri Lanka Development Bonds up to US$1,500 Million, under the supervision of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka to implement the Government Borrowing Programme for 2017, by strengthening the flexibility in domestic borrowing and the reserves of the country, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Providing Relief under Emergency Disaster Conditions to House Holders Adversely Affected by the Water Leaks of the Main Tunnel of the Uma Oya Multi Purpose Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7396",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Uma Oya Multi Purpose Development Project is being implemented with the objective of providing water to the Kirindi Oya Basin of the Southern Region which suffers from shortage of water. When the construction work was underway, due to the water ingress in the main tunnel of the Uma Oya, several adverse effects such as drying of domestic wells and development of cracks in the houses occurred in 08 Grama Niladharys' Divisions in the Divisional Secretarys' Divisions of Bandarawela and Ella.  Due to this reason, damages have been caused to the lives and the properties of the people living in those areas while it has also greatly affected the daily livelihoods of the people adversely. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to mitigate the prevailing disastrous conditions and to construct new houses in place of the completely damaged ones, to bring back normalcy to the day to day living conditions of the affected people, providing pipe borne  water connections free of charge etc. and such other reliefs as necessary, expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Procurement of 60 MW of Supplementary Power for a 06 month period to ensure uninterrupted power supply",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7395",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Public Utility Commission has submitted recommendations with regard to the measures to be taken to ensure an uninterrupted power supply to face the likely electricity deficit in a dry weather situation prevailing, presently, in the Island. A major recommendation among other recommendations is to install additional power capacity to the network, expeditiously.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapaitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to purchase a number of generators of 60Mw capacity necessary to generate  power supply for a short period of 06 months by Open International Competitive Bidding Procedure, in accordance with the proposal of the Ceylon Electricity Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Extension of the Expired Agreements of Furnace Oil Power Plants by 06 months",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7394",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers having considered the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapaitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to extend the Power Purchase Agreements made between the Ceylon Electricity Board and the following companies, granted its approval to extend the Agreements up to a period of 06 months, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee, to meet the power need in the likely electricity deficit in the future due to the dry weather conditions, presently, prevailing in the country and for an uninterrupted power supply.  \n\n*\tACE Power Embilipitiya (Pvt) Ltd., \n*\tACE Power Generation Matara (Pvt) Ltd.\n*\tHeladanavi (Pvt) Ltd.  Puttalam"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Amendment of the Irrigation Ordinance No. 32 of 1946 to suit the timely needs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7393",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Except for the Mahaweli Authority area, the responsibility of construction, improvement and management of major irrigation canals in all other areas of Sri Lanka is vested with the Department of Irrigation.  Accordingly, in order to enable the Department to carry out its responsibilities, successfully and efficiently, the joint proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management and Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to instruct the Legal Draftsman, to amend the said Ordinance, as recommended by the Expert Committee Appointed to study the Ordinance No.32 of 1946 and make recommendations, to suit the timely national requirements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Development and Improvement of Godigamuwa Tank in the Matale District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7392",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Godigamuwa Tank situated in the Naula Divisional Secretary's Division in the Matale District has a capacity of about 45 acre feet and paddy and several other crops are cultivated using its water. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management, to implement  the project for the development and improvement of the Godigamuwa tank, with a view to ensuring the supply of irrigation water for 162 farmer families living in Dambagalla, Bambaragahawatta and Helambagahawatta in the Naula area, by increasing its capacity from 45 acre feet up to 202 acre feet, at an estimated cost of Rs.165.9 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Implementation of the projects for Municipal Solid Waste Management, at Karadiyana and Muthurajawela areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7391",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to implement two projects at Karadiyana and Muthurajawela areas to generate electricity from waste material with the use of the incineration technology as a remedial measure to solve the problem of waste management in the Districts of Colombo and Gampaha.   It is expected to implement these projects on Public Private Partnership    basis. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the contract to the investors selected following the Government Procurement Procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Allocation of a land at Denzil Kobbekaduwa Mawatha, Battaramulla to the Department of Divineguma Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7390",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to release a plot of land belonging to the Urban Development Authority situated at the Denzil Kobbekaduwa Mawatha, Battaramulla, to the Department of Divineguma Development  to construct its Head Office, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Allocation of a land to the National Institute of Business Management (NIBM) for the construction of a new building",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7389",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present approximately 10,500 students follow the courses conducted in Management, Information Technology and Language Studies by the National Institute of Business Management (NIBM) located at Wijerama Mawatha, Colombo 07 and the demand for such courses is gradually increasing.  However, due to the limited space available at the current premises, it has become difficult to meet the increasing demand and commence new courses. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Skills Development and Vocational Training and Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to expand the scope of the infrastructure facilities of the National Institute of Business Management with the allocation of a land of about 45 perches belonging to the Department of Agriculture situated adjoining  the NIBM, to construct a new building, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Establishment of the Public Private Partnership Division",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7388",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The attention of the government has been focused on the implementation of the projects aligned with the national priority and the economic development agenda under the Public Private Partnerships.  Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance and Hon. Malik Samarawickrama, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to establish a division in the Ministry of Finance comprised of commercial technical expertise to assist the relevant Ministries in providing assistance advice and facilitating when selecting projects suitable to be implemented under the Public Private Partnership collaboration, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Amendment to the Prevention of Mosquito Breeding Act, No. 11 of 2007",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7387",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Presently, Dengue fever has become a major health problem in Sri Lanka.  The most effective and successful preventive measure identified currently is the control of mosquito breeding.  The Legislation which provides for  the control of Dengue is the Prevention of Mosquito Breeding Act, No.11 of 2007.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Dr. Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft Legislation with the objective of making the amendments necessary to the Act, to rectify the deficiencies and shortcomings identified in the implementation of this Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Increase of the Annual Grant to the Sri Lanka Cancer Society",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7386",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Cancer Society inaugurated in 1948, is a voluntary organization committed to serving the patients suffering physically and mentally from cancer. It provides the needy patients suffering from cancer with various needs they deserve and patient care services free of charge for the terminally ill cancer patients operating and maintaining a Hospice - 'Shantha Sevana' and the 'Bandaranaike Memorial Cancer Home'. Therefore, as Government sponsorship for renovation and maintenance activities and considering the services provided by it as a voluntary organization, the proposal made by Hon. Dr. Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to increase the grant of Rs.550,000/- to Rs.2,000,000, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Agreement between Sri Lanka and Iran on Science, Technology and Innovation Cooperation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7385",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Submissions made to the Cabinet by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research to sign the proposed Memorandum of Understanding between Sri Lanka and Iran during his official visit to Iran between 14 to 17 January, 2017, to enhance the cooperation between the two countries in matters related to the  implementation of technology development projects and programmes on Food and Herbal Technology, Bio-technology, Nano Technology and Advanced Material Technology Sectors, Integrated Research and Development, Exchange of Scientific and Technology Personnel and Management of Innovative Projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the United Arab Emirates and Sri Lanka on Cooperation in the field of Higher Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7384",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Education - Higher Education Affairs of the United Arab Emirates and the Ministry of Higher Education and Highways of Sri Lanka on cooperation in the field of Higher Education, with a view to further strengthening the mutual cooperation and also to further improve the cooperation between the higher educational sectors of the two countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Academy of Labour and Social Relations of the Russian Federation and the National Institute of Labour Studies (NILS), Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7383",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Institute of Labour Studies (NILS) functions with the objective of conducting research and carrying out surveys and provide training to widen  the field of labour studies.  In fulfilling its objectives, it is also expected to work in close collaboration with local as well as the foreign institutions. As such, the proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding with the Academy of Labour and Social Relations of the Russian Federation and the National Institute of Labour Studies in Sri Lanka, to exchange information on studies made in the field of socio-labour and to implement joint programmes and projects concerning studies in the field of labour, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Allocation of a plot of land to the Embassy of the State of Palestine",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7382",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to allocate a plot of land located in the Hewa Avenue, Colombo 07, to construct a permanent building for the Embassy of the State of Palestine, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Hosting the 10th Air Services Negotiation Event of the International Civil Aviation Organization in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7381",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) was established as an Agency of the United Nations to manage the administration and governance of the Convention on International Civil Aviation (Chicago Convention) signed in the year 1944 and Sri Lanka functions as a member of the organization since June 1948. Providing a Central meeting place for all member states with a view to improving the efficiency  of the negotiating process in regard to the Aviation Services Agreements, the International Civil Aviation Organization holds an Air Services Agreement Convention, annually. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to host the Convention of the year 2017 in the period from 04 to 08 December 2017 in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Puttalam District Integrated Tourism Development Plan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7380",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- There is an immense possibility of developing Kalpitiya and Puttalam Lagoon area as Sri Lanka's biggest and the main tourism zone.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, for the implementation of a project under the integrated tourism development plan with collaboration of the Ministry of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs and the Ministry of Sustainable Development and Wildlife within the 2 years from 2017 to 2018, with the objective of transforming this area into a sustainable tourism zone and increasing job opportunities in the tourism field through the enhancement of the biodiversity and the conservation in the area, developing tourist industry with increased employment opportunities and empowering the people in the area, a greater contribution towards the national economy based on the main tourism industries prevalent in the Puttalam District, enhancing the income sources of the people and enhancing the attraction of local and foreign tourists, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Marketing Facility Development Project of the Tourism Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7379",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Australian Government has submitted a proposal for the implementation of Marketing Facility Development Project with an investment of Rs.12 Million Australian Dollars for a period of 04 years, targeting the implementation of a project for stimulating business investment in the tourism industry. The proposed project aims at increasing facilities for international business activities in the fields of digital technology which is growing past in Sri Lanka for the identification of new attractive tourist destinations and activities of a more divers nature of the tourism industry, promotion of tourism investment activities in areas where tourism associated business investment is lagging and attracting international consumers for the highest quality 'Sri Lankan made' products.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to enter into an Agreement between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Australia for the implementation of the proposed Marketing Facility Development Project in Sri Lanka with the financial assistance provided by the Government of Australia, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Additional Financing for Kaluganga Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7378",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Kaluganga Development Project is presently implemented with the financial assistance of Saudi Fund for development (SFD), Kuwait Fund for Arab Economic Development (KFAED) and the OPEC Fund for International Development (OFID). The construction work of this project is scheduled to be completed by December 2018.  The revised cost of contract of this project amounts to US$140.35 and close upon US$89.85 has been provided by the Development Partners.  Accordingly, the funds amounting to US$50.5 have to be obtained additionally and therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into an Agreement with the Kuwait Fund for Arab Economic Development (KFAED) to obtain a sum of US$16.5 out of the above funds under the concessionary terms, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding for Development Cooperation Partnership between the Governments of Sri Lanka and Australia",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7377",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The development cooperation between Sri Lanka and Australia dates back to more than 60 years and Australia can be regarded as a leading country which provides Sri Lanka with long term scholarships on various subject fields. A Memorandum of Understanding between the two countries was entered into in the year 1998 to ensure the smooth implementation of the Australian assistance within Sri Lanka and the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to sign the reformulated Memorandum of Understanding with the Government of Australia taking into consideration the policy changes which occurred in both countries recently, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Provision of the required facilities for the Medical Faculties of Rajarata and Eastern Universities and the Faculty of Allied Health Sciences of the University of Peradeniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7376",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has become an urgent need to provide the necessary facilities with the required medical equipment and accessories essential for the faculties of Rajarata and Eastern Universities and the Faculty of Allied Health Sciences of the University of Peradeniya to uplift the quality and teaching and training facilities of the above faculties in par with the other State Universities. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct negotiations to obtain  the necessary funds from a Bank in Australia under concessionary terms and to enter into a loan Agreement in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Creating Awareness on Environment Education of the Teachers in accordance with the New Syllabus introduced",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7375",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The World Leaders and the Environment Organizations have entered into a number of conventions with regard to facing the challenge of climatic changes, successfully adaptation to such conditions and to minimize the damages caused, environment conservation etc. The environment sensitive components have been introduced to the science syllabus when the new syllabus for Grade 6 to Grade 11 were prepared to provide a formal education on such matters to school children with a view to making them aware about the future challenges on climatic and environment changes. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement a project to create awareness for the government teachers in environment education in order to effect an attitudinal change in the school children by providing them with a proper understanding about the environment sector, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-10-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-01-10",
    "description": "Implementation of the Guidelines for the Construction and Maintenance of State Buildings as widely Environment friendly Green Buildings",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7374",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to achieve sustainable development goals in Sri Lanka it is mandatory to obtain the contribution of the green and environment friendly construction sector.  In this respect, the Cabinet of Ministers have already granted approval for the Guidelines to be followed pertaining to designing, construction and maintenance of state buildings as widely environment friendly green buildings. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to obtain the approval to measure the qualitative status in implementing these Guidelines and the rating systems of the institutional structure in respect of the sectors namely energy efficiency, sustainable landscaping and management, infrastructure used for construction and resource management, qualitative aspects of the environment in-side the buildings, water efficiency, green innovation and their socio-cultural adaptability, in the construction of new state buildings, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "'Balagathu Sri Lankavak' - the Government Development Plan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7373",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The booklet titled 'Balagathu Sri Lankavak' which provides a snapshot of the proposed economic development plans and the ongoing progress made concerning such plans to provide a better understanding of the development process and progress made so far, to the public officers and the general public was presented by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "'Let's Protect Children' National Programme - 2017-2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7372",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has identified the necessity to safeguard the children,  the lifeline of the nation, as a priority need against numerous calamities prevalent in the Society. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement the 3 year Activity Plan 'Let's Protect Children' National Programme during the period 2017-2019, encompassing all facets covering, avoid abuse/abduction and ensure child protection, health, nutrition and welfare and personality development, education and life skills, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Construction of the Siyabalanduwa Water Supply Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7371",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Siyambalanduwa Water Supply Scheme in the Moneragala District proposed to be implemented under the water supply and sanitation improvement project, has been planned to provide safe drinking water to over 8,450 houses in the Siyambalanduwa and Muthukandiya areas.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for construction of this water supply scheme, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Greater Colombo Water and Wastewater Management Improvement Investment Programme - Project 2",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7370",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the construction of the Gothatuwa Reservoir with a capacity of 15,000 Cu.m, construction of the Gothatuwa Pump Station and the Booster Pump Station, with the Supply and Laying of 1,200 mm DI Pipes under Tranche 2 of the Greater Colombo Water and Wastewater Management Improvement Investment Programme, implemented with funds provided by the Asian Development Bank and the French Agency for Development (Agence Francaise de Development), as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Establishment of value addition centers in Sri Lanka for Vegetables and Fruits",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7369",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government is providing assistance to farmers and entrepreneurs to export vegetables and fruits to suit the needs of the conditions prevailing in foreign countries, targeting the global export market.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Primary Industries, to establish 03 centres for enhancing the value addition under Public Private Partnership associated with the farms with facilities for processing, packaging and storage, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Rehabilitation of the Elphinstone Theatre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7368",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Elphinstone Theatre Hall constructed in 1925 and acquired by the Government in 1988 is presently governed by the Tower Hall Theatre Foundation. The modernization activities of this Theatre with a 600 seating capacity are being presently carried out and it has been planned to reopen it for the public in the 1st quarter of the year 2017.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to generate the additional funds required for the completion of the remaining activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Recommendations of the Cabinet Sub-Committee on the proposed Registration of Electors (Special Provisions Bill)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7367",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The implementation of the Registration of Electors (Special Provisions) Act, No.27 of 2013 which made provisions for safeguarding the right to vote of the displaced persons and the members of their families who resided in the temporary shelters and lodgings situated in the other areas of the Island having left their villages and properties in the Northern Province due to the conflict situation which prevailed, ended with effect from the 19th of June, 2015. In accordance with the recommendations of the Cabinet Sub-Committee appointed to examine this matter, it is further necessary to achieve the objectivities of the Act. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, as the Chairman of the Sub-Committee, to publish in the Gazette the Registration of Electors (Special Provisions) Bill drafted with a view to providing an extension of the period of the validity of the provisions in the Act for a further period of 04 years and subsequently, present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Development of the Vattarama Sri Arahantha Maliyadewa Raja Maha Vihara sacred area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7366",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Buddha Sasana, to generate the additional provision of Rs.35 Million required for the completion of the development activities of the Vattarama Sri Arahantha Maliyadewa Raja Maha Vihara sacred area  situated in the Divisional Secretary's Division of Galigamuwa in the Kegalle District where the State Vesak Festival of 2017 is scheduled to be held, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Upgrading of the Sri Lanka Institute of Textile & Apparel as a Degree awarding Institution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7365",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka Institute of Textile and Apparel is engaged in the function of conducting training in the industry of Sri Lanka Textile and Apparel, quality testing and providing consultancy services. At present around 4,500 students follow the short term and long term courses offered by the Institute and currently the institute conducts in a wide range of demand driven courses including Certificate and Diploma Level.  With a view to providing the capability of the students of the institute to face the competition, prevalent in the job market, it is proposed to upgrade this institute as a Degree awarding institution in the Textile and Apparel field affiliated with the Lovely Professional University of Punjab in India.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Sri Lanka Textile and Apparel Institute and the Lovely Professional University of Punjab in India, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Establishment of the Ceylon German Technical Training Institute",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7364",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the necessity of incorporating the Ceylon German Technical Training Institute functioning under the Ministry of Skills Development and Vocational Training as a separate legal entity by an Act of Parliament, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Skills Development and Vocational Training, to publish the Draft Bill on the Ceylon German Technical Training Institute, in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Development of the infrastructure facilities of the University of Vocational Technology (UNIVOTEC), Ratmalana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7363",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Around 1,600 students take up the Bachelor of Technology Degree in the University of Vocational Technology at Ratmalana and there is a gradual increase of the number of applicants applying for these courses.  Further, a considerable number of these students are residents from remote areas away from Colombo. This University does not have adequate  hostel facilities to provide accommodation facilities for these students and even in the present canteen the space available is highly limited. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Skills Development and Vocational Training, to construct a new hostel to cater for 600 students, a canteen with 300 seating capacity at one and the same time and also a vocational training workshop to provide facilities for students, at an estimated cost of Rs.927.34 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "The National Policy on Health Information",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7362",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- When providing essential healthcare services and curative and treatment services to the people through the hospital system, diagnosis and treatment of the deceases and the outcome assessment pertaining to administrative decisions, planning and monitoring activities should be carried out properly.  In this respect, availability of an accurate, reliable, relevant and an easily accessible and cost effective information network is of paramount importance to provide health services more effectively. The National Health Information Network of Sri Lanka is mainly comprised of information inputs from the State health service and in future most of the information inputs of the private sector institutions which provide healthcare services will be included in the above information network.  It is also a felt need to improve the paper based system of data capture and transfer same with the use of the modern information and communication technologies.  Accordingly, the 'National Policy on Health Information' formulated in accordance with the objectives of the 'National Health Services Policy' and submitted by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "The Proposed National Elderly Health Policy of Sri Lanka and the Strategies",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7361",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The rapid increase of the ageing population, mainly due to the increase in the life expectancy and the fertility decline is a current problem faced by Sri Lanka.  It is anticipated that the current proportion of 12% of the people aged over 60 years will increase to 16% by 2020 and 29% by 2050. In order to face this situation, it is necessary for the health care  programmes to focus on preventing ill health. Accordingly, the proposal 'National Elderly Health Policy' submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, with a view to providing a wholestic health service for the senior citizens living in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Establishment of the National Science Technology and Innovation Coordinating Authority (NASTICA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7360",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to establish a 'National Science Technology and Innovation Coordinating Authority' by an Act of  Parliament, to facilitate the proper coordination of the research and development activities of Research Institutions and Research Centres numbering about 80 administered by 21 line Ministries with a view to harnessing maximum results on investments made for Science, Technology and Innovation towards Socio Economic Development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Declaration of National Parks and New Wildlife Sanctuaries and the Revision of Boundaries of Sanctuaries so declared",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7359",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Priority has to be accorded to safeguard the natural forests, wet lands and wildlife in order to minimize the danger of destruction of the habitats of animals which have been faced with danger due to various unauthorized activities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to declare the forest stretch of Kalawewa and Balaluwewa of the Kahalla - Pallekale sanctuary bordering the districts of Kurunegala and Anuradhapura as 'Kalawewa National Park', to name the balance forest stretch falling within the Kurunegala District as 'Kahalla - Pallekale National Park', to declare the marine region around the Pasikuda area in the Trincomalee District as 'Kayankarni Marine Natural Reservation', to declare the forest area around the 'Kotuaththawala wewa' situated in the Nikaweratiya Divisional Secretary's Division of the Kurunegala District as 'Kotuaththawala Wildlife Sanctuary', to declare the 'Akurala Wet Land' situated in the Hikkaduwa Divisional Secretary's Division of the Galle District as 'Akurala Wildlife Sanctuary', the 'Kodigahakanda Forest Stretch' situated in the Horana Divisional Secretary's Division of the Kalutara District as 'Kodigahakanda Wildlife Sanctuary' and the Oceanic Zone where Small Rawana and Great Rawana light houses with coral reef situated off the South East Coast of Sri Lanka as the 'Small Rawana and Great Rawana Marine Sanctuaries' and for the revision of boundaries of the Maadu River Sanctuary situated in the Balapitiya Divisional Secretary's Division of the Galle District, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Regulation of Tourist Hotels",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7358",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to place before Parliament for approval, the Regulations, Orders and Rules published in the Gazette Extraordinary No.1963/28 dated 2016-04-20 by the Minister, made in terms of the Tourism Act, No.38 of 2005, with regard to the minimum capacity and facilities required in tourist hotels for classification under 1  to 5 Star categories, the fees payable for registration, Code of conduct of tourist hotels, registration and licensing of tourist hotels and the  provision of minimum accommodation facilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-01-03-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-01-03",
    "description": "Implementation of the National Biodiversity Strategic Action Plan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7357",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka is a signatory to the International Convention on Bio-diversity  which was formulated to coincide with the 'Earth Summit' which was held in the year 1992. In accordance with the commitments of the convention, Sri Lanka has carried out a number of programmes from the year 1992 up to 2016 for the conservation of Bio-diversity.  The National Bio-diversity Expert Committee, with the participation of the relevant stakeholders, has also prepared a National Bio-diversity Conservation Action Plan with Bio-diversity Strategies to be implemented during the period 2016 to 2022.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, for the implementation of the National Bio-diversity Conservation  Strategic Action Plan for 2016-2022, with the objective of conserving Bio-diversity in Sri Lanka, sustainable use of Bio-diversity and the equitable sharing of the benefits accrued, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-12-20-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-12-20",
    "description": "Import of Rice to maintain a buffer stock for the prevention of a price hike in the Domestic Market",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7356",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-12-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the adverse weather conditions prevailing in the island, which has resulted in not having adequate rain, there is a steep decline in the extent of land cultivated in paddy in the Maha Season this year. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, for the private sector to import rice and maintain a buffer stock to prevent any shortage of rice in the market, to store the rice so imported in the bonded warehouses as a buffer stock and to release the rice to the market systematically, so as to enable the control  of price of  rice in the market, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-12-20-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-12-20",
    "description": "Expansion of the facilities in the Vocational Training Centre, Moneragala of the National Youth Services Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7355",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-12-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Moneragala Vocational Training Centre of the National Youth Services Council was established in the year 1987 and no proper programme has since been initiated up to now for the expansion of its facilities. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs,  to construct a new building to accommodate lecture halls in the Vocational Training Centre, Moneragala, to conduct 10 courses, with facilities for training of 250 youth, aimed at the job market for motor mechanism, construction and tourist hotel industry, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-12-20-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-12-20",
    "description": "Awarding four Contracts for the Development of Roads under the Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa District Development Programme of the Presidential Programme for 'Awakening Rajarata'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7354",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-12-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the following four contracts implemented under the Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa District Development Programme of the Presidential Programme for 'Awakening Rajarata, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tDevelopment of Manampitiya - Aralaganwila - Maduru Oya Road (from 3.0km up to 33.0km)\n*\tRehabilitation and Improvement of the Dehiattakandiaya - Aralaganwila of Road (from 0km up to 21.10km)\n*\tImprovement of the Minneriya - Galoya Road (from 0km up to 14.54km)\n*\tImprovement of the Elahera - Giritale Road (from 0km up to 29.0km)"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-12-20-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-12-20",
    "description": "Financing the Consultancy Services for Design Review and Construction Supervision of Civil Works for extension of the Southern Expressway Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7353",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-12-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction work of all the 4 Sections of the Southern Expressway from Matara to Hambantota commenced in the latter part of 2015 and as of now the construction work is underway.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to enter into a Framework Agreement with the Government of the Peoples Republic of China, to obtain a loan of Renminbi Yuan 577 Million for the Design Review and the Construction Supervision of Civil Work and also to enter into a Loan Agreement with Exim Bank of China to obtain the above Loan under the concessional loan facilities provided by the Government of China, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-12-20-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-12-20",
    "description": "The Pilot Project for establishment of a Ground Water Monitoring Network covering the Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa and Moneragala Districts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7352",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-12-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Proper management of ground water usage in Sri Lanka is extremely important and in this context, it is essential to collect timely data on quantity and quality of ground water.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management, to award the contract for the establishment of a pilot project on the data network on ground water monitoring, covering the river basins of the Malwathu Oya in the Anuradhapura District, the Maduru Oya in the Polonnaruwa District and the Kumbukkan Oya in the Moneragala District, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
