    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-10-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to sign at State Level, the Agreement to be entered into between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Republic of Finland, for the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of fiscal evasion of taxes on income with a view to improving economic relations and enhancing cooperation between Sri Lanka and Finland, and to move a resolution in Parliament to that effect, in terms of Section 97 (1) (a) of the Inland Revenue Act, No.10 of 2006, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-10-04-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-10-04",
    "description": "Provision of relief to persons affected by recent disasters - Progress as at 2016-08-31",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7089",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-10-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet noted the following information submitted by Hon. Anura Priyadharashan Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, relating to the progress  achieved by the end of August  2016, on the provision of relief to  persons affected by the explosion that occurred on 2016-06-05 at the Salawa Army Camp located in Seethawaka Divisional Secretariat Division of the Colombo District, provision of relief to persons affected by the landslides which occurred as a result of heavy rains in the Kegalle District between 10th  to 17th of May 2016 and the provision of relief for those who were affected due to floods and landslides that occurred in  May 2016:   \n *   Provision of Rs.422.85 million has already been issued to District Secretariat, Colombo, for the provision of relief  to people affected by the explosion that occurred at the Army Camp located at Salawa, and the said provisions have been spent to provide monthly allowances for  persons with damaged houses until they  return  to their houses, to grant allowances to those affected who were self-employed and  for the payment of compensation  for the damaged houses.  \n*      Provisions have been given to the District Secretariat Kegalle, at various instances, to provide relief to 34,653 people of 9,588 families in the said district, who were affected due to landslides which occurred as a result of heavy rains in the Kegalle District between 10th to 17th of May 2016 and action is being taken to construct 145 houses, for the families recommended to be resettled due to high-risk, with the contribution of the private sector.  \n*    \tMeasures have been taken to provide Rs. 586.79 million  under the National Insurance Programme for natural disasters, Rs.149.02 million  under  the National Insurance Programme and Rs. 111.21 million  under the treasury provisions for the  provision of relief to  586,731 persons of 142,942 families affected due to disasters of floods and landslides that occurred in  May 2016."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-10-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-10-04",
    "description": "Bilateral Air Services Consultations between Sri Lanka and Finland",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7088",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-10-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to formally sign the Air Services Agreement between Sri Lanka and Finland, agreed on 2013-12-12 in Durban, South Africa in order to  exercise the freedom traffic rights for both passenger and cargo flights of the two countries without any restrictions and to accept the designated airlines of the two countries, and thereafter to take appropriate measures for its entry into force, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-10-04-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-10-04",
    "description": "Air Services Consultations between Sri Lanka and the Kingdom of Norway/ Sweden/Denmark (The Parties)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7087",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-10-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to formally sign the Air Services Agreement agreed on 2015-10-21 by the Aeronautical Authorities of the states concerned, during the International Civil Aviation Negotiations Conference (ICAN) held in Antalya, Turkey, for the purpose of conducting both passenger and freighter operations between Sri Lanka and the Kingdom of Norway/Sweden/Denmark and to take appropriate measures for its entry into force, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-10-04-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-10-04",
    "description": "Implementation of Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme - Tranche 2",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7086",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-10-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to obtain funds from the Asian Development Bank (ADB), for the implementation of Tranche 2 of the Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme, comprising of the components of electricity transmission infrastructure enhancement, efficiency improvement of the medium-voltage network and expansion of demand-based power management for energy efficiency through development of a smart grid and metering pilot sub-project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-10-04-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-10-04",
    "description": "Strengthening the  Farmers of the Dry Zone to face up to the impacts of climate change",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7085",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-10-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the recent past, Sri Lanka had to face calamities such as rising temperatures,  erratic rainfall patterns as well as ensuing severe droughts and floods due to climate change and the people who farm in the Dry Zone using rain water and rural irrigation systems, are the ones most affected by these disasters.  Similarly, the Chronic Kidney Disease (CKDu), which has severely affected the Dry Zone, shows a high incidence in 81 Divisional Secretariat Divisions of 11 districts in the  said Zone. Accordingly,  with a view to  promoting integrated development in the watershed areas of Malwathu Oya, Yan Oya and Mee Oya river basins where  rural irrigation systems are more prevalent and the  Kidney Disease and Poverty are widespread, implementing drinking water supply schemes in the districts of Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa, Mannar, Vavuniya, Trincomalee, Kurunegala and Puttalam, which are connected to the above river basins and strengthening the institutional and organizational structures of the relevant areas with community participation to face up to disasters, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment,to implement a Climate Resilience Project through integrated water management, within 07 years from the year 2017,  utilizing the grant of US$ 38.087 million to be provided by the Green Climate Fund (GCF), established under the  United Nations Framework Convention on  Climate Change (UNFCCC),  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Redevelopment of the Bogambara Prison Precinct",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7084",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to entrust the redevelopment of the precincts of the Bogambara Prison of about 5ha in Kandy city, which has become vacant due to the said Prison being relocated in Pallekele area, as a tourist centre, in a manner that safeguards its historic value, to an internationally reputed institution which possesses expertise in designing such work, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Revision of taxes imposed on Cigarettes and Tobacco Products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7082",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been revealed through surveys that 15% of persons between the ages of 18 to 69  in Sri Lanka are smokers and it is estimated that the annual deaths which occur due to tobacco related diseases amount to approximately 30,000. It has been calculated that the Government has to spend annually, a sum of about Rs.72 billion to treat the ailments caused through the use of tobacco.  'Imposing of taxes' has been identified as a successful methodology in  controlling  the use of tobacco and the consumption of cigarettes, by the World Health Organization (WHO).   Accordingly, as per the recommendation made by the Ministerial Committee appointed to consider the joint proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena and Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to revise the tax imposed on cigarettes and tobacco products, the Cabinet decided to re-impose the 15% Value Added Tax (VAT) on cigarettes; to increase the production tax on a cigarette of any size by Rs.5/-; to increase the cess tax on import of beedi leaves from Rs.2,000/- to Rs.3,000/- per kilogram; and in addition, to take action to reduce the use of tobacco in the country, through the adoption of other measures as well."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Review of the Government Paddy Purchasing Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7081",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government Paddy Purchasing Programme, under this government, has been implemented up to now throughout the three consecutive harvesting Seasons of Maha 2014/15, Yala 2015 and Maha 2015/16. The Cabinet approved the implementation of the proposals made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of  Finance, to dispose the remaining paddy stock of the paddy purchased in the year 2015, following the government approved procurement procedure, prior to the  commencement of the reaping of harvest of Yala 2016; to dispose  the paddy  stocks purchased in the year 2016 and stored in warehouses of the Paddy Marketing Board, during the months of October and November, where the higher  price is reported; and to settle the outstanding balances to the General Treasury; and to settle the dues to the State Banks pertaining to  paddy purchasing through utilizing  the money derived from paddy disposal, with a view to implementing the said programme successfully in the future too, as per the recommendations made by the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management (CCEM)."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Restructuring of the Department of Labour and the Drafting of a Service Minute for Labour Officers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7080",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The private sector renders an immense contribution to the economic growth of the country and a huge task is being carried out by the Department of Labour to  maintain  industrial peace, which is required to  obtain the services of the private sector efficiently and qualitatively. The Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations has appointed an Officials' Committee to study the problems that arise in providing the services of the Department efficiently and with high quality and to make recommendations to restructure the Department to suit the present day needs and the recommendation process of the said Committee is at its final phase.  Simultaneous with the said process, an Officials' Committee comprising of the officials of the relevant ministries and the departments, has also been appointed  to draft a Service Minute for the Labour Officers' Service, for the improvement of the service conditions of the Labour Officers in the Department of Labour. Accordingly, the Cabinet noted the information submitted by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations, to the effect that the Reports of the above two (02) Officials' Committees will be submitted to the Cabinet in near future."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Awarding  the Contract for the Construction of  Anchorage Facilities at Peraliya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7079",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to award the contract for the construction of  the proposed anchorage facilities to be established at Peraliya, Galle district, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Supply of Medical Equipment for the Epilepsy Unit of the National Hospital of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7078",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the procurement/tender for the supply and installation of the Monitoring Medical Equipment essential for providing an advanced healthcare service through the newly constructed Epilepsy Unit of the National Hospital of Sri Lanka, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Completion the Construction Work of the Cancer Treatment Centre at  Teaching Hospital, Kandy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7077",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Teaching Hospital, Kandy, which is the second largest tertiary healthcare institute in Sri Lanka, caters to about 4,000 cancer patients every year. With a view to increasing the number of beds in the hospital by 340 and providing a more qualitative healthcare service to the cancer patients, the construction of a 11 storied Cancer Treatment Centre for the Teaching Hospital, Kandy was commenced in the year 2013 and the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the completion of the balance work (Phase III) of the Centre, to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Improvement of the Main Road, that runs towards Nedunkerni Town  from Gajabapura area of Welioya, Mullaitivu District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7076",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The main road of 11.1 km long running from Gajabapura, Welioya to the Nedunkerni Town, is the shortest route  available for the people living in Welioya, Mullaitivu District, to access the Mullaitivu Town, which is the main town of the  district. The development of this road, which is highly dilapidated at present, would ease the daily life of the people living in the Welioya area. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to improve this road, at an estimated cost of Rs.466.3 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Implementation of Projects with the objective of dispersing the benefits of the digital technology to every citizen of the country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7075",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the objective of dispersing the benefits of  digital technology to every citizen in the country, a number of development projects that should be implemented within the three year period from 2016 to 2018, have been identified by the Information and CommunicationTechnology Agency (ICTA) of Sri Lanka.    Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, the Minister of Telecommunication and Digital Infrastructure, for the implementation of 40 projects under the programmes of 'National Digitization' and 'Upgrading Nenasala', utilizing the budgetary provisions approved for the year 2016, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "13. National Anti-Corruption Summit scheduled to be held in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7074",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted approval to conduct a National Anti-Corruption Summit in Sri Lanka, with the objectives of educating politicians, senior officials in public and private sectors, other relevant parties and the general public for the establishment of a corruption free society and creating a dialogue in society on the eradication of bribery and corruption. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to hold a 'National Summit on Anti-Corruption' in Colombo, on the 09th of December, 2016, with the participation of about 700 local and foreign  representatives, to coincide with the International Anti-Corruption Day, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Prevention of the difficulties caused to the general public due to stray dogs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7073",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, for the implementation of the Action Plan containing the recommendations focusing on the areas of controlling the dog population, efficient conducting of dog vaccination programmes, establishing  dog care centres and creating proper coordination in this regard between the Local Government Authorities and other institutions, submitted by the Officials' Committee appointed by the Cabinet to formulate a suitable mechanism to prevent the difficulties caused to the general public due to the stray dogs, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Improving the nutritional levels of the Children of Early Childhood Development Centres/Pre-Schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7072",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The programme to provide a glass of fresh milk for the children learning in  Childhood Development Centres and Pre-Schools is being implemented since the year 2006, with the objectives of improving the nutritional levels of the children of low income families who suffer from nutritional deficiencies and strengthening the domestic dairy farmer. When reviewing the said programme, experts have pointed out that the nutritional requirements of  a pre-school child could not be fulfilled  through merely providing a glass of milk. With a view to minimizing the nutrition deficiencies of children in their early childhood,  the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to select the Divisions of Medical Officers of Health (MOH), where a higher percentage of underweight children of 2-5 years of age reside and to implement a programme of providing a balanced breakfast to the children of the Early Childhood Development Centres in such divisions, during the five (05) days of the week, from the year 2017, in place of the programme of providing a fresh glass of milk, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Acquisition of Land for the Construction of the Proposed Economic Centre in Vavuniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7071",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- A sum of Rs.200 million has been allocated through the Budget Proposals - 2016, for the construction of a Dedicated Economic Centre in the vicinity of  Vavuniya Town.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, to acquire for the said Ministry, a block of land in extent of 2.5 Acres situated in the Madauwythakulam village in the Munrumurippu Grama Niladhari Division, selected with the consent of the Co-Chairmen of the District Coordinating Committee of Vavuniya, for the construction of the said Dedicated Economic Centre,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Incorporation of the Institute of Food Science and Technology of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7070",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Institute of Food Science and Technology of Sri Lanka functions with the objectives of providing modern technological knowledge required for food production and processing industry in Sri Lanka, improving the quality and  safety of foods on a scientific basis in keeping with international standards and bringing the country's food industry up to an internationally competitive level.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to incorporate the Institute of Food Science and Technology of Sri Lanka, through an Act of Parliament, in order to strengthen the operations of the said Institute, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Purchase of Soya Bean for the Production of Thriposha",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7069",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The annual requirement of Soya Bean in Sri Lanka is around 220,000 MT and the average annual production of Soya Bean in the country is around 22,500 MT.  Therefore, high priority has been given by the Government to enhance the production of Soya Beans.  As such, during the Yala Season of 2016, Soya Bean has been cultivated in about 4,000 ha, giving priority to the Mahaweli Zones and the Anuradhapura District and the anticipated harvest from that is about 8,000 MT.  With a view to protecting the local farmers and promoting supplementary food crop production, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to purchase about 5,000 MT. of the said anticipated harvest from farmers and issue to the Thriposha Production Programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Transferring the freshwater hatchery at Panapitiya, Kalutara, to the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency, permanently",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7068",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The ornamental fisheries industry is a high-potential area that can make a considerable contribution towards employment generation, and researches related to the said industry are being successfully conducted by the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency (NARA). Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development to permanently transfer the freshwater hatchery at Panapitiya, Kalutara, which is presently, a property of the National Aquaculture Development Authority of Sri Lanka (NAQDA), to the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency, to enable the the fulfilment of research requirements related to the ornamental fisheries industry, while enhancing its infrastructure facilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Providing Water Supply Facilities for the Villages where the affected families in the Kegalle District are resettled",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7067",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- About 2,000 families in Kegalle District have been temporarily settled in 65 locations, due to the destruction of their houses or the removal from their homes as a result of landslides and high-risk  warnings. It has been planned to resettle the said displaced people in 11 Divisional Secretariats of the Kegalle District.  Water supply facilities have to be provided expeditiously to the 45 places so identified as suitable for resettlement. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to provide the necessary water supply facilities, at an estimated cost of Rs.455 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Ensuring safety at unguarded railway crossings",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7066",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- There are about 676 unguarded railway gates within Sri Lanka and even though there should be 2028 gate keepers, consisting of 03 persons per gate, only 1953 gate keepers are currently employed to assure the safety of pedestrians, passengers and  vehicles. An honorary service is rendered by them for a monthly allowance of only Rs.7,500/-, which consists of Rs.250 per day, without any right to salaries, wages and other privileges to which  government servants are entitled. Considering the requests made by the said gate keepers to the effect that this allowance is  inadequate,  the proposals made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, as per  the recommendations of the Officials' Committee appointed to submit  recommendations to resolve this problem, that the allowance of Rs.22,500/- presently  allocated per a month for 03 gate keepers, should be granted not as an allowance made for a person but as an allowance made per a gate, and that a suitable internal arrangement should be formulated to distribute that allowance  among the railway gate keepers involved per gate and to install railway gates with 'Bell and Light' systems  in relevant places, as a long-term solution, giving priority to places where most accidents occur and unsafe locations with bends, were approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Enforcement of the Memorandum of Understanding relevant to Youth development due to be signed between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Islamic Republic of Pakistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7065",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted approval to sign the Memorandum of Understanding pertaining to Youth development between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Islamic Republic of Pakistan. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, for the revised Memorandum of Understanding, incorporating the subsequent amendments made by the Government of Pakistan, to be signed between the Ministry of National Policies and Economic Affairs of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Inter Provincial Coordination of Pakistan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Filling of the Existing Teacher Vacancies",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7064",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- An adequate number of teachers should be available in schools to ensure equal access to a qualitative education in  schools  throughout the island.  However, there is a dearth of about 22,500 teachers as a whole, in  schools across  the island. Neither Teachers nor resources have been adequately provided for, especially, to the schools in rural areas to teach the subjects of Science, Maths and English. With a view to providing a sustainable solution to this problem, in addition to the recruitment of graduates from state universities and diploma holders, it has been planned to implement a programme to recruit youth who have passed A/Ls and qualified for university entrance,  to the teaching service, after completion of a B.Ed (Science) or a B.Ed. (Arts) Degree awarded by a  private university approved by the Ministry of Higher Education and Highways, and also to provide a sum of Rs.275,000/- annually by a state bank to those who have been admitted to such Degree programme and after completing the Degree, to have them serve in a teacher vacancy in a school in a district of their choice for 10 years. In case they serve for a period of 10 years in the relevant district, action will be taken not to recover the loan granted to them for the Degree programme. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickramasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to recruit 5,000 students, who have passed the G.C.E. (A.L) Examination, as teachers of Science and Maths under this programme during the 1st Phase, was approved by the Cabinet. \n \n\tIt was also decided to vest authority on the Ministry of Education, to recruit graduates expeditiously to address the dearth of Science teachers existing in the government schools."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Construction and maintenance of Government and Semi-government buildings widely as eco-friendly green buildings",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7063",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although our ancestors had constructed their dwelling places using very simple plans and maintaining very high standards to suit the tropical climatic conditions; in the recent years, due to imitating foreign architectural designs without paying attention to the climatic conditions in Sri Lanka, most of the present day buildings are deprived of sufficient sunlight and natural ventilation and have become dependent on artificial lighting and air conditioning and as a result, a plethora of environmental, economic and technological issues have arisen. Buildings which are constructed with eco-friendly materials and methods and optimal and efficient utilization of other resources including energy, are commonly known as 'green buildings' and when moving towards sustainable development, the adoption of the Guidelines on  Green Buildings is of utmost importance.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the Guidelines on Green Buildings, prepared with the concurrence of the relevant Ministries, by the Officials' Committee appointed to submit recommendations on bringing all government buildings to up to a sustainable and eco-friendly level and maintaining such buildings in a safe and user-friendly manner, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-27-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-09-27",
    "description": "Construction of a Quay at Naval Dockyard - Trincomalee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7062",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the terrorist activities which prevailed in the past, the Trincomalee harbour which is one of the deepest natural harbours in the world and the second deepest in Asia, could not be properly developed. The largest base of the Sri Lanka Navy is located in this harbour and the naval dockyard situated there is the home to the Eastern Naval Command and the Maritime Academy of Sri Lanka. Although the construction work of a quay at the naval dockyard had been commenced in the year 1990 to provide berthing facilities for larger vessels, the said construction work has been subsequently suspended due to various reasons.  Since action is being  taken by the Sri Lanka Navy to  acquire four (04) larger vessels during the period of 2017-2019 to expand the patrolling of the Sri Lankan territorial waters, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to recommence the construction work of the proposed quay, with a length of 220m and a width of 20m, and an access bridge, in order to provide berthing facilities for such larger vessels at the naval dockyard in Trincomalee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Extending the service period of Experienced Clinical Consultants up to 63 Years of Age",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7061",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- There are 1,164 vacancies in the posts of Medical Consultants in the curative sectors of Hospitals in the Island. Since a considerable period of time will be needed to fill the said vacancies under the prevailing system and taking into consideration their ability to serve beyond the existing  compulsory age of retirement, with the skills and experiences acquired during their service period, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to extend the age of compulsory retirement of experienced Medical Consultants serving in the curative sectors up to age of 63 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Conducting the Cremation Ceremony of Late Most Venerable Nauyane Ariyadhamma Thero, the Venerable Sub-Chief Incumbent of the Ramanna Chapter, under State Sponsorship",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7060",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Appreciating the great service rendered to Sri Lanka nationally and religiously by the Late Most Venerable Nauyane Ariyadhamma Thero,  Maha Kammattanacharya, Mahopadya, Thripitakacharya, Venerable Sub-Chief Incumbent of the Ramanna, Chapter and  Chief Advisor to Kalyani Yogashrama Sansthawa, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to hold the Cremation Ceremony of Ven. Thero, under state sponsorship, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Organizing the 69th  Independence Day falling on 04th  February 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7059",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to appoint a Committee under the Chairmanship of Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to organize and monitor the programmes pertaining to the 69th Independence Day Celebration falling on 04th of February 2017, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Amendments to the Act on Value Added Tax",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7058",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the Budget proposals 2016, the decision taken at the special Cabinet Meeting held on 2016-03-04 and in accordance with the recommendation of the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management (CCEM) held on 2016-06-15, it was decided to revise the provisions pertaining to the VAT under the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to publish the Value Added Tax (Amendment) Bill  amended incorporating the following proposals, in the Government Gazette instead of the Bill submitted previously with regard to the VAT amendment and thereafter to present same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet:     \n\n   \t(i)\tFixing VAT rate at 15%;\n\n(ii)\tReduction of the threshold of Registration for VAT from Rs.3.75 million per quarter or Rs.15 million per annum to Rs.3 million per quarter or Rs.12 million per annum;\n\n(iii)\tImposition of VAT on the following goods and services\n*\tWholesale or retail trade valued more than Rs.50 million per annum (i.e. Rs.12.5 million per quarter);\n*\tPrivate health services other than OPD services that do not contain diagnostic tests, dialysis and medical consultancy services;\n*\tTelecommunication services; \n*\tTobacco products;\n*\tPowdered milk containing added sugar or other sweeteners;\n*\tAir ticketing fee of Air passengers moving from an airport in Sri Lanka to an airport outside Sri Lanka;\n\n(iv)\tRestriction of the VAT exemption applicable on the supply, lease or rent of residential accommodation services carried out by projects of which the investment cost does not exceed US$ 05 million, other than services made by Strategic Development Projects (SDPs) approved prior to 2015-11-01 or by SDPs and other projects where the sales agreements are entered into or project completed before 2016-10-01. \n \n(v)\tIncrease of the piece rate of garments supplied to the local market by companies registered under the Sri Lanka Board of Investment (BOI) up to Rs.75/- per piece."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Construction of a Three Storied New Building for the Divisional Secretariat, Panadura",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7057",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Divisional Secretariat, Panadura belonging to the Kalutara District, consists of 72 Grama Niladhari Divisions with a population of about 205,969. Since there is insufficient space in the buildings where the Divisional Secretariat is housed, the people who daily visit the office to  receive services and also the staff of the office have to undergo many difficulties. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to construct a new building for the Divisional Secretariat, Panadura, with the necessary facilities, at an estimated cost of Rs.172.8 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Projects implemented by the Ministry of Telecommunication and Digital Infrastructure  for the improvement of the Information  Technology Literacy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7056",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, the Minister of Telecommunication and Digital Infrastructure, to implement the two (02) projects namely the 'School Computer Labs Project' carried out with a view to improving the Information Technology (IT) infrastructure and literacy in the identified schools across the country coming under the purview of the Provincial Councils and the 'District IT Resources Centres Project' carried out with the main objective of coordinating with the district administration on issues related to IT resources management in each district, utilizing the budgetary provision of Rs.250 million and Rs.42 million set apart from the Budget 2016, respectively, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Acquisition of Soranawatta land in Horana, to the Department of Prisons, to relocate the Welikada Prison and its supportive units",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7055",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to vest the Soranawatta land in extent of 28 acres situated in Horana, presently possessed by the UDA, with the Department of Prisons, for the relocation of Welikada Prison, Prison Hospital, Women's Ward and Prison Quarters and the other Units of the prison and to handover the land in extent of 38.5 acres in extent belonging to the Department of Prisons where the Welikada Prison is presently situated, to the UDA for town development activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in the Fields of Radio, Television and Film between Sri Lanka and   Bangladesh",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7054",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to exchanging current news and television programmes,  success stories and technology in the Media field between the two countries, the proposal made by Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Parliamentary Reforms and Mass Media, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Ministry of Parliamentary Reforms and Mass Media of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Information of the People's Republic of Bangladesh, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Mihintale Town Centre Re-development Project at Mihintale",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7053",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Urban Development Authority (UDA) has prepared a plan to develop the Mihintale Town with facilities required for around 8,000 people that daily visit the town for various requirements as well as for the devotees and tourists who visit the town in the festive season.  Under this plan it has been proposed to construct commercial buildings, a public market, a surface drain system, children's parks, public places,  car parks  and street seating places.  Accordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement the Mihintale Town Centre Re-development Project, during the period from 2016 to 2019, at an estimated cost of Rs.200 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Vesting of Lands required for the Development of the Angunakolapelassa Town",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7052",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Urban Development Authority (UDA) has designed to develop the Angunukolapelassa Town which is located in a place that links towns in the Hambantota District with each other, under a formal development plan. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development,  to vest a block of land in extent of 9A-2R-10P belonging to the Mahaweli Development Authority, situated in the Angunukolapelassa town, with the UDA, required for the development projects such as the construction of proposed circuit bungalows, bank buildings, commercial complex, buildings for government institutions, public car park and the  development of the town centre and the bus stand, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Construction of a New Building for the National Design Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7051",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The building which currently accommodates the National Design Centre established for the betterment of local handicraft artists is in a very  dilapidated condition and cannot withstand renovation or alteration to suit  the present day requirements.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to demolish the said building and construct a new building with the required facilities including a workshop, design unit, library, craft demonstration area and administration block etc., for each handicraft sector, at an estimated cost of Rs.80 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Introduction of Contributory Pension Scheme for Artists",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7050",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Through the Budget proposals for 2016, funds have been allocated for the creation of a Contributory Pension Scheme for Artists, engaged in various fields of Arts, with a view to ensure their professional recognition and social security.  Accordingly, the proposal  made by Hon. S.B. Nawinne, the Minister of Internal Affairs, Wayamba Development and Cultural Affairs, to implement a Contributory Pension Scheme for the Artists selected by the Department of Cultural Affairs, adopting a method of awarding marks based on age, through the Social Security Board,  effective from this year onwards, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Amendment of the Sri Lanka Disaster Management Act, No.13 of 2005",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7049",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'The National Council for Disaster Management' and 'the Disaster Management Centre' were established in the year 2005, under the provisions of the Sri Lanka Disaster Management Act, No.13 of 2005, as institutional structures which function to manage the disaster situations  that occur due to natural and human activities and a separate Ministry was established in the year 2010 for the subject of Disaster Management.  The likelihood of the occurrence of disasters has rapidly increased in the recent past and taking into consideration the practical difficulties encountered by the Disaster Management Centre and the Ministry of Disaster Management in carrying out the responsibilities and functions entrusted under the above Act, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadarshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to amend the Sri Lanka Disaster Management Act, to enable the performance of the functions mentioned in the said Act with proper coordination and collaboration, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "National Occupational Safety Week 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7048",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The arrangements have been made to conduct the 'National Occupational Safety Week' organized annually by the National Institute of Occupational Safety and Health (NIOSH), from 7th to 14th of October 2016, with the main objective of making an outstanding contribution towards boosting the national production through creating a healthy labour force, by minimizing all forms of work related hazards.  It is scheduled to hold an International Conference and a National Seminar on Occupational Safety and Health concurrent with this year's 'National Occupational Safety and Health Week'; and the 'National Occupational Safety and Health - Awards of Excellence Ceremony' will be held, with a view to appreciating the selected business entities which are committed to creating a safe working environment for the employees.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations, to implement this year's National Occupational Safety Week' in collaboration with the relevant public and private institutions, treating it as a National Programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Increasing the compensation paid for damages to human lives and property caused by wild elephants",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7047",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The compensation paid for damages to human lives and property caused by wild elephants has been revised lastly in the year 2004.  Accordingly, the total sum of compensation paid annually is around Rs.25million to Rs.35 million. The proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to provide redress through increasing the existing compensation up to Rs. 200,000/- for a death, Rs. 200,000/- for permanent disability (regardless of the existing age limit), Rs. 75,000/- for injuries, and Rs.100,000/- for house and property damages, caused due to a wild elephant attack, and in order to minimize the delays caused when approving such compensation, to entrust the responsibility of payment of compensation to a Committee headed by the District Secretary and to establish an Appeal Committee headed by the Director General of Wild Life to consider the appeals submitted by the parties dissatisfied with the decisions of the said Committee pertaining to payment of compensation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-13-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-09-13",
    "description": "Creating an Accelerated Economic Transformation in Sri Lanka - Setting up a Central Programme Management Unit",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7046",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Setting up of a unit dedicated to track, monitor and take timely corrective actions in respect of development activities, is considered most critical to achieve the objectives of enabling an accelerated economic development across the country and transforming the country's economy into a sustainable social market economy. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, and the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to obtain the assistance of McKinsey & Company of USA, which is a foreign consultancy firm with proven experience and capability of setting up of similar CPM Units in rapidly transforming economies such as Malaysia, for setting up of a CPMU in Sri Lanka to carry out the desired objectives, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Financial Assistance from the Asian Development Bank for the Proposed Capital Market Development Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7045",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to mobilizing financial resources required for the economic development through the capital market of Sri Lanka productively, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to conduct negotiations to obtain a policy based loan assistance of US$ 250 million from the Asian Development Bank (ADB), for the development an  efficient, stable and transparent capital market comprised of a strong, legal and regulatory framework, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Construction of Section 4 of the Central Expressway from Kurunegala to Dambulla (60 km)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7044",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted its approval to rehabilitate 150 km of the existing roads and to construct 100 km of new roads, under the 'Rajarata Navodaya' Development Programme.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to implement the proposed project of constructing Section 4 of the Central Expressway, 60 km in length, commencing from Kurunegala and running up to Dambulla, under the 'Rajarata Navodaya' Development Programme,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Maduru Oya Right Bank Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7043",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Maduru Oya Reservoir constructed in the year 1982 is one of the major reservoirs constructed under the Mahaweli Accelerated Development Progrmme.  It was expected through the above reservoir to develop 39,000 ha of land in the Mahaweli System 'B' based on the districts of  Polonnaruwa and Batticaloa, for agricultural purposes. Although, the Maduru Oya Left Bank development activities were initiated and completed, the development of the Right Bank area has not been implemented so far due to the inadequacy of the financial provisions.  Accordingly, with a view to expediting the supply of drinking water, provision of irrigation water and development of infrastructure facilities for the socio\u2011economic development in the districts of Polonnaruwa and Batticaloa, where development had stalled due to the impact of prolonged conflict, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the Maduru Oya Right Bank Development Project during the period of 2017-2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Completion of the Construction Work of Polpithigama Police Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7042",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction work of the  Polpithigama Police station, belonging to the Police Division of Nikaweratiya and with 130 Police personnel in service, had been initiated in the year 2007, but however, has been suspended midway due to various reasons.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Rathnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to complete the construction work of the Polpithigama Police Station, at a total estimated cost of Rs.49.7 million, also incorporating the subsequently identified requirements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Project for the Construction of Thambalagamuwa Police Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7041",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Thambalagamuwa Police Station, which functioned as a Police Post to provide public security in the areas of Muthur, Seruwawila and Trincomalee in the Eastern Province and subsequently established as a Police Station in the year 2004, is presently housed, with 155 Police personnel in service, in two buildings obtained on a rental basis, with minimum facilities.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Rathnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to construct a new building for the said Police Station, in a  land belonging to the Police Department, at an estimated cost of Rs.90.4 million, to enable it to provide a better public service, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Implementation of a new Inland Water Transport System through Private-Public Partnership",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7040",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- In a backdrop where there is a steady escalation of traffic congestion in the city, it has been identified that a rapid and economical transportation service based on reservoirs and canals could be provided for the areas where bus or railway transportation services are inadequately deployed.  Therefore, using the existing canal system and sea, an efficient transportation service that links the East-West and North-South areas of Colombo, could be provided.  Accordingly, three inland water transport lines, namely Wellawatta - Battaramulla (through the canals), Fort - Union Place (along the Beira Lake) and Mattakuliya - Hanwella (along the Kelani River) have been identified by the Megapolis Transport Committee as potential routes for the purpose.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to carry out a feasibility study with regard to the construction of an Inland Water Transport System under a Private\u2011Public Partnership system, identifying a suitable private investor, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "'Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa' District Development Programme -  Implementation of Priority Water Supply Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7039",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the objective of providing safe drinking water for the upliftment of the living standard of the people of Polonnaruwa District, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to implement nine (09) water supply projects under the 'Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa' District Development Programme and to get the required sum of Rs.6,464.36 million set apart for the purpose, for the years 2017 and 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding on the Establishment of a Political Consultation Mechanism between Slovenia and Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7038",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to promoting, strengthening and expanding bilateral relations including political, economic, consular, technological and scientific and cultural cooperation between Slovenia and Sri Lanka, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to sign the above Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Slovenia, during his official visit to be made to Slovenia from  04th to 08th September, 2016, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Relocation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7037",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Republic Building situated in Colombo Fort area, where the Ministry of Foreign Affairs is presently located, is a building constructed in the British Colonial Era and it has been identified as a heritage that should be preserved.  Accordingly, it is essential to shift  the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to another place and the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to get a land in extent of 2 Acres, situated at Jawatta Road, Colombo, allocated for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which has been identified as suitable to construct a new building for that Ministry, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Enforcement and Regulation of the activities related to the International Conventions pertaining to Wildlife Conservation, in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7036",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- By now, Sri Lanka has signed several International conventions relating  to Wildlife Conservation, however, specific legal provisions have not been provided for the formal implementation of the activities related to the said Conventions.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to amend the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance, in order to enable the Minister to make necessary regulations for the implementation of  International Conventions related to wildlife conservation signed by Sri Lanka, locally, including the activities relating to the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Declaration of 'The National Marine Resources Conservation Week'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7035",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The accumulation of non-decayable substances on beaches and marine regions directly or through canals causes adverse effects to the marine  ecosystems as well as to the related industries such as fishing and  tourism. Therefore, it is essential to formulate a systematic arrangement with public participation to protect the marine ecosystems as well the sustainability of  the related industries.  As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to declare the period from Saturday of the 3rd week to Saturday of the  4th week of September of every year as the 'National Marine Resources Conservation Week' simultaneously to the International Coastal Clean up Day, from this year onwards, to implement the coastal clean up and conservation programme with the participation and contribution  of the general public, school children, government and non-governmental organizations from 17th to 23rd of September, 2016 and also to conduct its national celebration at the coastal stretch of Mattakkuliya, Colombo, on 17th of September, 2016, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Proper Management of the use of Polythene to minimize environmental issues caused by Polythene",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7034",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The use of plastic and polythene related products is a common occurrence  in present day society and as such, a number of social, environmental, health and economic issues have emerged due to the improper use,  disposal and burning of such products.   The per capita use of plastic and polythene in Sri Lanka is approximately 0.5 kg per day and around five (05) lakhs of tonnes of polythene is imported to Sri Lanka annually.  Certain countries in the world have totally banned the use of polythene while some other countries have allowed the use of only  selected types of plastic material.  Taking into consideration, matters such as the need to control the adverse environmental effects caused due to the addition of plastic and polythene related products that take a long time to decay, to the environment as well as the engagement of a large number of employees in plastic and polythene related industries, the proposal made by  H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, for the appointment of a Committee of Experts to formulate a National Policy and an Action Plan pertaining to the use of polythene, plastic and biodegradable plastic in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-09-06-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-09-06",
    "description": "Controlling the Importation and the use of non-eco-friendly Asbestos in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7033",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-09-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Asbestos is used for numerous products such as roofing sheets, floor tiles, cement pipes, brake pads of vehicles, paper and ropes. The importation of blue asbestos (Crocidolite) to Sri Lanka, which was identified as a carcinogen by the World Health Organization (WHO),  has been banned since the year 1987 and by now all types of asbestos, including white asbestos (Chrysotile) which is most commonly used in Sri Lanka, have been identified as carcinogens by the WHO.  Around 80% of the white asbestos imported to Sri Lanka is used to manufacture roofing sheets.  Accordingly, with a view to minimizing the adverse effects caused to health through asbestos and improving public health, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to move towards cost effective substitutes and limit  the import, use and production of asbestos related products from 01-01-2018 and to formulate an action plan to totally ban the production of asbestos related products in the country by 01-01-2024,   was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Declaration of the Year 2017 as the Year of Poverty Alleviation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7032",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the pledge made through the Election Manifesto for the Presidential Election-2015, to create \u201ca nation that is suitable to live in\u201d (Pathirupa Desa) and according to the United Nations (UN) Sustainable Development Goals, the special focus of the Government is drawn towards poverty alleviation. It is important that the economic development agenda of the Government does not solely target economic growth but also to focuses attention on areas such as social security, reducing the disparity in income distribution, people being socially marginalized due to various reasons and the prevailing development disparities at provincial and district levels. Therefore, it is essential to give priority to rescuing people from poverty and fields related to that within the economic and social policy followed by the Government. Accordingly, identifying the necessity of having a macro arrangement for the purpose and giving priority to working with a collective approach, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena,  to declare the forthcoming Year 2017 as the 'Year of Alleviation of Poverty' and to monitor this programme through a Committee headed by H.E. the President and the Hon. Prime Minister and comprised of the relevant Ministers and other stakeholders, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Development Policy Funds (Private Sector Development, Governance Improvement and Fiscal Consolidation)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7031",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Focusing attention on the financial stability of Sri Lanka, development of public resources management and facilitating the competitiveness of private sector, the Japanese International Cooperation Agency (JICA) has agreed to provide funds for the implementation of government development measures to attain economic stability. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister Ranil Wickremasinghe, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to sign the Exchange of Notes with the Government of Japan, to obtain development policy funds of Japanese Yen 10,000 million (approximately Rs.14,453.2 million) under the terms and conditions favourable to the country and to enter into a loan agreement with the JICA, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Ratification of Paris Agreement by Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7030",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- 178 countries including Sri Lanka have placed their signatures to the Paris Agreement on Climate Change at the United Nations (UN) Headquarters, on 22nd April 2016.  It is expected to significantly reduce the impact and risk of Climate Change by making every effort to keep the increase of global temperature level well below 2 0C, relative to the pre-industrial era level, and not exceed 1.5 0C.  It is important for Sri Lanka, being an island nation which may be prey to adverse impacts of climate change such as prolonged droughts, flash floods, rise in sea levels, landslides and inundation of low lands, to become a party to such  Agreement and therefore, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, for the ratification of said the Paris Agreement by Sri Lanka and to proceed with related future action, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Establishing Japan-Sri Lanka Joint Comprehensive Partnership (JCP) Secretariat in Colombo and Tokyo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7029",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- A declaration on Joint Comprehensive Partnership was agreed upon by the Governments of Japan and Sri Lanka, during the Prime Minister's official visit to Japan in October 2015, covering the sectors of Advanced Agriculture, Science and Technology for Industry, Quality Infrastructure and Regional Development, Education and Human Resources Development and Civil Safety and Security.  Accordingly, with a view to facilitating for the purpose, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, and the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, for the establishment of Japan-Sri Lanka Joint Comprehensive Partnership (JCP) Secretariat in Colombo and in  Tokyo, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Using a Standardized term for the Sri Lanka 'Police' Department",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7028",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Police of Sri Lanka has been denominated under various terms during different eras. Under the Police Ordinance, No.16 of 1865 and the Departmental Orders it has been known as 'Sri Lanka Police Force', after 1945 it has been termed as the 'Sri Lanka Police Department' and since the year 1972 it has been known as the 'Sri Lanka Police Service'. The Sri Lanka Police Department commemorates its 150th anniversary this year and in this context, considering the need to use a standard term to address that department, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayaka, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to use the name 'Sri Lanka Police' hereinafter for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Construction of the Prison Complex, Jaffna - Phase II",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7027",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been designed to implement the project on construction of the Prison Complex in Pannai, Jaffna, to accommodate 1,000 detainees. The construction work of the Phase I of the project has been completed and declared opened with accommodation facilities for 130 inmates. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. D.M Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to commence the construction work of Phase II of the project, at an estimated cost of Rs.623.32 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Implementation of Short Term Priority Water Supply improvements for 3 BOI Zones and surroundings in Ranpokunugama, Kirindiwela and Biyagama areas of Gampaha District and Koggala area of Galle District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7026",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to carry out the necessary improvements to the existing water supply schemes in the relevant areas, treating them as national priority projects, at an estimated cost of Rs.1,531.9 million, to ensure an adequate supply of drinking water to the people living in the BOI Zone of Biyagama, Wathupitiwala and Koggala and suburbs in the Biyagama area and the areas of Ranpokunagama, Kirindiwela and Habaraduwa, was approved in principle by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Implementation of Three Water Supply Schemes for the provision of drinking water to the people of the areas affected due to the water leakage that occurred in the main tunnel of Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7025",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted approval for the implementation of three (03) water supply schemes for the provisions of purified drinking water to the people living in the areas of Weheragalatenna, Makul-ella and Kurundugolla which were affected due to the water leakage that occurred in the main tunnel of Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Project. Accordingly, the construction activities of the said projects have been commenced and it has been revealed that the number of beneficiary families including the families living close to the water resources have increased up to 2,400 from 1417.  Therefore, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to revise the cost involved for the above mentioned 03 water supply schemes as Rs.317.24 million, and implement the said projects expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Task Force on Legal and Judicial Causes of Prison Overcrowding",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7024",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tThe joint proposal made by Hon.(Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice; and Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to establish a Task Force co-chaired by the Secretary, Ministry of Justice;  and the Secretary, Ministry of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs with the representation of the representatives of other institutions including the relevant Departments, to identify the legal and judicial causes of prison overcrowding and to obtain proposals on amendments to be made to the existing laws and procedures from the above Task Force, for the reduction of overcrowding prevalent in the Prisons, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Prevention of Coastal Erosion that occurs in the areas of Oluvil and Ninthavur in the Ampara District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7023",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per a proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, an Officials' Committee has already been appointed to study and submit recommendations on finding long term solutions for the prevention of severe coastal erosion that takes place in an area of around 550 meters of coastal stretch situated north of Oluvil Port in the Ampara District and providing relief to the people affected by  the said erosion. The Sri Lanka Ports Authority has already initiated the conservation activities of an area of 150 meters along this coastal stretch and the balance portion of about 400 meters has to be conserved very early.  Since long term conservation methodologies will take time, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to carry out expeditious steps of raising obstructing sand mounds along the coastal stretch and the erecting stone ridges as remedial measures, with the assistance of the Coast Conservation and Coastal Resources Management Department, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Development of Farms belonging to the National Livestock Development Board (NLDB) under the Public-Private Partnership Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7022",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- There are 31 crop and livestock farms across the island belonging to the National Livestock Development Board (NLDB) that contribute to the provision of necessary patronage to small scale farmers, national dairy production, meat production and the egg production process. Although the 04 large scale diary farms of the NLDB situated in Central and Southern Provinces have been developed, investing a large sum of money, it has been found difficult to obtain necessary funds to develop other farms with similar potential. Therefore, the focus of the Government has been drawn towards the development of such farms in collaboration with the private sector.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, to amend to the State Agricultural Corporation Act, No.11 of 1972, incorporating the legal provisions required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Leasing out of a block of land of 10 Acres at Muthurajawela for a Project for generating Energy out of Solid Waste",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7021",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to lease out a block of land in extent of 10 acres situated in Muthurajawela area, belonging to the Sri Lanka Land Reclamation and Development Corporation, to a private company, on a 30 year lease basis, for the implementation of a project for energy generation out of solid waste, as a solution to the issue on generating of solid waste disposal, was approved by the Cabinet in principle."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Registration of Motor Cycles which are being driven without registration",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7020",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Motor Cycles which are not registered in the Department of Motor Traffic can be commonly found in the country. These motor cycles which are frequently used in areas where public transport facilities are low, render a sufficient contribution to the agricultural economy of the rural areas while many of such motor cycles are also used by self-employed persons. Although, such motor cycles make a sufficient contribution to the rural economy, the Government annually loses a considerable income due to non-registration and it has been identified that it would be appropriate to grant an opportunity to register these motor cycles by imposing a surcharge, in order to suppress frauds, corruption and thefts and establish the rule of law in the country.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to allow registration as a concession after inspection of motor cycles without legal documents, to implement it in a manner without causing prejudice to legitimate motor cycle importers and in conformity with the provisions of the Motor Traffic Act and to grant this relief only for a period of four (04) months, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-08-30",
    "description": "Obtaining Membership of International Sustainable Tourism and Eliminating Poverty (ST-EP) Organization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7019",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to obtain the membership of International Organization on Sustainable Tourism - Eliminating Poverty (ST-EP) by Sri Lanka which is proposed to be established under the patronage of UN World Tourism Organization (UNWTO), with the main objectives of facilitating knowledge management and project development for economic improvement through tourism promotion, undertaking researches and projects for achieving sustainable tourism development through elimination of poverty and contributing for the protection of culture and nature through public\u2011private partnership, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Establishment of the National Media Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7018",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- On implementing the state mechanism, the timely dissemination of complete, reliable and accurate official information to the general public is a main responsibility of the Government, and it has been further ensured through the  provisions of the recently enacted Right to Information Act. As a one more step in this direction, with a view to ensuring the implementation of the principles of  Good Governance in a more enhanced manner, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickramasinghe, the Prime Minister, for the establishment of a 'National Media Centre', which would function as the Official Media Spokesman of the Government in disseminating official government information to both electronic and print media and coordinating information, while obtaining the views of the general public for policy formulation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Construction of Quarters for the Married Special Task Force (STF) Officers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7017",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The provision of housing facilities for married officers engaged in security activities such as maintaining law and order in the City of Colombo and suburbs, controlling riots and commotions that arise on various occasions, and providing  quick relief in disaster situations has become an urgent need and accordingly, in order to provide housing facilities for the said officers, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayaka, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to construct a housing complex, at an estimated cost of Rs.388 million, utilizing the space and facilities available at the Kalapaluwawa Camp of the Special Task Force (STF), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Award of Contract for the Construction of Habarana-Veyangoda 220kV Transmission Line",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7016",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the construction of Habarana- Veyangoda 220 KV Transmission Line - (Lot B), funded by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Construction of a New Three-Storeyed Building for the Divisional Secretariat, - Haliela",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7015",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Divisional Secretariat, Haliela, situated in Badulla District, comprises of 57 Grama Niladhari Divisions and has a population exceeding 90,000. The Haliela Divisional Secretariat Office is presently housed in a very old building with minimum space and facilities, and as a result, the general public who come to receive its services are faced with various difficulties. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to construct a three-storeyed building for the Divisional Secretariat, Haliela, at an estimated cost of Rs.176 million, in order to provide an efficient and effective service to the people of Haliela area as well as to provide a conducive work environment to the staff, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Ratnapura Expressway Project - Obtaining of Proposals for the Procurement of Civil Work Contracts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7014",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The feasibility studies, preliminary designs and the environment impact assessments are underway, in respect of the proposed Ratnapura Expressway, 73.9 km in length, which is designed to run from Kahatuduwa Interchange of the Southern Expressway to Pelmadulla. The Export and Import Bank (EXIM) of China has agreed to provide funds for the civil construction works of this expressway.  As per the recommendation of the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management (CCEM), the expressway is scheduled to be constructed under four (04) sections and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to call for bids on technical and financial proposals in respect of each road section, from the companies recommended by the Chinese Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Development of Infrastructure Facilities of the Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education, Jaffna",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7013",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the contract for construction of a four (04) storied building complex for the Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education, Jaffna, as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Central Expressway Project - Construction of Phase 03 from Pothuhera to Galagedara (32.5 km) and the Receipt of Bids and Proposals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7012",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways to call for bids and proposals as per recommendations of the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management (CCEM), to select a suitable contractor and a consultant for the construction activities of Phase 03 of the Central Expressway from Pothuhera to Galagedara (32.5 km), to be constructed under the financial assistance of Japan International Cooperation Corporation Agency (JICA), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Construction of Roads in the Downstream Development Areas under the Moragahakanda - Kaluganga Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7011",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to resettle the families affected by the Moragahakanda - Kaluganga Development Project as well as to reap the full benefits of the project, it is of utmost importance to develop the irrigation and infrastructure facilities in the downstream area of the said reservoirs. Therefore, the proposal made by H.E. the President, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to award the contracts for the construction of Moragahakanda-Wellawela Road (6.37 km), Medirigiriya-Kantale Road through Agbopura (8.5 km) and the construction of internal roads within the new Laggala Town (road surfacing), which are essential road development works, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Supply of Uniform and other Clothing Material for the Sri Lanka Army, Navy,  Air Force and Civil Security Force for the Year 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7010",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The textile requirements of the three forces and the other institutions under the Ministry of Defence have been met by local textile manufactures since the year 2005 and the relevant activities are carried out by the Domestic Textile Allocation Committee (DTAC) established under the Ministry of Industry and Commerce. Accordingly, the proposal made by H. E. the President, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, for the purchase of uniform material and other textile requirements of the Sri Lanka Army, the Sri Lanka Navy, the Sri Lanka Air Force and the Civil Security Force for the year 2016, from the relevant local textile manufactures, as recommended by the Domestic Textile Allocation Committee (DTAC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Obtaining Fishnet Products required for distribution among the fishermen from the Northsea Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7009",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The joint proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs and Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to purchase from North-Sea Ltd., a 100% State owned Company, the fishing nets required annually by the Department of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources for subsidy distribution among fishermen, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "International Religious Conference - To be held in Colombo in November 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7008",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the timely need to create peaceful co-existence, religious tolerance, multi-cultural reflection as well as reconciliation among the races, through religious harmony and understanding, the Cabinet has already granted approval to hold two International Religious Conferences in Sri Lanka.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. M.H.A. Haleem, the Minister of Posts, Postal Services and Muslim Religious Affairs, to provide the funds required for the organizing activities of the International Religious Conference to be held in Colombo in November 2016, under the theme 'Role of Religion in Pluralistic and Democratic Societies in South and South East Asia: Perspectives of Islam' with the participation of high level local and foreign dignitaries including Heads of State of 16 Countries, was approved in principle by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-08-23-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-08-23",
    "description": "Construction of the Proposed Dedicated Economic Centre, Vavuniya at Two Places and the Obtaining of Consultancy Services",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7007",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-08-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The responsibility of selecting a suitable place for the construction of the Dedicated Economic Centre, Vavuniya, in accordance with the Budget proposal 2016, was vested with the District Development Committee of Vavuniya.  Considering the representations made by various parties and the necessity of  completing the salient construction work concerned within the year by utilizing the relevant budgetary allocations, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, as per the recommendation of the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management (CCEM), to construct two Dedicated Economic Centres at Mankulam in the Mullaitivu District and at Mathauwaithakulam in the Vavuniya District, instead of one Dedicated Economic Centre,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
