    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-04-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the Government of Sri Lanka and the People's Republic of China in the field of Tourism Cooperation, during the forthcoming official visit to China by the Hon. Prime Minister, as proposed at its 7th meeting of the China - Sri Lanka Joint Committee on Economic Cooperation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-30-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2016-03-30",
    "description": "Recent Power Blackout and Supply of Electricity without interruption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6679",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- After a comprehensive discussion regarding the recent power blackout and the measures to be taken for the provision of Electricity without interruption in future, the Cabinet reached the following decisions: \n\n(i)\tto implement recommendations in the Reports submitted by  the Committees appointed to examine the simultaneous Power Blackout in the country and make recommendations by H.E. the President with the Chairmanship of the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy and by the Hon. Prime Minister with the Chairmanship of Mr. C. Maliyadde.\n\n(ii)\tto take necessary action to purchase the electricity power, only absolutely necessary, from the private sector in order to face the power generation limits that could be arisen, if there is no adequate rain in the coming days."
  },
  {
