    "doc_id": "2015-12-02-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2015-12-02",
    "description": "Cabinet Sub-Committee on Constitutional Reforms",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6440",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-12-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the decision taken taken at the Cabinet meeting held on 2015-11-18 to appoint a Cabinet Sub-Committee chaired by the Hon. Prime Minister, to submit recommendations pertaining to the methodology to be followed and the Constitutional changes to be made in order to implement the proposal presented by H.E. the President to draft necessary Constitutional provisions to abolish the Executive Presidency and amend the Electoral System, the proposal made by the Prime Minister, Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, in his capacity as the Chairman of the said Sub-Committee, to appoint the following Cabinet Ministers to the said Sub-Committee, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n\t* Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva\n\t* Hon. Lakshman Kiriella\n\t* Hon. Rauff Hakeem\n\t* Hon. Susil Premajayantha\n\t* Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen\n\t* Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka\n\t* Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa\n\t* Hon. D.M. Swaminathan\n\t* Hon. Mano Ganeshan\n\t* Hon. Malik Samarawickrama"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-12-02-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2015-12-02",
    "description": "Completion of the Remaining Construction Work of the District Secretariat Building, Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6439",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-12-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the purpose of establishing the government institutions which provide  services to the general public of Colombo district under one roof, the Colombo District Secretariat is being built with 20 storeys in the Narahenpita area, and most of its construction work has already been completed. By now, several government offices carry out their services within this building and therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to take necessary steps to complete the remaining construction work expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
