    "doc_id": "2015-09-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-09-09",
    "description": "Mid Year Fiscal Position Report - 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6276",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Section 10 of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No.3 of 2003, the Minister of Finance is required to issue the  Mid Year Fiscal Position Report to the general public by 30th June of every financial year and thereafter, to table it in Parliament. Accordingly, the proposal made by  Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to present 'the Mid Year Fiscal Position Report - 2015' which provides analyses of the macroeconomic situation of the country and the global economic trends and a detailed explanation on fiscal developments along with the updated information on the government's fiscal position pertaining to the first four (04) months of 2015, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2015-09-09",
    "description": "Implementation of the Polgahawela, Pothuhera and Alawwa Integrated Water Supply Project and the Kundasale \u2013 Haragama Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6275",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The rapid urbanization, increasing commercial activities and the industrial zones have intensified the necessity of highly standardized water supply projects. Accordingly, the Government has planned to implement the Polgahawela, Pothuhera and Alawwa Integrated Water Supply Project and the Kunadasale \u2013 Haragama Water Supply Project at an estimated cost of US$ 280.1 million. The water source of Polgahawela, Pothuhera and Alawwa Integrated Water Supply Project is Ma Oya and the four Divisional Secretariat Divisions of  Polgahawela, Alawwa, Kurunegala (Part) and Weerambugedara will be covered through this project. A distribution network of 380 km will be established, meeting the present water supply demand of 10,000 m\u00b3 per day by providing 50,000 new water connections to 250,000 houses through the  Kunadasale \u2013 Haragama Water Supply Project. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister Ranil Wickramasinghe, to obtain funds for the implementation of the above projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2015-09-09",
    "description": "Rationalization of Government Procurement Procedure",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6274",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- A vast amount of money from the Government annual expenditure is spent on the purchasing of goods and services required to provide various services to the general public, such as constructions carried out under various development projects, procurement of capital goods and pharmaceuticals, fertilizer subsidies, text books and uniforms for school children. These purchases are done according to the Government Procurement Procedure and it is observed that the government has to face inordinate delays and disadvantages due to some shortcomings found in the procedure. Hence, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to appoint a Committee comprising of the proficient retired Public Service Officials who possess experience in this field, to submit suitable proposals to make the existing Government Procurement Procedure more efficient and effective, for the utilization of the Government funds more frugally in a manner so as to prevent waste and also to avoid fraud, corruption and irregularities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2015-09-09",
    "description": "\"Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa\" - District Development Programme - 2016 - 2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6273",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Polonnaruwa District which forms a part of Rajarata area of 07 Divisional Secretariat Divisions and 295 Grama Niladhari Divisions. The infrastructure facilities, which are basically limited to the urban area are inadequate to meet the present day needs of the community and the infrastructure facilities such as health, education and roads available in the rural areas are of a very low standard. Especially, the infrastructure facilities available in the Divisional Secretariat Divisions of Welikanda, Dimbulagala, Medirigiriya and Lankapura affected by conflict situation which prevailed in the North and East are in a very poor state. As such, the people in the Polonnaruwa District lead a difficult life and are becoming more inclined to avail themselves of various services they need  from the adjoining districts. \n\nUnder the above five year programme, it has been proposed to implement number of various development projects in the district at a cost of Rs.60 billion and out of which the Cabinet approval has already been granted to implement the Drinking Water Project and the Project on construction of a Hospital for Kidney Patients. It is expected to finance number of projects under  this programme through the personal donations obtained from the local and foreign parties. \n\nSeveral projects in the sectors such as Education, Health and Rural Roads which have been identified to be implemented expeditiously under the proposed five year plan, are anticipated to be initiated in the year 2015 and it has been estimated that these projects would involve a cost of approximately, Rs.750 million. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement the proposed District Development Programme -  \"Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa\" during the period of 2016 - 2020, and to initiate the projects that should be commenced expeditiously under the programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Procurement of Fertilizer for the Year 2015 (October Delivery)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6272",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The supply of fertilizer to the farmers on a subsidy scheme  under the Fertilizer Subsidy Programme is being implemented by the Department of Agriculture. The required quantity of fertilizer will be supplied through the Government owned fertilizer companies, namely the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Limited (CFC) and the Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Limited, in par with the monthly requirement.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to award the relevant contracts for the supply of the necessary quantity of fertilizer through above companies, as recommended by the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SSCAPC), to distribute among farmers, for the month of October 2015, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Rehabilitation of the Railway Track between Maho / Vavuniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6271",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The primary objective of the Sri Lanka Railways is to provide a safe,  reliable and punctual Rail Transport Service for passengers and for freight traffic. It has been identified by the Government, that a systematic improvement of the railway track is an essential factor for achieving the said objective. Considering the importance of the improvement to the railway road section between Mahawa and Vavuniya, with the railway tracks constructed newly beyond Vavuniya under the Northern Railway track development activities carried out recently, the Sri Lanka Railways Department has planned to rehabilitate the said track of 120.7 km (inclusive of the 5 km loop line).  Accordingly, the Mahawa - Vavuniya Railway Track will be developed and the section between the Anuradhapura - Vavuniya (49.4 km) is to be rehabilitated as its First Phase and the section between Mahawa - Anuradhapura (66.4 km) is to be rehabilitated as its Second Phase.  The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Internal Transport, to carry out the rehabilitation activities through procuring track materials including concrete sleepers required for the purpose and the necessary equipments locally, as wherever possible and utilizing the manpower  of the Department, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Purchasing of Diagnostic Medical Imaging Equipment for Epilepsy Unit at the National Hospital of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6270",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- As another measure of providing an effective health service to the public, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to award the relevant contracts, to purchase a MRI Scanner, a SPECT Scanner, a PET-CT Scanner each for the Epilepsy Unit and to install a Digital Subtraction Angiography (DSA) System at the National Hospital and to select relevant companies to maintain the said equipments in  future, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Renovation of Intensive Care Unit of Renal Dialysis & Transplant Unit at Maligawatta",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6269",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Renal Dialysis & Transplant Unit at Maligawatta provides an invaluable patient care service to the patients coming from all over the country. The Intensive Care Unit and the Isolation Unit of this hospital are also housed in the residential patients' ward.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to renovate the Intensive Care Unit (ICU) expeditiously, with a view to minimize the vulnerability of patients, for infections, through the retention of such patients in the ICU after the surgeries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Investigation on Corruptions, Mal-administration and Irregularities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6268",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by the Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Internal Transport to consult the Attorney General's Department, to institute legal actions against the responsible institutions and persons, in accordance with the Report pertaining to the following matters submitted by the Special Investigation Committee appointed by the Secretary to the Ministry, on a directive made by the Minister of Internal Transport, to make investigations into corruption, maladministration and irregularities said to have been taken place during the past five year period in the Ministry and its affiliated institutions and to avoid occurrence of such situations in future, was approved by the Cabinet:  \r\n\r\n*\tNon-recovery of a sum of Rs.142 million for the buses hired by the Sri Lanka Transport Board (SLTB), for the presidential election-2015.  \r\n\r\n*\tNon-receipt of the discount offered in procuring 2,200 new buses for the SLTB. \r\n\r\n*\tLoosing the anticipated quality and the import duty concessions to the SLTB when purchasing spare parts. \r\n\r\n*\tOperation of private buses under SLTB logo. \r\n\r\n*\tOperation of 20 luxury buses imported for the Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting, by the Road Development Authority. \r\n\r\n*\tIssues with regard to enormous cost and the estimates in the construction of the Northern Railway Line. \r\n\r\n*\tSubmission of estimates with an enormous cost in the construction of the Matara - Kataragama Railway Line. \r\n\r\n*\tVesting and leasing out lands owned by the Railway Department, to the external institutions and persons,  deviating from the formal procedure. \r\n\r\n*\tOperation of rail carriages/special trains with private sector participation and loses incurred in the operation of the Vice Roy special train. \r\n\r\n*\tSale of scrap iron deviating from the accepted procedure."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "\u2018Sri Lanka Expo 2016\u2019 to be held from 15th - 17th September, 2016 at the BMICH, Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6267",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Organizing of International Expositions to showcase the country's export capabilities while facilitating Sri Lankan producers, exporters and service providers to meet the prospective international buyers, partners and potential investors is one of the strategic promotional tools. In the back-drop of the special political and economic developments taken place recently in the country, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen,  the Minister of Industry and Commerce to hold the 'Sri Lanka Expo - 2016' from 15th - 17th September 2016 at BMICH, Colombo, enabling concerned parties to obtain valuable business experience with a combination of events such as  expositions, seminars, meetings, programmes conducted simultaneously and visits to factories, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between the Government Analyst\u2019s Department of Sri Lanka and the National Forensic Service of the Republic of Korea",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6266",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to sign a MOU between the Government Analyst's Department of Sri Lanka and the National Forensic Service of the Republic of Korea to extend cooperation on matters as follows, was approved by the Cabinet: \r\n\r\n*\tPromotion of the standards of the Forensic testing of the Government Analyst's Department in order to achieve excellence in the process of investigations into criminal matters in Sri Lanka; \r\n\r\n*\tInstallation of new methodologies for the advancement of laboratory testing in the field of forensic science including new researches,   examination of questioned documents, forensic toxicology, analysis of narcotics, firearms and explosives  and the most modern analysis of DNA; \r\n\r\n*\tSharing the knowledge on testing methods pertaining to criminal investigations, the knowledge of the experts in the field, theoretical and practical knowledge in the conduct of criminal investigations; \r\n\r\n*\tExchange of knowledge mutually through workshops, seminars, training programmes and meetings conducted by experts; \r\n\r\n*\tGranting assistance in the purchase of state-of-the-art laboratory equipment and tools; and  \r\n\r\n*\tEnsuring the international level of \"Accredited Testing Samples\" and the standards of the laboratories in the Government Analyst's Department."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Incorporating the Divi Neguma Social Security Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6265",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Samurdhi Social Security Fund established under the Samurdhi Programme which commenced with a view to alleviating poverty of the low income earners is implemented with effect from 1st January 1997 and its  objective is to extend financial assistance to Samurdhi beneficiaries beset with unexpected problems during their journey towards economic development. As of now, 1,478,288 families receive monthly Samurdhi subsidy and a contribution of Rs.45/- out of it is debited to this Fund.  Having taken into consideration the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Samurdhi, to incorporate the said Fund, the approval of the Cabinet was granted to operate the said Fund as a Trust under the Trust Ordinance until it is formally incorporated."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Protocol of Phytosanitary Requirements for the Export of Banana from Sri Lanka to China between the General Administration of Quality Supervision, Inspection and Quarantine of China and the Ministry of Agriculture of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6264",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Banana is being cultivated successfully in Sri Lanka as if suits with the climatic and environmental conditions prevail in the Country and it is a crop which could be used to meet the local food requirements and to generate export income. There is a healthy potential for the exportation of banana to China through developing trade relations with China, a friendly country of Sri Lanka. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to enter into an Agreement with the General Administration on Quality Supervision, Inspection and Plant Quarantine of China, enabling Sri Lanka to export banana to China complying with laws and regulations on phytosanitary requirements and to provide information on banana cultivation lands and localise packing houses, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Purchasing of Plasma from the National Blood Transfusion Service in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6263",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- No substitute has yet been found for blood and the blood necessary for transfusion is obtained from the donors.  Although, blood used to be transfused as \u201cwhole blood\u201d up to recent times, the situation has now changed. If one unit of blood could be separated accurately as recommended, there is a possibility of deriving up to four components out of it.  As such, a patient can be given only the portion of blood he needs and the balance components can be given to other patients who need them.  The National Blood Transfusion Service (NBTS) collects 100,000 litres of Plasma, annually, from the donors and after the separation of components the NBTS utilizes only around 60,000 units out of them for the clinical use.  Since the facilities are not available with the NBTS to separate a large number of components there is the possibility of providing the balance quantity of 40,000 litres which is currently discarded,  to the companies which possess the technology of producing Plasma Protein.  Although, the situation is such, the Plasma Protein requirement of Sri Lanka is imported from the foreign companies / institutions which produce Plasma Protein incurring a heavy expenditure.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to give the excess quantity of Plasma for Plasma Protein production, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Development Project of National Hospital Health Square \u2013 Providing Houses for the unauthorized settlers in Bosevanawatte",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6262",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cardiology Unit of the Sri Lanka National Hospital provides an invaluable patient care service to the heart patients of the country.  However, the building complex where the Cardiology Unit is housed is very old and the space available in the building is not at all sufficient, in considering the services currently provided by the Unit.  As such, the health staff as well as the patients under go excessive difficulties.  As a remedy, the Cardiology Unit should be extended,  but the prevailing land is inadequate for the purpose.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to utilize the adjacent land called 'Bosevanawatte' to improve the required facilities of the Cardiology Unit, by providing the unauthorized settlers reside in the said land with the alternative houses from a Multi-storeyed Housing Project is being constructed at another place under the Urban Regeneration Project of  Urban Development Authority, in lieu of the 63 housing units of the said unauthorized settlers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Agreement on Exemption from Visa Requirements for Holders of Diplomatic and Official / Service Passports between the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Republic of Kazakhstan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6261",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The purpose of entering into this Agreement is to further strengthen the friendly relations between two countries and to simplify the relevant procedures to facilitate the movement of citizens of Sri Lanka and Kazakhstan between the two countries. The permission is granted for the Nationals of States of one Party, holders of valid diplomatic or service/official passports to enter, leave and transit through the territory of the  State of the other Party without obtaining visas for a period of thirty (30) days, through this Agreement. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Public Order and Christian Affairs, to enter into the above Agreement between Sri Lanka and Kazakhstan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Archaeological Heritage Management in the Rajagala Archaeological Reserve",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6260",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Rajagalatenna Ancient Ariyakara Viharaya situated in the Uhana Divisional Secretariat Division of the Ampara District of the Eastern Province is considered to be established by the King Lajjitissa.  The ruins of this monastery which is believed to be a combination of a Pabbatha Vihara and a forest monastery type are scattered in an area of 1,025 acres.  The ashes of the great Arahath Mahinda is said to be interred in a Stupa found in the premises. The Rajagala Archaeological Project is being carried out as a joint project of the Department of Archaeology and the University of Sri Jayawardenapura since 2012, to arrest the deterioration process of the archeological remains in this monastery and to conserve them in order to secure them sustainably in the future and for the developemnt of the Heritage Tourism Programme. \r\n\r\n\tThe total estimated cost of this project is Rs.323.8 million and the sum spent on the project  up to the end of 2014 amounts to Rs.55.5 million including the funds provided for by the American Embassy Fund and the University of Sri Jayawardenapura. The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister and the Minister of Policy Planning, Economic Affairs, Child, Youth and Cultural Affairs, to obtain a sum of Rs. 268.3 million required for the completion of these project, from the Government Consolidated Fund,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Establishement of a Wastewater Management System for the Negombo town area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6259",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- As far as Sri Lanka wastewater management sector is concerned, only 2.4% of the Sri Lankan population is connected to a collective wastewater management system and the vast majority of the population uses individual sanitation systems.  In reality, most of the existing collective systems are out dated and poorly maintained.  This has decreased their efficient functioning. Therefore, under treated wastewater is discharged into drainage channels and this has brought adverse consequences for both the public health and the environment. Considering the prevailing situation, the 'Sanitation and  Hygiene Initiative for Towns' (SHIFT) Project has been initiated to establish three collective wastewater management systems for Negombo, Galle and Kelaniya - Peliyagoda areas.  \r\n\r\n\tUnder first phase of this project, it is expected to establish a wastewater management system for the Negombo Urban Area at a cost of Euro 107 million and the Agence Francaise De Development (AFD) has agreed to provide a financial facility of Euro 76 million for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Minister of Policy Planning, Economic Affairs, Child, Youth and Cultural Affairs, to enter into an agreement with AFD of France, for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Resettlement of Families affected due to acquiring of lands for Moragahakanda - Kaluganga Agricultural Development Project - the increase of families due to the delay of the project - Revision of benefits including approval of alternative proposals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6258",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "Moragahakanda - Kaluganga Agricultural Development Project was commenced in 2008 and it has been identified that the 1,747 families of 12 Grama Niladari Divisions in Naula Divisional Secretary's Division and 907 families of 11 Grama Niladari Divisions in Laggala Pallegama Divisional Secretary's Division will be affected in the implementation of the said project. However, the following issues have arisen due to the delay in the implementation of the project by 8 years:   \r\n\r\n*\tSince the new marriages have taken place within the families to be affected, another 224 families have been added to the earlier number, as families to be affected. \r\n\r\n*\treluctance of the newly added families, to leave the area \tand settle down in Medirigiriya. \r\n\r\n*\tthe expression of unwillingness by 345 families which consented to settle down in Medirigiriya in the year 2007 to go and live in the said area.  \r\n\r\n*\tthe alternative lands have to be provided with the newly added families who have expressed their unwillingness to settle down in Medirigiriya area. \r\n\r\nThe proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripla Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment,  to acquire the lands identified to be given to the famiies to be added under above project belonging to the Government Owned Plantation Companies situated in the relevant area and suburbs, to pay compensation for the lands owned by such families and to provide assistance for building houses in alternative lands, as a remedy to solve the above issues, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Project on Construction of Defence Headquarters Complex at Akuregoda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6257",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- An Officials' Committee has been appointed, by the Cabinet to investigate into the activities of the Defence Headquarters Complex which is being constructed at Akuregoda, Battaramulla, and to report on same.  The attention of the Cabinet was drawn to the following facts mentioned in the Officials' Committee Report, with regard to a company to which the consultancy services of this project have been awarded, that is,  \r\n\r\n*\tthe company has been selected without calling competitive bids; \r\n\r\n*\tthe company has been registered under the Registrar of Companies and under the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects, only after it has been selected  for consultancy services; \r\n\r\n* \tthe  authorities concerned have not entered into a formal Agreement, to obtain services of the said company; \r\n\r\n* \tit has been decided to pay the said company Rs.606.032 million in cash, for the consultancy services of the entire project; Although, the company has been paid Rs.509.926 million as at 2015-05-31, (83% of the total payment) it has only completed 30.02% of the entire work of the project as of now. \r\n\r\n\tThe Cabinet decided to investigate into the above facts mentioned in the Officials' Committee Report pertaining to the Consultancy Services Company and to take legal action, on the findings of the  said investigation, as appropriate."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Modernization of Infrastructure Facilities of Multi Storeyed Housing Schemes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6256",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, Minister of Housing and Samurdhi, to renovate the public roads and rain water drainage systems in the following 13 Housing Schemes where 1700 families reside, at a cost of Rs.143.29 million, under the Programme of Modernization of Infrastructure Facilities of Multi Storeyed Housing Schemes in Colombo City, was approved by the Cabinet. \r\n\r\nBolamesawatta Housing Scheme\r\nVeluwanarama Housing Scheme\r\nElvitigala Housing Scheme\r\nMallikarama Housing Scheme\r\nCentral Road Housing Scheme\r\nKammalwatta Housing Scheme\r\nJumma Masjid Housing Scheme\r\nDissanayakewatta Housing Scheme\r\nAluth Mawatha Housing Scheme\r\nDias Place Housing Scheme\r\nBloemandhal Housing Scheme\r\nSt. James Street Housing Scheme\r\nAluthkada Housing Scheme"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "The present status of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6255",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Hon. Ranil Wickramasinghe, the Prime Minister, brought to the notice of the Cabinet the situation that has arisen in the CIABOC, as a result of the failure on the part of the Chairman and the Commissioners of the CIABOC, who have been appointed to the said posts by the previous Government, to provide necessary guidance and cooperation to conduct its operations properly.  As the functions of the Commission has been utterly blocked due to the conduct of its Chairman and Commissioners, and as such, the Cabinet noted the difficulty of taking legal action against the large number of complaints where the investigations have been concluded."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Preparation of Budget \u2013 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6254",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Hon. Ravi Karunayake, the Minister of Finance, brought to the notice of the Cabinet that it has been planned to prepare the Budget for the year 2016, with a view to achieving the following objectives: \r\n\r\n*\tto limit the Budget deficit to 5.5% of Gross Domestic Production (GDP); \r\n\r\n*\tto maintain the public investments around 6% - 8% of GDP; \r\n\r\n*\tto encourage the private investments to reach around 22% - 24% of GDP; \r\n\r\n* \tto raise the total investment level of the economy up to 30% of GDP; and \r\n\r\n*\tto achieve an economic growth rate beyond 8% during the  Medium Term Framework of 2016 \u2013 2018; \r\n\r\n\tThe Government, while successfully achieving the challenge of settling the unsettled liabilities accumulated for a long period, and creating a better treasury management system, has decided to introduce a Zero Based Budgeting Method as a tool of budget preparation and implementation from 2016 onwards. Accordingly, the Cabinet noted that it has been planned to prepare the Budget 2016 allocating the resources based on the sectoral ceilings, and the arrangements have been made to issue the 'Budget Call 2016' incorporating the guidelines and instructions for preparation of this year's Budget and that action will be taken to conduct preliminary discussions with the Ministries regarding the preparation of the Budget 2016 from first week of August 2015 onwards, on the information submitted by Hon. Ravi Karunayake, the Minister of Finance."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Removal of the Pensions Anomalies  of the Three Armed Forces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6253",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Public Administration Circular No.16/2015 has been issued in accordance with the  approval granted by the Cabinet on 2015?06?10, to adjust the pensions of the salary structure effective from 2006?01?01, to revise the pensions of those who retired before the year 2006 by removing their salary anomalies. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Karu Jayasuriya, the Minister of Public Administration, Local Government and Democratic Governance, to revise the pensions of those retired from the services of Three Armed Forces before the year 2006, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Obtaining Netherlands Assistance to finance the Development of General Hospital, Kalutara as a specialized Maternal and Children\u2019s Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6252",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2015?07?08, has granted approval to develop the General Hospital, Kalutara as a specialized Maternal and Children\u2019s Hospital and the Cabinet noted that the Government is to enter into two Agreements with the Rabo Bank of the Netherlands and the Hatton National Bank of Sri Lanka, to obtain a financial facility of Euro 28.7 million required for the purpose, on the information submitted by Hon. Ravi Karunayake, the Minister of Finance."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Printing of School Textbooks required for the year 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6251",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The main task of the Department of Educational Publications is to print  and duly distribute the textbooks required by all the school students and the student monks in Pirivenas, through out the Island, free of charge. Accordingly, the Cabinet has already been granted the approval to get it printed 13,210,600 copies of 80 types out of 410 books from the State Printing Corporation, Department of Government Printing and Associated Newspapers of Ceylon Limited, and the relevant printing orders have already been referred to the said Institutions. A further 30,862,500 copies of textbooks from 330 categories have to be printed during this year through the Private Printing Institutions. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to get 30,862,500 copies of textbooks from 330 categories printed from 19 printing institutions of private sector, to enable the textbooks prescribed for the year 2016 to be distributed in schools before 2015?12?03, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Implementation of Laggala and Wilgamuwa Water Supply Projects with funding secured from Local Banks with a Treasury Guarantee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6250",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Laggala and Wilgamuwa Water Supply Projects implemented by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board, under the supervision of the Ministry of Urban Development, Water Supply and Drainage, are expected to be completed by the year 2017. The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickramasinghe, the Minister of Policy Planning, Economic Affairs, Child, Youth and Cultural Affairs, to authorize the National Water Supply and Drainage Board, to secure the funds required for the implementation of the said two projects from the local banks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Development of Apparel and Allied Industries in Welioya and Musali Divisional Secretariat Divisions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6249",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has already been granted to establish Apparel and Allied Industries to elevate the income level and the living conditions of the unemployed and resettled people living in the Welioya and Musali Divisional Secretarys' Divisions. Although, the construction of  factories should be carried out through utilizing the funds of the investors, as per the said approval, it has not been able to achieve the task successfully as the investors are  reluctant to invest on such buildings, since these areas are situated in the remote districts such as Mullativu and Mannar.  \nAccording to a survey conducted, it has been revealed that over 2,500 workers in these two divisions are willing to employ in apparel industry, out of them 500 are skilled workers with experience in the field. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to construct three factories each on the lands identified in the Welioya and Musali Divisional Secretary Divisions, by the Government and to recover the expenditure incurred on factories from the investors as long term lease rental, based on the Government valuation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Construction of a new building to the Attorney General\u2019s Department",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6248",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "-Due to the inadequate space available in the present building, where the Attorney General's Department is housed, the construction work has been commenced to construct a seven storeyed new building for the Department, in the premises of the Superior Court Complex. The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to award the contract for the pilling work of the building, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Establishment of  Clinical Waste Management Systems for the hospitals in Sri Lanka, under the Australian Assistance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6247",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Lack of a proper management methodology for the disposal of clinical waste with infectious materials, without causing adverse effects to public health  is a serious problem faced by the hospitals in Sri Lanka. As such, the previous Cabinet has granted its approval for a proposal made voluntarily, to establish a formal clinical waste management system for the Government hospitals, under the Australian loan assistance. As per the recommendations made by the Committee appointed to review and report the project proposal, and by the Cabinet Sub-Committee on Economic Affairs, and taking into consideration the importance of such a project, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to implement the above project, subject to making changes to the scope of the project as appropriate,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "Completion of the remaining work of the New Baby Unit of the De Soyza Hospital for Women",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6246",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-07-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- De Soyza Hospital for Women situated in Kinsey Road, Colombo functions under the Ministry of Health provides an invaluable service to the pregnant mothers afflicted with complications, who come from various parts of the country. The buildings in which the hospital is housed are very old and inadequate space is a constraint to provide a quality service. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to entrust the work relating to the completion of the construction of the new Baby Unit which includes the Premature Baby Care Unit expeditiously, with the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau, on the design and build basis, at a cost of Rs.325.4 million, where the construction work has now been stopped owing to the negligence of the contractor who had started the construction work ten years ago, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-07-29-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2015-07-29",
    "description": "13. Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme",
