    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2015-06-10",
    "description": "MoU between the Coconut Research Institute of the Ministry of Plantation Industries of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Chinese Academy of Tropical Agricultural Sciences of the Coconut Research Institute of the People\u2019s Republic of China",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6115",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of the above MOU is to strengthen the co-operation in the field of coconut research and development between the two countries and to develop integrated coconut research and development programmes relating to scientific, technological and skill development prevalent in the sphere.  Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation Industries, Lakshman Kiriella, to obtain covering approval for the MOU entered into during H.E. President's visit to China in March this year and to implement the matters covered in the agreement within the next three (03) years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-06-10-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2015-06-10",
    "description": "Ratification of the United Nations Convention on the use of Electronic Communications in International Contracts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6114",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The above convention was prepared by the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law (UNCITRAL) and adopted by the United Nations General Assembly in the year 2005.  The objective of the Convention is to offer practical solutions for issues related to the use of electronic means of communication in connection with International contracts.  Sri Lanka has signed the Convention in the year 2006 and in the preparation of Sri Lankan Electronic Transactions Act No.19 of 2006, the features and underlying principles of the Convention have been included in the Act.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs, Mangala Samaraweera, to authorize the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to ratify the Convention, to empower  the Information and Communication Technology Agency (ICTA) to undertake a review of the Electronic Transactions Act No.19 of 2006 and make recommendations for such revisions as may be required to meet the obligations under the above Convention, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
