    "date_str": "2015-04-01",
    "description": "Amendment to the Penal Code",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6014",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Lessons Learnt and Reconciliation Commission (LLRC) was appointed with the mandate to have a flashback of the armed conflict that Sri Lanka experienced and to ensure the dawn of an era where reconciliation is built and issues involved are resolved on the experiences so gained.  The Commission has observed  the instances where \u201cHate Speech\u201d and statements relating to ethnicity and religion have aggravated ethnic and religious tensions in the past four or five decades. The Commission has recommended that tough laws be enacted to deal with such practices and these laws should strictly be enforced. The proposal made by Dr. Wijayadasa Rajapakshe, Minister of Justice, to publish the draft Bill in the Government Gazette as amended by the Legal Draftsman incorporating provisions in the Penal Code to prohibit and punish those who advocate religious and racial hatred and present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-01-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2015-04-01",
    "description": "Sri Lanka Energy Sector Development Plan for a Knowledge Based Economy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6013",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Energy Sector Development Plan has been developed with a view to making available the maximum contribution of the energy sector for the strength required for development drive which strides along competing at international levels, making Sri Lanka as knowledge based middle income economy.  The prime objective of this Plan is to  provide an affordable, high quality and reliable energy supply for all citizens irrespective of their being rich of poor, while preserving the environment and giving priority to the indigenous sources of energy and minimizing regional disparities.  The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, Minister of Power and Energy, to implement the development plan (2015-2025), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-01-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-04-01",
    "description": "Programme to Control Weligama Coconut Leaf Wilt and Rot Disease - 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6012",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Weligama Coconut Leaf Wilt and Rot Disease caused by a vector called \u201cPhytoplasma\u201d is a disease which brings destruction to  the coconut plantation.  This was first reported from the Weligama area in Matara district in the year 2006.  No decisive cure for the disease has yet been found in the world.  The disease is prevalent in 12 Divisional Secretary Divisions in the Matara District, 02 Divisional Secretary Divisions in the Hambantota District and 02 Divisional Secretary Divisions in the Galle District and the authorities have taken all necessary precautions to prevent the spread of the disease to other areas.  The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, Minister of Plantation Industries, to continue the implementation of the project to control the spread of the disease, for a further period of 03 years from 2015 to 2017, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
