    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2015-03-12",
    "description": "Proposed Administrative Procedure for granting Dual Citizenship",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5981",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, Minister of Public Order, Disaster Management and Christian Affairs, to grant dual citizenship under a new Administrative Procedure, was approved by the Cabinet.  Accordingly, individuals who satisfy at least one of the following qualifications are eligible to apply for dual citizenship: \n\n \t\t*\twho possesses professional or educational qualifications;\n*\twho owns immovable property worth of Rs.2.5 million or above;\n*\twho has a fixed deposit of Rs.2.5 million or above for a period of three (03) years in any Bank approved by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL);\n*\twho has fixed deposit of US$25,000 or above in NRFC/RFC/SFIDA accounts for a period of three (03) years in a Commercial Bank approved by the CBSL;\n*\twho has invested US$25,000 or above for three (03) years in a Treasury Bond or a Security Investment Account; and\n  \t\t*\ton attaining the age of 55 years.\n\n\tFurther, the spouse or unmarried children under the age of 22 years of the applicant are also eligible."
  },
  {
