    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, Minister of Women's Affairs, to extend the duration up to 30th June 2016 of the project which was initiated in the year 2010 on a Memorandum of Understanding signed with the Government of India to economically and socially strengthen the war affected women in the Batticoloa District through the implementation of various Entrepreneur Development Training Courses,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-03-04-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2015-03-04",
    "description": "Rs.20,000/- Nutritional Food Package for Pregnant Mothers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5972",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The above programme which was incorporated in the 100 Days Programme of the Government has been planned to be implemented as the \u201cHealthy Motherhood Programme\u201d effective from 21st March 2015 as proposed in the Budget Speech 2015. Accordingly - \n\n*\tall pregnant mothers, registered and regularly attending the Government Antenatal Clinics are eligible for the proposed allowance on the recommendation of the Doctors;\n*\tnutritional food will be provided under this programme in installments of Rs.2,000/= each for a period of ten months including the last six months of pregnancy and the first four months after the child birth;\n *\tthe programme will be implemented by the Divisional Secretaries with the assistance of the Medical Officers and the Family Health Officers serving in the antenatal clinics under the supervision of the respective District Secretary/Government Agent on the direction  of the State Ministry for Child Affairs.\n\n\tThe above proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister and the Minister of Policy Planning, Economic Affairs, Child, Youth and Cultural Affairs, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-03-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-03-04",
    "description": "Implementation of Warehouse Receipts Financing System for Storage of Farm Produce by Farmers in the Dry Zone Districts of the Country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5971",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction of warehouses in the districts of  Anuradhapura, Moneragala and Mannar, has been commenced under Phase I of the Warehouse Receipts Financing Mechanism introduced by the Government of Sri Lanka with a grant assistance from the World Bank, innovated a mechanism with a view to providing cultivators in the dry zone with high quality storage facilities to secure a higher income and profit for them by selling their produce in the off season rather than in the harvesting season and to providing them with financial assistance for the purpose. \n\n\tThe construction of the first warehouse under this programme inaugurated in the Divisional Secretary's Division of Galenbindunuwewa in the Anuradhapura district, has by now been completed and the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, Minister of Finance, to enter into a Management Service Agreement with the Divisional Development Bank and appoint the  District Secretary Anuradhapura, as the authorized operator thereof, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-03-04-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2015-03-04",
    "description": "Distribution of subsidized fertilizer for paddy cultivation during Yala Season 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5970",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "-The fertilizer subsidy provided for the paddy cultivation has resulted in high yields. Accordingly, the total extent of land envisaged for cultivation in the Yala season of 2015 is 540,000 hectares and the total  fertilizer requirement is estimated at 162,733 MT. Taking these facts into consideration, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, Minister of Irrigation and Agriculture, to implement the fertilizer subsidy scheme in the Yala Season 2015 and also to take necessary activities to purchase the required quantity of fertilizer ensuring its quality, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
