  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2014-12-23-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2014-12-23",
    "description": "Programme to strengthen Small and Medium Scale Millers and Stockists",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5909",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-12-23",
    "decision_details_body": "-  the small and medium scale millers and stockists contribute largely to the process of offering a government guaranteed price for paddy farmers and providing rice to consumers at an affordable price through purchasing paddy and also processing and distributing rice.  The monthly consumption of rice in the country is around 180,000 mt. and the small and medium scale millers and stockists have the capacity to produce 60% of the market requirement.  The Government intends to strengthen the small and medium scale millers and stockists financially and to provide immediate relief to settle their outstanding loans during the past due to natural calamities and loss of harvest.   Accordingly, the following proposals made by H.E. the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance and Planning, were approved by the Cabinet: \r\n  \r\n*\tto suspend legal action taken by State Banks against the defaulted pledge loans of small and medium scale millers and stockists;\r\n\r\n*\tto write off the outstanding loan balances of pledge loans for paddy purchasing obtained by them from  State Banks during the period from 1997 to 2010 and for the General Treasury to provide the required funds to the relevant banks;\r\n\r\n*\tto offer a grace period of six (06) months with effect from 2015?01?01 for the repayment of the pledge loans granted by State Banks for paddy purchasing in Maha 2013/2014 and Yala 2014;\r\n\r\n*\tto purchase Samba rice and other rice stocks processed by them, through Lanka Sathosa Limited at Rs.85/- and Rs.82/- per kg. respectively and to provide financial facilities to Lanka Sathosa Limited in this regard;\r\n\r\n\r\n*\tto provide transformers free of charge for them, considering their electricity capacity requirement and to bear the cost of same by the Government; and\r\n\r\n*\tto implement a new Loan Scheme for them with concessionary  interest rates to improve the paddy purchasing and storage capacity and to improve the quality of rice through introduction of modern technology."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2014-12-23-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2014-12-23",
    "description": "Increase of the Monthly Allowance paid to Trainees of Traditional Handicrafts Sector under the National Crafts Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5908",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-12-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- the National Crafts Council has undertaken many craft training programmes to strengthen the skills and capacity of the craftsmen and provides training in the 20 craft clusters of handicrafts industry at rural level through the Master Craftsman Training Programme since 1985 and in addition, through the Handicraft Training Centres since 2009.  Handicrafts which is a traditional national heritage, provides a formidable platform to showcase the culture of our country to the world.  The proposal made by Hon. Douglas Devananda, Minister of Traditional Industries and Small Enterprise Development, to increase the monthly allowance of Rs.500/- paid to trainees undergoing training in the handicrafts field under the National Crafts Council, to Rs.1,000/- was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
