    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- the two way trade between Sri Lanka and Russia has been increasing \tover \tthe\tyears.  Sri Lanka's exports to Russia have increased from US $11.6 million in 2001 to US $279.91 million in 2013 while Sri Lanka's imports from Russia have increased from US $3.7 million to US $145.85 million during the same period.  The proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, Ministry of Industry and Commerce, to enter into an Agreement on establishment of the Inter-governmental Commission on Trade, Economic, Scientific and Technical Cooperation, to enhance cooperation between the two countries in the said fields, was approved by the Cabinet."
