    "description": "Strengthening the Small and Medium Industrial Estates",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5092",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2013-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "the Ministry of  Traditional Industries and Small Enterprise Development has facilitated the Small and Medium Scale Enterprises/Industries spread out across the country through the establishment, operation and servicing of 18 Industrial Estates which are managed by the Industrial Development Board.  The proposal made by Hon. Douglas Devananda, Minister of Traditional Industries and Small Enterprise Development to adapt and adopt the lease rental policy recommendations to the Small and Medium Industrial Estates operated by the Industrial Development Board, to provide relief to all small and medium industrialists  with effect from 2011\u00a006\u00a001, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2013-06-20-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2013-06-20",
    "description": "Proposed Amendment to the Regulation of Insurance Industry Act No. 43 of 2000",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5091",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2013-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "provisions of the Regulation of Insurance Industry Act require insurers registered with the Insurance Board of Sri Lanka (IBSL) prior to 2011\u00a002\u00a011 to list themselves on a licensed Stock Exchange within a period of 5 years from the date of enforcement of the Amendment Act and such Insurance Companies are required to comply with this requirement on or before 2016\u00a002\u00a011.  Those insurers registered on or after 2011\u00a002\u00a011 are required to be listed on a licensed Stock Exchange within a period of 03 years.  The proposal made by H.E. the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance and Planning, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft amending legislation, to exempt the Insurance Companies registered under the Insurance Board of Sri Lanka prior to 2011\u00a002\u00a011 from the requirement of registering under a licensed Stock Exchange, subject to stipulations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
