    "description": "17th SAARC Summit held in Addu City, Maldives",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4295",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- the 17th SAARC Summit was held in Maldives from 10 - 11 November 2011 and was attended by Heads of States of  Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Maldives, Nepal, Pakistan and Sri Lanka.  H.E. the President in his address stated that the Region of  South Asia consists of a large, creative and talented pool of young human resource base reflecting an increasingly promising future for the Region of SAARC and that the Region should take necessary courses of action to realize the potential of such unprecedented human resource base.  He also stated that the other challenges the Region confronts are food and energy security, environmental degradation, upgrading of infrastructure and protection of our societies from terrorism.  During the Summit, the following four (04) crucial Agreements were signed:\r\n\r\n*\tAgreement of Multilateral Arrangement for Recognition of Conformity Assessment,\r\n\r\n*\tAgreement on Implementation of Regional Standards,\r\n\r\n*\tAgreement on Establishing SAARC Seed Bank,\r\n\r\n*\tAgreement on Rapid Response to Natural Disaster.\r\n\r\n\tH.E. the President also held discussions with other Heads of States and dignitaries.  At his meeting with the Prime Minister of  India, the President appreciated the contribution made by India for the reconstruction and development of the Northern Province and elaborated on the measures the government is taking on re-settlement, rehabilitation and re-integration, including that of former LTTE combatants."
  },
