    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4184",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- the proposal made by Hon. Basil Rajapaksa, Minister of Economic Development, to provide more opportunities to the private sector  to participate in Regional Development activities implemented by the Government, was approved by the Cabinet. Under this scheme, contractors nominated by the Chamber of Construction Industries and Contractors Association of Sri Lanka, complying with ICTAD regulations and standards and maintain good track records and short listed within the District/Province could submit quotations for identified work. This will also provide competitive bidding between the public and private sector construction companies."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "National Action Plan for the Protection and Promotion of Human Rights in Sri Lanka - 2011 - 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4183",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "-  this action plan has been prepared in consultation with and the cooperation of the relevant stakeholders of the Government as well as the civil society. This document not only provides a detailed policy and a legislative programme to realize  the fundamental rights and freedoms provided in the Constitution, but also looks to expand these rights and freedoms. This action plan mainly focuses on the following: \r\n\r\n\t\t*\tCivil and Political Rights;\r\n\t\t*\tEconomic Social and Cultural Rights;\r\n\t\t*\tPrevention of Torture;\r\n\t\t*\tRights of Women;\r\n\t\t*\tMigrant Workers;   \r\n\t\t*\tChildren; and,\r\n\t\t*\tInternally Displaced Persons.\r\n\r\n\tThe above Action Plan presented by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, Minister of Plantation Industries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Kapruka Navodawa - National Coconut Sector Development Plan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4182",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- with the peaceful environment prevailing in the country, the Ministry of Coconut Development and Janatha Estate Development has already commenced rehabilitation and new coconut plantations in all provinces with potential for coconut cultivation, including the Northern and Eastern Provinces. The proposal made by Hon. A.P. Jagath Pushpakumara, Minister of Coconut Development and Janatha Estate Development  to implement the National Coconut Sector Development Plan within the next 06 years in 180 selected Divisional Secretary Devisions in the country, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Establishment of Diplomatic Relations with the Republic of EL Salvador",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4181",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of the Republic of EL Salvador has expressed its wish to establish diplomatic relations with Sri Lanka in order to enhance the friendship and cooperation between the two countries. There has been an increase in trade between the two countries during the last five years, with the trade balance being in favour of Sri Lanka. EL Salvador is a smallest country in  Central America but has the 3rd largest economy in that region . The proposal made by Hon (Prof.) G.L. Peiris, Minister of External Affairs to establish diplomatic relations between the two countries, was approved by the Cabinet of Ministers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "33rd Annual Forum of the Parliamentarians for Global Action (PGA) Colombo, Sri Lanka 28 - 30 October 2011",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4180",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Parliamentarians for Global Action (PGA) is the World's only International Organization of democratically elected national legislators. Its network includes 1350 Parliamentarians from 105 countries drawn from both Government and Opposition Parties. Its concerns include a wide range of international issues such as, peacemaking and peacekeeping, sustainable development and population, human rights and the rule of law, strengthening democratic institutions and women's empowerment. The joint proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management and Leader of the House of Parliament; and  Hon. (Prof.) G.L. Peiris, Minister of External Affairs, to get the cooperation of all concerned to hold the 33rd Annual Session in Sri Lanka from 28th to 30th October 2011, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Supply of Locally Produced Whole Milk Powder for the Thriposha Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4179",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Thriposha is a nutritious food distributed free of charge to the malnourished children, pregnanat mothers and breast feeding mothers under a national programme. Whole Milk Powder is a main raw material use for Thriposha production. The proposal made by Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Minister of Health to purchase 187 MT. of Whole Milk Powder from 06.08.2011 up to 31.12.2011 at a cost of Rs.100.79 million was approved by the Cabinet.  Purchase of the quantity of Milk Powder required for this programme for 2012 is to be made through competitive bidding from domestic milk food manufacturers, following tender procedure."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Annual Report of the National Apprentice and Industrial Training Authority (NAITA) for the year 2008",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4178",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- training provided by NAITA could be broadly categorized as follows:\r\n\r\n*\tEnterprise Based Apprenticeship Training - under this programme, trainees are attached to an enterprise throughout the training period to earn skills by doing.  This programme provides skills specific to the enterprises to which apprentices are attached according to a training guide prepared by NAITA in consultation with the employer.  \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n*\tInstitutional / Centre Based Duel Apprenticeship Training - in this system, trainees are directly enrolled to the National Level Training Institutes for a specific period of institutional training followed by an on-the-job training component in public or private sector industrial organizations. \r\n\r\n*\tIn Plant Training - this offers training for undergraduates of the Engineering Degree Courses at Moratuwa, Peradeniya and Ruhuna Universities and Diploma Courses conducted by the Universities and other tertiary level educational institutions. \r\n\r\n*\tOn-the-job Training - NAITA conducts a programme of 06 months duration for students of other vocational training institutions.  \r\n\t\r\n\tIn 2008, NAITA has recruited 25875 apprentices for different modes of training.  The \tabove report submitted by Hon.Dallas Alahapperuma, Minister of Youth Affairs and \tSkills Development, was approved by the Cabinet for presentation in Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Annual Reports of the State Timber Corporation for the years 2008 and 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4177",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "-  the \tCorporation has increased its income from Rs.3141 million to Rs.3581 million, the\tgross profit from Rs.1210 million to Rs.1351 million and the net profit from Rs.647\tmillion to Rs.810 million, in 2009.  It contributed Rs.1635 million to the National\tIncome in 2009.  With the view to protect natural resources for the benefit of the future\tgeneration, the Corporation has instituted an island-wide tree planting programme to\tpromote developing the forest cover in the country. The above report submitted by\tHon. Anura  Priyadharshana Yapa,  Minister  of  Environment, was  approved by the\tCabinet for presentation in Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
