    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2011-08-17",
    "description": "Medium Term Expenditure Framework 2012-2014 and Preparation of Budget for the Year 2012",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4151",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-08-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- a broad framework of the above was presented to the Cabinet by H.E. the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance and Planning and Cabinet approval was granted for the General Treasury to proceed with the work pertaining to the above and the preparation of the Budget for the year 2012.  The Budget 2012 is to be mainly focused on the following parameters:\r\n\r\n\t\t*\tEconomic Growth \t\t- \tto be maintained at least at 8%  \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t*\tInflation \t\t\t-\tto be maintained within a range \t\t\t\t\t\t\tof 6% - 7% \r\n\t\t*\tPublic Investment\t\t-\ttarget to maintain at 6.5%  of \t\t\t\t\t\t\tGDP\r\n\t\t*\tBudget Deficit\t\t-\ttarget to be reduced to 6.2% \t\t\t\t\t\t\tfrom 6.8% of GDP\r\n\t\t*\tTotal Debt\t\t\t-\ttarget to be reduced to 75% \t\t\t\t\t\t\tfrom 80% of GDP"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-08-17-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2011-08-17",
    "description": "The Annual Report and Accounts of the Sri Lanka Savings Bank - 2010",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4150",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-08-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- the assets and liabilities of the defaulted Pramuka Savings and Development Bank were vested with the Sri Lanka Savings Bank in August 2007 by the Central Bank. The Sri Lanka Savings Bank commenced business in March 2008 as a State Owned Savings Bank. The profit after tax for the year 2010 has been 277.5 million which is an increase of Rs.90.2 million (48.2%) from the previous year. The gross income of the Bank in 2010 has been Rs.500.7 million, an increase of Rs.46 million (10.1%) from the previous year.  The proposal made by H.E. the President to submit the above Annual Report and Accounts of the Bank in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
