    "doc_id": "2011-08-17-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2011-08-17",
    "description": "New Homeopathy Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4145",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-08-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- the proposal made by Hon. Salinda Dissanayake, \tMinister of Indigenous Medicine to repeal the existing Homeopathy Act which \twas enacted in 1970 and to present a new Bill for the purpose prepared by the \tLegal Draftsman, was approved by the Cabinet.  The new Bill will provide the \tfollowing:\r\n\r\n*\tregulate and control the practice of Homeopathic medicine;\r\n\r\n*\tpromote and encourage the study, research in and practice of Homeopathic medicine;\r\n\r\n*\testablish and maintain a Homeopathic Medical College;\r\n\r\n*\tdevelop or encourage measures for the investigation and treatment of diseases with a view to improve public health; and\r\n\t\t\r\n*\tregulate and control institutions providing treatment and control of the manufacture, importation, sale and distribution of Homeopathic drugs."
  },
