    "date_str": "2011-08-03",
    "description": "Hambantota Port Development Project - Commencement of Business Ventures",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4134",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-08-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a decision taken by the Government to develop a Sea Port at Hambantota on a proposal made by H.E the President, the construction works of the project (Phase I) were commenced and completed as scheduled. Accordingly, a Business plan has been prepared by the Sri Lanka Ports Authority in order to identify the Business ventures that could be undertaken one of the project. Proposals were called from interested parties for the commencement of Business ventures at the Hambantota Port and those received have been evaluated by a Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee and a Project Committee. The proposal to award the contracts for operation of the following on the recommendations of these Committees, was approved by the Cabinet: \r\n\r\n\t\t*\tSugar Refinery Plant; \r\n\t\t*\tPetro Chemical Plants; and,\r\n\t\t*\tFertilizer Storage/Processing/Bagging Plant."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-08-03-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2011-08-03",
    "description": "Formulation of a Combined Programme for the promotion of Tourism in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4133",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-08-03",
    "decision_details_body": "? \tthe tourist industry in Sri Lanka which earned around US$ 500 million in foreign exchange in 2010 is gradually forging ahead in an accelerated manner and it is intended to attract tourists to the tune of about 2.5 million by 2016. A trend of heavy increase in the number of tourists visiting Sri Lanka in view of the present peaceful environment is noted and Sri Lanka is internationally accepted as an highly attractive tourist destination. The proposal made by Hon. Basil Rajapaksa, Minister of Economic Development, to promote Sri Lanka with a single identity in the international market with all relevant public and private agencies jointly launching a combined programme  capable of building a sustainable single image of Sri Lanka was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
