    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2011-07-27",
    "description": "Appointment of a Cabinet Sub-Committee on Power and Energy and Supply and Distribution of Petroleum Products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4114",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-07-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet of Ministers decided to appoint a Cabinet Sub-Committee on Power and Energy and Supply and Distribution of Petroleum Products to oversea importation and distribution of petroleum products for all purposes, including power generation, comprising of the following Ministers: \r\n\r\n*\tHon. A.H.M. Fowzie, Minister (Senior) for Urban Affairs;\r\n*\tHon. Susil Premajayantha, Minister of Petroleum Industries;\r\n*\tHon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, Minister of Power and Energy;\r\n*\tHon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, Minister of Public Administration and Home Affairs; and\r\n*\tHon. Dilan Perera, Minister of Foreign Employment Promotion and Welfare.\r\n\r\nSecretary, Ministry of Power and Energy will function as the Secretary to this Sub-Committee.  Secretary to the Ministry of Finance and Planning, Co-Chief Executive Officer of the Secretariat for Senior Ministers and the Secretary to the Ministry of Petroleum Industries should attend the Meetings of this Sub-Committee."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-07-27-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2011-07-27",
    "description": "Appointment of the Procurement Appeal Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4113",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-07-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted for the extension of the term of office of the presently functioning Procurement Appeal Board (PAB) comprising of the following for a period of three years with effect from 16.08.2011: \r\n\r\n*\tHon. Justice K. Vignarajah, former Justice of the  Court of Appeal - (Chairman);\r\n*\tMr. P.A. Pemathilaka, former Auditor General - (Member)\r\n*\tMr. T.P.G.N. Leelaratne, retired Secretary to a Ministry - (Member);\r\n\r\nIt is mandatory for all Government Institutions to inform the decisions of the Procurement Committee (PC) to all unsuccessful bidders within seven days from the decision of the Committee, so that any unsuccessful bidders can make their appeals to the PAB.   Ministries should await the decision of the PAB prior to awarding of any tenders for the successful bidders."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-07-27-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2011-07-27",
    "description": "Food Aid Assistance from the World Food Programme (WFP) to Sri Lanka for 2011",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4112",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-07-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- the World Food Programme has agreed to provide food aid assistance under Protracted Relief and Recovery Operation (PRRO) and Emergency Operation (EMOP) to Sri Lanka and Letters of Understanding are to be signed for the programmes between the Government and the WFP.  The objectives of the programmes are to support the Government in its efforts to provide relief to the affected people and for rehabilitation activities.   The two programmes consist of the following: \r\n\r\n\t\t*\tMother-Child Health Nutrition;\r\n*\tFood for Education for all Primary Students in selected Schools;\r\n\t\t*\tFood for Work Programmes; and\r\n\t\t*\tFood Distribution for the Displaced people in Camps.\r\n\r\n\tThe PRRO programme will be implemented in Mannar, Vavuniya, Mullaituvu, Kilinochchi and Jaffna Districts in the Northern Province and selected areas in the Eastern Province and the estimated number of beneficiaries would be 371,000.   The EMOP programme will be implemented in selected Divisional Secretariat Divisions in Ampara, Batticaloa and Trincomalee Districts in the Eastern Province and Anuradhapura and Polonnaruwa District in the NCP covering 500,000 beneficiaries.  The proposal made by H.E. the President to sign the  Letters of Understanding with the WFP in a sum of US $39,755,501 and US $8,869,131 to implement the WFP Food Aid Programmes in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
