    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "The Sustainable Agriculture Water Management Project (SAWMP) ? An Assessment of Progress of Phases 1 & 11",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3969",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- the above project combines a number of innovative technologies to increase small farm productivity, raise incomes and improve livelihoods of rural farm families throughout the Dry Zone of Sri Lanka.  Under Phases I and II of the project, 10,000 solar powered drip irrigation units have been provided to small farmers in the dry zone under a concessionary financing scheme, by the Ministry of Agriculture.  The Phase I of the project valued at US $16.1 million has been implemented under a loan from Australian Export Finance & Insurance Corporation and the City Group and has supplied 5000 of these units to farmers in 11 dry zone and intermediate zone districts.  Phase II of the project has supplied another 5000 units covering 17 dry and intermediate zone districts, including the North and the East.  The proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Yapa Abeywardena, Minister of Agriculture, to purchase 5000 Units of Solar Power Drip Irrigation Systems under Phase III of the project with the financial assistance from the State Banks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Land Alienation Policy to Promote Development Activities of the Government",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3968",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a joint proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management; Hon. Basil Rajapaksa, Minister of Economic Development; and  Hon. Janaka Bandara Tennakoon, Minister of Lands and Land Development, Cabinet approval was granted to streamline the procedure of land alienation / disposition so as to ensure that there is a consistent policy on the extent of land that would be made available by the Government and Government Agencies to specific sectors, in the national interest.  Under the proposed procedure - \r\n\r\n*\tland alienation for agricultural purposes will be strictly on lease basis for a period not exceeding 35 years;\r\n\r\n*\tland alienation for industrial purposes will also be strictly on lease basis for a period not exceeding 35 years;\r\n\r\n*\tland alienation for tourism will be on the basis of 99 year lease and the extent of land will be 30 acres or less; and\r\n\r\n*\tin case of land required for agricultural or industrial purpose on investments over US $20 million, a suitable long term tenure will be considered."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Implementation of a Pilot Project to Improve the Easy Accessibility and Sustainability of Financial Facilities to Rural Communities for obtaining the Electricity Service Connection",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3967",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- with the view to facilitate  the provision of electricity to low income household categories and Samurdhi beneficiaries, Cabinet approval has already been granted  for a Scheme to recover the electricity service connection charge up to a maximum limit of Rs.30,000 for such categories, by the Ceylon Electricity Board in 48 equal monthly installments.  On a proposal made by Hon.Patali Chapika Ranawaka, Minister of Power and Energy, Cabinet approval was granted to implement a micro credit based electricity connectivity programme with a grant of US$3.5 million from the Asian Development Bank to provided financial assistance to those who would not be eligible to obtain a loan under the CEB-Samurdhi Programme.  Under this programme, a pilot project has been designed to be implemented in three Districts, namely Hambantota (Southern Province), Ratnapura (Sabaragamuwa Province) and Ampara (Eastern Province)."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Development and Expansion of Fishnet Factory of Northsea Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3966",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- this is a 100% government owned fishnet factory situated in Jaffna which manufactured about 300 Mt. of fishnets per annum and was damaged during the conflict situation in the area during the last 3 decades.  Fishing  industry has been a major economic activity and  a source of livelihood in the Northern Region during the past, where about 18,500 fishermen are engaged in fishing in the region.  The sea food production in 2010 was 20,740 Mt. and is expected to be increased up to 25,000 Mt. per annum.  On a proposal made by Hon. Douglas Devananda, Minister of Traditional Industries and Small Enterprise Development, Cabinet approval was granted to develop and expand this fishnet factory at Gurunagar, Jaffna with financial assistance from the Government of India at a cost of Rs.152 million."
  },
  {
