    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Completion of Stage II of the Sinhapura Housing Project on premises of Estate No. 48 at Wanathamulla, Colombo 08",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3944",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- this Housing Project consists of 120 Housing Units and under Stage I of the project, 03 buildings consisting of 60 Housing Units were completed and they have been allocated to the Public in 2007.  On a proposal made by Hon.Wimal Weerawansa, Minister of Construction, Engineering Services, Housing and Common Amenities, Cabinet approval was granted to entrust the completion of Stage II of the project to the State Engineering Corporation at a cost of Rs.150.27 million, which amount has been allocated to the Ministry by the Budget 2011."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Conservation of Digavapi Chaitya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3943",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Digavapi Chaitya is situated in the Divisional Secretary's Division of Addalachchenai in the District of Ampara in the Eastern Province. On a proposal made by Hon.(Dr.) Jagath  Balasuriya, Minister of National Heritage, Cabinet approval was granted to commence restoration of the Digavapi Chaitya and other related renovation work in the area.  The estimated cost of the first stage of the project will be Rs.77 million.  Bank of Ceylon has already agreed to donate Rs.37.0 million for this project under its corporate social responsibility."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Establishment of two new Vocational Training Centres in Vauniya and Jaffna Districts of the Northern Province and Development of Existing Vocational Training Centres in Batticaloa, Nuwara Eliya and Trincomalee Districts under the grants assistance of the Government of India",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3942",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by Hon. Dullas Alahapperuma, Minister of Youth Affairs and Skills Development, Officials of the Government have held discussions with a delegation from the Government of India to establish new Vocational Training Centres in the Northern Province and to develop the existing centres in the Eastern and Central Provinces. Cabinet approval was granted to implement the project proposal totaling to Rs.2,669.18 million under the grant assistance of the Government of India and to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) for the purpose."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "An Act to provide financial assistance for Higher Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3941",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- at present students entering Universities from lower income families are provided financial assistance through University bursaries or through the Mahapola Scholarship Fund.  It has been observed that funds received by students through these Schemes are inadequate for their academic activities and also that they are encountered with difficulties in obtaining Bank Loans for the purpose. On a proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissasnayake, Minister of Higher Education, Cabinet approval was granted to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill for the purpose, whereby students from poor families entering Universities could obtain loans from Banks for their academic activities, to be repaid compulsorily through their prospective employers from their monthly salaries, once they get employed after passing out from Universities."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Maintaining a proper and updated database regarding housing by establishing the Janasevana National Housing Secretariat",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3940",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by Hon. Wimal Weerawansa, Minister of Construction, Engineering Services, Housing and Common Amenities, Cabinet approval was granted for the establishment of this Secretariat which will act as a Centre that connect the housing market in order to provide information for all those in need of houses, for Housing Property Developers, Contractors and Capital Providers. This institution will gather information on housing programmes implemented by various institutions and individuals in Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "A Credit of Special Drawing Rights 63,600,000 from the International \tDevelopment Association of the World Bank for the Road Sector \tAssistance Project ? Second Additional Financing",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3939",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "?  The Government has \tconcluded negotiations with the International Development Association (IDA) of the \tWorld Bank to obtain additional financing of Special Drawing Rights (SDR) \t63,600,000 (approximately US$ 100 million) for the Road Sector Assistance Project. \tThe main objective of the project is to reduce transportation cost and to improve the \tconnectivity to the Northern and Eastern Provinces by re-surfacing and rehabilitation \tof 134 Km. of the Road Sections from Ambepussa to Dambulla (91 Km.) and \tKantale to Trincomalee (43 Km.) of the A6 Road. The total cost of the project is US$ \t110 million, of which US$ 100 million will be provided by the IDA and the balance \tof US$ 10 million by the Government of Sri Lanka.  This credit facility is interest \tfree.  The proposal made by H.E. the President to enter into a Financing Agreement \twith the IDA  of the World Bank was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Order made under the Payment Devices Frauds Act No. 30 of 2006",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3938",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- This Act \twhich was passed by Parliament in 2006, has introduced provisions to counteract the \thigh incidence of payment card frauds and for investigation, prosecution and \tpunishment of offenders. Provisions under this Act provides powers for the Minister \tin charge of the subject to make regulations with the approval of Parliament, to \tappoint a Panel of Experts with qualifications in electronic engineering or software \tengineering to assist the police in investigations under this Act. The proposal made \tby H.E. the President to present such regulations in Parliament was approved by the \tCabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Greater Colombo Urban Transport Development Project Phase 2 (II) ? Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3937",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- In keeping with the official pledge, the Japanese government has agreed to provide a loan of Japanese Yen 31,688 million (approximately Rs.42,145 million) through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) for the construction of the Northern Section of the Outer Circular Highway (OCH). The proceeds of the loan will be utilized to construct 8.9 Km. length of Road Section from Kaduwela to Kadawatha of the OCH, to ease traffic congestion in the Colombo Metropolitan Region and improve the connectivity with the Southern Expressway from Colombo to Katunayake and other National Roads connected to the City of Colombo. The proposal made by H.E. the President to enter into a Loan Agreement with JICA for the purpose was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Vavuniya-Kilinochchi Transmission Line Project (II) Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3936",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the official pledge made by the Government of Japan, the Japanese Government has agreed to provide a loan of Japanese Yen 1422 million (approximately Rs.1891 million) through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), as additional financing for the construction  the transmission line from Vavuniya to Kilinochchi and the Grid Substation at Kilinochchi. The objective of the project is to reinforce the transmission network in the northern area of the country. Completion of this project will ensure reliable, adequate and efficient electricity supply to consumers in the Northern Province. The proposal made by H.E. the President to enter into a Loan Agreement with JICA was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "A Grant of Japanese Yen 360 million from the  Government of Japan for the Food Security Project for Low Income Farmers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3935",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Japan has agreed to provide a grant of Japanese Yen 360 million (approximately Rs.468 million) to purchase agricultural machinery and equipment for the use of low income farmers in the country to assist in the food production programmes.  820 units of Two Wheel Tractors  and 50 units of  Four Wheel Tractors will be provided under this grant. On a proposal made by the H.E. the President Cabinet approval was granted to enter into a Grant Agreement for same and to sign the Exchange of Notes with the Government of Japan."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Emergency Financial Assistance of US $ 38 million from the International Development Association of the World Bank for the Community Livelihoods in Conflict Affected Areas Project (Re-awakening Project)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3934",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to conduct negotiations with the International Development Association (IDA) of the World Bank and also to enter into an agreement with the IDA to obtain a loan of US$ 38 million as additional financial assistance for the ongoing community livelihood development in the conflict affected areas project to support emergency rehabilitation and restoration of irrigation schemes and rural roads affected due to the recent floods. This credit facility of the IDA is interest free and the project is scheduled to be completed in 2013."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Additional financial assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) for implementation of the Secondary Towns and Rural Community-based Water Supply and Sanitation Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3933",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "?  Asian Development Bank (ADB) has agreed to provide an additional loan of US$ 17.6 million (approximately Rs.1.98 billion) for implementation of the Muttur Water Supply Scheme under the on-going Secondary Town and Rural Community Based Water Supply Sanitation Project. The proposed additional financing will ensure successful completion of the head works of the project and above 50,000 people in the project area will be benefited. The Government of Sri Lanka will contribute a sum equivalent to US$ 2.0 million (approximately Rs.218 million) for this project. The proposal made by H.E. the President to enter into Loan Agreements with the ADB was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
