    "doc_id": "2011-03-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-03-30",
    "description": "Loan facility of US$ 500 million from China Development Bank Corporation to Finance Improvement and Rehabilitation of Priority Road Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3932",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- China Development Bank Corporation (CDB) has agreed to provide US$ 500 million to finance improvement and rehabilitation of priority Road Projects covering the entire island and connecting all electorates. This will contribute to lower transportation cost and improved the integration of all parts of the country, thus increasing the economic activities and productivity and also provide employment opportunities to the residents of the area. The proposal made by H.E. the President to enter into a Loan Agreement for US$ 500 million with the China Development Bank Corporation to implement the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Establishment of Colombo Metropolitan City Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3931",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- with a view to assist to local bodies within the Colombo City Region namely, Colombo Municipal Council, Dehiwala-Mt. Lavinia  Municipal Council, Kolonnawa Urban Council, Kotikawatta-Mulleriyawa Pradeshiya Sabha and Sri Jayewardenepura-Kotte  Municipal Council, a supervisory body by the name of  Colombo Metropolitan City Corporation is to be set up for the efficient management of the Colombo City Region.  While existing elected local bodies will continue to function, all Heads and Deputy Heads of the said five local authorities and a nominated member from the opposition of each local authority and officials of Ministries involved in the delivery of utilities and other services, Chief Secretary of the Western Provincial Council will constitute the composition of the City Corporation, which will be headed by the Governor of the Metropolitan Corporation.  Twelve Advisory Committees comprising of elected members of local bodies will be set up to advise the Corporation.  \r\n\t\r\nThe proposal made by Hon. A.L.M. Athaullah, Minister of Local Government and Provincial Councils, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare legislation for presentation to Parliament accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet of Ministers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Proposed New Law to Regulate Finance Business",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3930",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- in December 2010 Cabinet has approved a proposal to draft a Bill to amend the Finance Act No.78 of 1988 with a view to providing for a strong governance framework to regulate finance business.  The purpose of this effort is to update the law with the developments in technology in keeping with international best practices to combat unauthorized deposit taking businesses and to ensure the stability of the financial sector.  Some of the salient features of the Bill are - \r\n\r\n\t\t*\tacceptance of deposits without authority is made an offence;\r\n\t\t*\tdefinition of \"deposit\" is introduced; \r\n\t\t*\tenhanced examination/investigative powers;\r\n\t\t*\tenhancement of supervisory action on licensed finance companies;\r\n\t\t*\tenhanced public disclosure;\r\n\t\t*\tenhanced penalties.\r\n\r\n\tThe proposal made by H.E. the President to present the  relevant Bill in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Hosting of the Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting (CHOGM) in Sri Lanka in 2013",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3929",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- at the Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting held in Trinidad & Tobago in November 2009, it has been unanimously agreed that the next Meeting for the year 2013 will be held in Sri Lanka. Thereafter, Sri Lanka will serve as the Chair of the Commonwealth for two years from 2013.  This will be the largest international event to be hosted by Sri Lanka since 1976.   54 Heads of State or Government of the Commonwealth or their representatives will participate at this Meeting.  On a proposal made by Hon. (Prof.) G.L. Peiris, Minister of External Affairs, Cabinet approval was granted to establish the relevant Committees for the purpose."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Expansion of Sangaramaya Bhikku Hostel of the University of Peradeniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3928",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Government has observed that the annual intake of student monks to the University has increased significantly over the past two decades and as such, the required hostel facilities have to be expanded.  On a proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, Minister of Higher Education, Cabinet approval was granted to expand the existing Sangaramaya Bhikku Hostel of the University of Peradeniya through construction of a two storied building at a total cost of Rs.34.2 million.  The Project will be commenced with funds provided to the University Grants Commission for 2011."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Construction of a Building for Installation of Telecobolt Unit Bhabhatron II & Simulator at District General Hospital - Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3927",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Government of India has expressed its willingness to donate the above unit to be installed at the District General Hospital, Hambantota, to facilitate Cancer Treatment for patients in remote areas in and around Hambantota.  This was on a proposal made by Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Minister of Health.  Cabinet approval was granted to award the contract to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB) at a cost of Rs.127.44 million, on approval of estimates by the Department of National Planning."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Coconut Research Institute of Sri Lanka and the International Centre for Agro Forestry Research (ICRAF), Kenya for the Development of Coconut Based Agro Forestry Systems",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3926",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by Hon. Jagath Pushpakumara, Minister of Coconut Development and Janatha Estate Development, Cabinet approval was granted to enter in to the above Memorandum of Understanding (MOU).   Facilities available under this MOU will be exchange of Scientific Staff and Technicians, Training Scientists and Coconut Small Holders, establishment of field demonstrations, exchange of scientific information on research and development, exchange of planting material of agro-forestry species, promotion of contacts between relevant public and private enterprises and universities and preparation of joint projects for funding for the coconut sector of Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Continuation of provisions for maintaining of a Residential Care Home for the children profoundly disabled by Autism and Autism related Disorders",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3925",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- a Trust named as the 'Udapadi Trust' has been established in 2003 by a group of parents of the above category of children to meet the needs of these children to a certain extent.  The objective of this Trust is to maintain residential homes for mentally retarded children, provision of funds for residential, social welfare and for recreation facilities etc. of these children.  On a proposal made by Hon. Felix Perera, Minister of Social Services, Cabinet approval was granted to provide Rs.1.5 million to this Fund in 2011 in quarterly installments.  Action will be taken by the Ministry to provide funds for the purpose from the year 2012 onwards through United Nations and other International  Organizations assisting Child Development Charity Institution.  A Ministerial Committee comprising of the Ministers of Health; Education; Social Services; and Child Development and Women's Affairs was appointed to study the problems and make recommendations to the Cabinet on mobilizing resources to assist this category of  children."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Asian Regional Ministerial Meeting on Aquaculture for Food Security, Nutrition and Economic Development - 28th to 29th July 2011, Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3924",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, this meeting is to be held in July in Colombo with the participation of the representatives from 115 countries.  The meeting will be jointly organized by the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO), the Network of Aquaculture Centres in the Asian and Pacific Region and the Ministry of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development.  This will facilitate to develop bilateral relationship with Asian countries which can be beneficial in respect of technology transfer and attracting investments to Sri Lanka in the field of Aquaculture.  Cabinet approval was granted to hold this conference in Colombo in July 2011."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-23-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-03-23",
    "description": "Extension of the Project on Delimitation of the Outer Edge of the Continental Margin of Sri Lanka under the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea (DEOCOM Project)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3923",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Sri Lanka is a party to the above convention.  The objective of the above project is to conduct a Geophysical Survey in the seabed area adjacent to Sri Lanka's 200 nautical miles, Exclusive Economic Zone and process, interpret the data gathered from the survey and to prepare Sri Lanka's claim under the United Nations Convention of the Law of the Sea for submission to the UN Commission on the Limits of the Continental Shelf.  On a proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, Cabinet approval was granted to extend the above project up to the end of 2012 or until such time the project is completed."
  },
