    "description": "Equipment requirement for the Clinical Building - Wards Complex, Faculty of Medicine & Allied Science - Saliyapura Rajarata University of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3887",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- this Faculty was inaugurated in 2006 and the first batch of students of this new Medical Faculty will commence the final year in March this year.  This Medical Faculty has to conform to the strict criteria laid down by the Sri Lanka Medical Council (SLMC).  In keeping with this requirement, a ward complex consisting of wards, operating theatres, intensive care units, labour rooms and many other specialist areas are being constructed near the Teaching Hospital, Anuradhapura.  On a joint proposal made by the Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Minister of Health; and Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, Minister of Higher Education, Cabinet approval was granted for the procurement of the necessary equipment for the above units of the Faculty of Medicine of the Rajarata University of Sri Lanka at a cost of Rs.250 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Signing of Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the United Nations and the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka Concerning Contributions to the United Nations Stand-By Arrangement System (UNSAS) for Enhancing Participation in UN Peacekeeping Operations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3886",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has been an active troop and police contributing country to the UN Peacekeeping Operations.  At the end of December 2010, Sri Lanka had a total of 1215 Service Personnel deployed in seven Peacekeeping Missions.  With the conflict situation in the country being over, the Armed Services and the Police are now in a position to enhance their contribution to the UN Peacekeeping Forces and accordingly, on a proposal made by Hon. (Prof.) G.L. Peiris, Minister of External Affairs, Cabinet approval was granted to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the United Nations for same, which will provide the following: \r\n\r\n * raise the image of the country as a dependable partner in promoting international peace and security.\r\n * provide international exposure and training for our Armed Forces and the Police personnel by working with foreign troops.\r\n\t\t* bring monetary benefits to the personnel involved. \r\n * gain priority over other Member States in being selected for deployments."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Imposition of a Tax on transfer of land to non-citizens",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3885",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the present legal provision in the country is to charge a tax equivalent to the value of the related property, when a property is transferred to a non-citizen.  But it has been observed that, as a means to circumvent the payment of the transfer tax, non-citizens enter into lease agreement with land owners, causing,  loss of revenue and also resulting in foreigners getting long term possession of valuable land at a minimal value.  To overcome this situation, on a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to prepare legislation to amend the law to make leases to non-citizens to be liable for the payment of this tax."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Impact of recent floods and providing relief to those affected",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3884",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "-  thousands of families in the Districts of Batticaloa, Ampara, Trincomalee, Polonnaruwa, Anuradhapura, Vavuniya, Mannar, Mullaitivu and Kilinochchi have been affected due to the recent floods and those in the Districts Badulla, Nuwara-Eliya, Kandy and Matale have been affected due to heavy rains and landslides.  Immediate relief measures have already been taken by the Government to provide cooked meals, dry rations and \tshelter for those affected.  Provisional Estimates are as follows:\r\n\r\n\t* affected population - 1.2 million\r\n\t* houses damaged/destroyed - 20000 \r\n\t* minor tanks/anicuts damaged - \t500\r\n\t* cultivation areas lost - 100,000 ha.\r\n\t* paddy cultivation lost - 800,000 mt.\r\n\t* displaced families due to landslides -7000\r\n\t\r\n\tA Task Force for the purpose under the Chairmanship of H.E. the President and consisting of relevant Cabinet Ministers and Chief Ministers has been appointed to direct and monitor the implementation of a well coordinated and effective programme for restoration activities of the affected areas, through the District Secretariats and Chief Secretaries of Provinces.  Accordingly, Cabinet approval was granted - \r\n\r\n(i) to set apart Rs. 33 billion for the proposed rehabilitation programme; \r\n\t\t(ii) to suspend all supplementary budget programmes in 2011\r\n(iii) for Line Ministries and Agencies to use their existing programmes to a maximum possible extend to generate some earnings to facilitate the General Treasury to contribute to the rehabilitation programme;\r\n(iv) to concentrate on an accelerated food production drive including one million home gardens to improve food supply; and,\r\n(v) to extend the fertilizer subsidy scheme to vegetable and all other crops and make subsidized fertilizer available in the open market. \r\n\r\n\tCabinet approval was also granted to authorize the District Secretaries / Government Agents in the Districts affected by disasters to engage persons who have lost their livelihood on account of the above, for work pertaining to renovation and rehabilitation of Rural Roads, Minor Irrigation Works, Tank Bunds, Cannals etc. for a maximum period of two months, in the following manner:\r\n\r\n* to provide work for 04 days per week in work sites on payment of Rs.500/- per day.\r\n* reconstruction work to be carried out by the District Secretaries / Government Agents by deployment of Grama Niladharies and other Field and Technical Officers, as found necessary.\r\n\r\n* the Divisional Secretaries of the areas to identify the immediate needs of the disaster areas and make necessary arrangements to organize activities at the work sites.\r\n* since the renovation works and provision of relief to those affected have to be attended to expeditiously and effectively in the disaster stricken Districts, the District Secretaries / Government Agents to obtain the services of any Pubic Officer engaged in field activities, as found necessary.\r\n\r\n\tDry rations will be provided to the affected people as follows:\r\n\r\n\t\t* Rs.500/- per week for a family of two or less. \r\n\t\t* Rs.750/- per week for a family of three or four.\r\n\t\t* Rs.1,000/- per week for a family of five or more.\r\n\r\n\tCabinet also authorized Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, Minister of Disaster Management to issue a Circular embodying the enhanced rates as indicated above and for engaging of persons who have lost their livelihood on rehabilitation work. \r\n\r\nIn addition to the above, the Government has also arranged food supply through the World Food Programme to be used to improve the food supply situation and rural work programmes in the affected areas."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Greater Colombo Waste Water Management Project funded by the Asian Development Bank: Award of Contract for Design, Supervision and Management Consultancy (DSC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3883",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Development Bank has agreed to provide financial facilities for the Greater Colombo Waste Water Management Project to be implemented at a total cost of US $116.63 million, with Rs.369.0 million to be provided by the Government of Sri Lanka to rehabilitate the sewerage system and thereby improving health facilities of the residents of Greater Colombo area.  On a proposal made by Hon. A.L.M. Athaullah, Minister of Local Government and Provincial Councils, on the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Consultant Procurement Committee (CACPC)  to award the contract for the design, supervision and management consultancy of this project at a total cost of US $5.60 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Ear, Nose and Throat Complex (ENT) for Teaching Hospital, Kandy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3882",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the ENT section of the Teaching Hospital, Kandy caters to more than 100 patients a day and nearly 2500 ENT surgical operations annually.  This section also provides teaching facilities to the under-graduates and training facilities to the post-graduates of the Medical Faculty of the Peradeniya University. On a proposal made by Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Minister of Health, Cabinet approval was granted to construct a seven storied building for this ENT Unit at the Teaching Hospital, Kandy and also to provide necessary equipment to the new building.  The total cost of the project is estimated to be Rs.1033 million.  The project will be implemented with funds to be provided in stages under the Medium Term Expenditure Framework."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Rehabilitation of National Highways with Concrete Surfacing through Domestic Contractors",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3881",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- since it has been observed that concrete roads are more durable and require less maintenance than the roads constructed with bitumen, it has been decided that rehabilitation / construction of roads and highways in future should be with concrete surfacing where it is viable.  Accordingly, the Road Development Authority has selected 600 Km of highways for rehabilitation through domestic contractors, as a pilot project.  On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to call for technical and financial proposals from eligible domestic contractors for rehabilitation of roads by using concrete surfacing and for appointment of a Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee (CANC) and Project Committee (PC) to evaluate the proposals submitted."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Financing and Rehabilitation of the Road Section from Dambulla to Habarana on Ambepussa - Kurunegala - Trincomalee (A6) Road by International Construction Consortium (Pvt) Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3880",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Habarana - Kantale (44 Km) road section of the Ambepussa - Kurunegala - Trincomalee (A6) Road has been recently rehabilitated under Asian Development Bank Funding.  The road section from Ambepussa to Dambulla (91 Km) on (A6) road has been earmarked for rehabilitation and improvement under World Bank Funding.  On a proposal made by H.E. the President, on the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Review Committee, Cabinet approval was granted to award the contract for rehabilitation of the remaining section of the road from Dambulla to Habarana (21.5 km), to the above Construction Consortium.  The rehabilitation of this section of the road will facilitate easy access to tourist destinations in the East Coast."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Southern Transport Development Project (STDP) - completion of the Balance Works of Galle Port Access Road in time",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3879",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Southern Expressway is being constructed from Kottawa to Godagama (Matara) and is being implemented through four separate contracts, viz - \r\n\r\n\t\t*\tKottawa - Dodangoda \t\t\t- \t34.3 Km\r\n\t\t*\tDodangoda - Kurundugahahetekma\t-\t31.7 Km\r\n\t\t*\tKurundugahahetekma - Pinnaduwa\t-\t30.0 Km\r\n\t\t*\tPinnaduwa - Godagama\t\t\t-\t30.0 Km\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\tSince it is expected to commence operation of the Expressway from Kottawa to Pinnaduwa in July 2011, and as the Galle Port Access Road too has to be completed, Cabinet approval was granted to engage the services of domestic contractors who have the capacity and capability to complete construction of this Access Road on time."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Landscape Development Project of Mahamewna Uyana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3878",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Jagath Balasuriya, Minister of National Heritage, Cabinet approval was granted in principle for the project to improve and uplift the Mahamewna Uyana area.  This will include the renovation and restoration work on the road network within the city of Anuradhapura to facilitate local pilgrims and tourists to patronize the place to pay homage and view the place."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Extension of the National Co-ordinating Unit that is functioning under the Ministry of Resettlement for implementation of the UNHCR Project with  regard to resettlement process, shelter and livelihood activities of the Internally Displaced Persons, consequent to the Humanitarian Activities by the Government",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3877",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- this Unit is functioning under the Ministry of Resettlement with financial assistance provided by the United Nations High Commission for Refugees for implementing the resettlement programme and for coordinating activities for the provision of shelter and livelihood facilities for the Internally Displaced Persons who are being resettled. About 90% of the displaced persons have been resettled and facilities have to be provided for the rest who are still in Relief Villages mainly due to de-mining activities taking place in their native places.  On a proposal made by Hon. Gunaratne Weerakoon, Minister of Resettlement, Cabinet approval was granted for the continuous functioning of the National Coordinating Unit for a further period of one year from 01.01.2011."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Amendment of the Act of the National Institute of Business Management",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3876",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by Hon. Dullas Alahapperuma, Minister of Youth Affairs and Skills Development to change the composition of the Governing Council of the institute, for the smoothing functioning of the administrative activities of the institute, Cabinet approval was granted for same and for the draft Bill prepared for the purpose to be presented in Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Amendment to the fine imposed under the Pesticide Control Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3875",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Provisions under this Act enable the control of Import, Packing, Labeling, Storing, Mixing, Transporting, Selling and Utilizing pesticides to ensure its proper management.   Since the existing fines for violation of provisions in the above Act have been imposed nearly three decades back and also due to the increase of environmental and health hazards caused due to handling of pesticides in an irresponsible manner, on a proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Yapa Abeywardhana, Minister of Agriculture, Cabinet approval was granted to increase the fine on an individual, from Rs.50,000/- to Rs.100,000/- and on a Body Corporate such as registered companies or corporations, from Rs.100,000/- to Rs.500,000/- and to present the relevant Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman in Parliament for approval. \r\n\r\n\tIt was also decided that an aggressive awareness campaign should be launched to educate farmers about the proper use of Agro chemicals and the disposal of empty containers in a non-hazardous manner."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Intake of  more foreign Students to Sri Lankan Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3874",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the present policy is to   reserve 0.5% of the proposed intake in each course of study for the benefit of foreign students. The proposal by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, Minister of Higher Education, to increase the intake of foreign students to the Sri Lankan Universities initially from 0.5% to 5% and later to 10% based on the success of the initial stage,without reducing the opportunities for local students, was approved by the Cabinet. This would not only gain additional foreign exchange to the country, but will also give wide publicity throughout the world for the quality of education in Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Indo-Sri Lanka Free Trade Agreement (ISFTA) and Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3873",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the representatives of the two Governments which met in November 2010 in Colombo noted the significant progress made under the ISFTA and reaffirmed the understanding that it would be timely to build on this achievement through a more comprehensive framework of economic cooperation.  Accordingly, on a proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, Minister of Industry and Commerce, Cabinet approval was granted to appoint an Inter-Agency Committee to prepare a new draft framework for the purpose between India and Sri Lanka.  Views of the professionals and other stakeholders will also be entertained by this Committee."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Methodology of Implementation and Supervision of Procurement and Payment for Liquid Milk to Dairy Farmers According to the Approved Purchase Price of Milk",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3872",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by Hon. Arumugan Thondaman, Minister of Livestock and Rural Community Development, Cabinet approval has already been granted to pay Rs.50/- per litre of liquid milk purchased from farmers.  This is an increase of Rs.16.80 per litre of milk in comparison with the price which prevailed in June 2010.  Awareness programmes will be conducted to educate the dairy farmers on the new rates of purchase of milk and the payment scheme will be monitored by a team of Officials in the respective areas to ensure the receipt of the correct payment by farmers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Funds for the payment of Farmers Pension of the Agriculture and Agrarian Insurance Board and the Insurance Payment for Crop Damages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3871",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Agriculture and Agrarian Insurance Board deals with the Farmers' Pension Scheme, Fishermen's Pension Scheme and the Social Security Benefit Scheme.  With the view to restructure this institute, this has been assigned to the Ministry of Finance and Planning from 2010.  On a proposal made by H.E. the President, it is intended to establish a stable Citizens' Pension Insurance Fund to provide more benefits to those employed in the fields of agriculture, fisheries, transport, construction industry and also in the self-employment sectors and steps have been taken to amalgamate the National Insurance Trust Fund and the Agriculture and Agrarian Insurance Board as an initial step.  The legislation for the purpose will be finalized by the end of March 2011.  Until such time the new institution is established, Cabinet approval was granted to provide Rs.347.5 million for the payment of Farmers' Pension for the three (03) months from January to March 2011."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "National Backbone Network to be implemented by the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka (TRCSL)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3870",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The intention of this project is to create a network which would ensure access to reliable high speed broadband connectivity to urban as well as rural under-served areas which would enhanced the Information and Communication Technology in the country, which is targeted to be increased to 75% by 2016. The proposal made by H.E. the President for the TRCSL to negotiate with Sri Lanka Telecom PLC to provide broadband connectivity facility on equitable terms and at affordable prices, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-02-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2011-02-02",
    "description": "Acceleration of National Food Production Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3869",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet having observed the recent price escalation of commodities in the open market affecting the cost of living of the general public, decided, on a proposal made by the Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, to enhance local production of food items with the active participation of regional public officers and institutions and the public, with the political leadership taking the lead role.  It was decided to appoint a Special Committee for the purpose consisting of representatives of the following institutions which should meet weekly for action to be taken expeditiously: \r\n* Ministry of Economic Development; \t\r\n* Ministry of Agriculture;\t\r\n* Ministry of Agrarian Services and Wildlife;\t\r\n* Ministry of Health;\t\r\n* Ministry of Public Administration and Home Affairs;\t\r\n* Ministry of Local Government and Provincial Councils;\t\r\n* Ministry of Mass Media and Information;\t\r\n* Ministry of Education; and,\t\r\n* Provincial Ministries of Agriculture.\t\r\nThe Special Committe will emphasis on the following:\t\r\n* to accelerate the cultivation activities of the one million homestead \t\t\tgardens under the \"Api Wawamu - Rata Nagamu Programme\"; \t\r\n* to provide planting material to school children to develop their home gardens;\t\r\n* to convert office premises and premises of official quarters to homestead gardens as far as possible;\r\n* to strengthen the national programme by providing seeds and planting materials to the needy, free of charge; and\t\r\n* to utilize cultivated lands destroyed by the recent floods for cultivation of short-term crops such as green gram, cowpea, maize, vegetable etc."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-02-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-02-02",
    "description": "Agreement with the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3868",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of UNESCO is to provide cooperation among nations for peace and security through the development of education, science and culture. Since sports play and important role in the protection of health and physical education, the need to encourage and coordinate international cooperation towards the elimination of doping the in sports has been greatly felt. On a proposal made by the Minister of Sports Hon. Mahindananda Aluthgamage, Cabinet approval was granted to sign an Anti-doping agreement with UNESCO for the elimination of doping in sports and to amend the Sports Law No.25 of 1973 and other relevant legislation as found necessary."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-02-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-02-02",
    "description": "Kilinochchi - Chunnakam Transmission Line, Lot A - Construction of Chunnakam 132/33kV Grid Substation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3867",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-02",
    "decision_details_body": "-  with the liberation of the LTTE controlled areas in the Northern Province, the Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB) envisages commencing developments / construction activities in these areas.  Accordingly, steps have been taken to commence construction work of the Kilinochchi - Chunnakam Transmission Line.                   On a proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy, Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, on the recommendation of the Cabinet appointed Procurement Committee, Cabinet approval was granted to award the contract to the lowest evaluated bidder, M/s. Siemens Limited of India, for a total bid price of US $3.74 million plus Sri Lankan Rupees 154.52 million."
  },
  {
