    "doc_id": "2011-02-02-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-02-02",
    "description": "Construction of a Hostel for 400 Male Students of the University of Visual Performing Arts at Dehiwala",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3864",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- this University which was setup in 2006, has a current student population of 2960, of which only 320 students have been provided with hostel accommodation.  On a proposal made by the Minister of Higher Education, Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, on the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, Cabinet approval was granted to award the contract for the construction of a hostel for 400 male students at this University at a cost of Rs.97.95 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-02-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-02-02",
    "description": "Import of Raw Cashew on temporarily basis to protect Local Cashew Processing Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3863",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has already been granted for the importation of 5000 MT of raw cashew up to 30.11.2010. Since the shortage of cashew in the market has badly effected the confectionery industries and also the tourist industry and also since the cashew harvest commences in April 2011, on a proposal made by the Minister of Minor Export Crop Promotion, Hon. Reginald Cooray, Cabinet approval was granted for the importation of 500 MT of raw cashew from South and Western African countries, India and Indonesia up to 20th March 2011."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-02-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-02-02",
    "description": "Provision of Technical Advisory Services and Physical Resources of State Farms for Projects being implemented with State and Private Sector participation for the production of (Agricultural) Seeds",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3862",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Large quantities of seeds such as potatoes, maize, onions, beans are imported annually to Sri Lanka for cultivation purposes costing over Rs. 1000 million as foreign exchange. It has been noticed that local farmers prefer to have local seed varieties due to their higher productivity and resistance to pests and diseases  and as such, on a proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture Hon. Mahinda Yapa Abeywardana, Cabinet approval was granted in principle for the production of seed varieties in Sri Lanka with the participation of both State and the Private Sector, on a programme to be developed for the purpose, and to provide facilities for same at the 19 State owned farms at Mahailluppallama, Aluththarama, Bata-Atha, Middeniya, Seeta Eliya, Kandapola, Meepilimana etc.  It was also decided to put idle lands at State Farms to productive use with the assistance of the Armed Forces so that they could be developed and cultivated."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-02-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-02-02",
    "description": "Investigation Unit for the Ministry of Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3861",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- it was agreed to expand and strengthen the present investigation unit of the Ministry in association with the categories of officers serving under the Minsitry, so as to identify the shortcomings in  National Schools and Colleges of Education and propose remedial measures to the authorities concerned for improving the quality of education."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-25-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-01-25",
    "description": "Supply of 50 Units of Terminal Tractors to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3860",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by H.E. the President, negotiations have been completed with the Exim Bank of Malaysia to obtain a Loan of US$ 4 million on concessionary terms, which is 86% of the cost for the purchase of 50 Units of Terminal Tractors to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority. The balance 14% is to be financed by the Sri Lanka Ports Authority. This project is expected to enhance the revenue generated by the SLPA and would improve the productivity in handling the increased number of containers in Colombo Port. Cabinet approval was granted to enter into a loan agreement with the Exim Bank of Malaysia for the purpose and to on-lend the proceeds of the loan to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority for the purchase of these terminal tractors."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-25-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-01-25",
    "description": "Development Project for the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka - Phase I - B",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3859",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Kuwait Fund for Arab Economic Development has agreed to provide a loan of  Kuwait Dinars 3 million (approximately US $10.5 million to finance the implementation of the above project. The objective of this project is to develop essential academic infrastructure and introduce new demand driven degree programmes to meet  the national needs of the country. The project consists of 2 phases, namely, phase I - A  and Phase 1 - B costing US$ 7.0 million and 12.0 million respectively. Phase 1 - A is now being implemented and of the total cost of phase 1 - B, US $10.5 million will be financed by the Kuwait fund and the balance of US $1.5 million will be borne by the Government of Sri Lanka. The proceeds of the loan will be utilized to complete construction of buildings for the Faculties, Student hostels and for the  development of infrastructure facilities such as roads, water supply, electricity, sewerage and waste management system and supply of furniture and educational equipment."
  },
  {
