    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Northern Province  consists of 5 Districts namely, Jaffna, Mannar, Vavuniya, Kilinochchi and Mullaitivu.  The majority of the population is Sri Lankan Tamils and this population was heavily affected by terrorist activities which prevailed for a period of nearly 30 years and as a result most of the health institutions in the Districts were damaged.  Since the commencement of the re-settlement process in the Northern Province, many development activities in healthcare institutions have been carried out with donor assistance.  On  a proposal made by the Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, for the improvement of facilities and renovation work in hospitals in these Districts, Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) has pledged its assistance in a sum of Rs.150 million, for the following: \r\n\t* Construction of Regional Training Centre, Jaffna    - cost  Rs.50.0 million. \r\n\t* Provision of Medical Equipment to the Intensive Care Unit at District General Hospital,Kilinochchi - cost Rs.25.0 million. \r\n\t* Construction of Nursing Quarters at District General Hospital, Kilinochchi - cost Rs.45.0 million. \r\n\t* Construction of Blood Bank at District General Hospital, Vavuniya - cost Rs.30.0 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-25-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-01-25",
    "description": "Extension to the Rural Electrification Project to expand the Electrification coverage of the North Central Province (NCP) to 100%",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3857",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- this project will provide 550 new Rural Electrification Schemes in the NCP. A total number of 110,000 domestic connections and 10,000 connections for small businesses/industries will be provided under this project. Cabinet approval was granted to enter into a Credit Facility Agreement with Nordea Bank AB of Sweden for US$ 53.49 million being 85% of the cost of the project.  Proceeds of this loan will be utilized by the Ceylon Electricity Board for the above Electricity Project.  The balance 15% will be borne by the GOSL. On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to enter into an Export Credit Facility Agreement amounting to US$54,163,022, including the increased insurance premium with Nordea Bank AB of Sweden."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-25-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-01-25",
    "description": "Proposal to raise the minimum age of females migrating for foreign employment as Domestic Workers from 18 Years to 21 Years",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3856",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Majority of labour receiving countries do not have a minimum age limit for females to be taken in for employment to their countries, specially for the domestic sector, and at present, females above 18 years are permitted by the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign  Employment, to take up overseas employment. Since there appears to be a tendency for abuses and vulnerability to different forms of exploitation, on a proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Employment Promotion and Welfare, Hon. Dilan Perera, Cabinet approval was granted to increase the minimum age of females and males migrating for employment as domestic workers, to 21 years."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-25-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-01-25",
    "description": "Relocation of the Ministry of Defence, Office of Chief of Defence Staff and Headquarters of the Armed Forces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3855",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to relocate the Ministry of Defence, Office of the Chief of  Defence Staff and Army Headquarters at Battaramulla.  The project will be funded through the revenue generated from the sale of land at the present location of these buildings near Galle Face Green, for two major hotel projects, Cabinet approval for which has already been granted."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-20-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-01-20",
    "description": "Relief to Disaster Victims due to Floods caused by Climate Change",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3854",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to available statistics nearly 280,000 families consisting of 1,061,000 have been affected due to the recent floods in the Northern, Eastern and North Central Provinces as well as the Central and Uva Provinces in the Island.  Immediate relief measures were taken by the Government on the direction of H.E. the President to provide cooked food, dry rations and other urgently required items and shelter for the victims.  On a proposal made by the Minister of Disaster Management, Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, Cabinet approval was granted to provide relief assistance to all flood victims in January 2011, relaxing existing Circular instructions, where essential, and irrespective of their income level and of their stay in welfare centres or with relatives and friends and for the appointment of an Officials' Committee consisting of representatives of the relevant ten (10) Ministries to examine the matter of providing further relief to the victims and the reconstruction activities to be carried out in these areas and submit recommendations to the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-20-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-01-20",
    "description": "Project for Improvement of Cartoon Production Facilities at the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation (SLRC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3853",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-20",
    "decision_details_body": "-  On the initiative of H.E. the President, the Government of Japan has agreed to provide a grant of Japanese Yen 41,700,000 (approximately Rs.54 million) for the above project through the Japan International Corporation Agency (JICA).  Under this project, a new 3D Animation Studio is to be established which will enable SLRC to produce 2D and 3D cartoon programmes and new TV programmes, thereby raising the quality of cartoon production in Sri Lanka to international standards. The project will be implemented by the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation, under the supervision of the Ministry of Mass Media and Information.  Cabinet approval was granted to sign the Exchange of  Notes with the Government of Japan and enter into a Grant Agreement with JICA."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-20-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-01-20",
    "description": "Procurement of a Survey and Research Vessel for Hydrography, Oceanography and Marine Biology Research Work of the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency (NARA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3852",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- NARA has to undertake research work pertaining to the above, of the entire water column and the sea bed which falls within the jurisdiction of Sri Lanka.  Government has observed that deployment of a Research Vessel for NARA would enhance its research and survey/seabed mapping capabilities covering near shore and off shore areas.  Accordingly, on a proposal made the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Research Development, Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne and on the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, Cabinet approval was granted for the purchase of the relevant vessel from Taiwan at a cost of Rs.313.84 million, to be delivered within a period of 09 months."
  },
  {
